#: src/index.md:1
msgid "rut"
msgstr "rut"


#: src/index.md:3
msgid ""
"**rut** is a small, statically typed, embeddable scripting language with Rust-flavored syntax, implemented in Rust. It is designed to be the scripting layer of host applications — typically UI apps — replacing JavaScript engines with a language whose type system is _not erased_: types exist at runtime, drive bytecode specialization, and make the host boundary fully checked."
msgstr ""
"**rut** 是一门小型、静态类型、可嵌入的脚本语言，语法带有 Rust 风味，用 Rust 实现。它被设计为宿主应用的脚本层——通常是 UI 应用——用一个类型系统_不被擦除_的语言取代 JavaScript 引擎：类型在运行时存在，驱动字节码特化，并让宿主边界受到完整检查。"


#: src/index.md:10
msgid ""
"Syntax feels like TypeScript (simple `enum`, the `class` shape, anonymous functions), with a Rust-flavored trait surface (`trait` + nominal satisfaction through `impl I for T` blocks) and Kotlin-style structured concurrency (`async`/`await` over poll-based futures). The runtime is a bytecode VM with **no JIT** — deterministic, fuel-metered, and small enough to embed everywhere a wasm binary fits."
msgstr ""
"语法感觉像 TypeScript（简单的 `enum`、`class` 的形状、匿名函数），带一套 Rust 风味的 trait 表面（`trait` + 经由 `impl I for T` 块的名义满足），以及 Kotlin 风格的结构化并发（基于轮询 future 的 `async`/`await`）。运行时是一台字节码 VM，**没有 JIT**——确定性、按燃料计量，而且小到能嵌进任何放得下一个 wasm 二进制的地方。"


#: src/index.md:17
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"fn sieve(limit: i32) -> Vec<i32> {\n"
"    let mut marks = Vec<u8>.filled(0, limit + 1);\n"
"    let primes: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();\n"
"    for (let i = 2; i <= limit; i += 1) {\n"
"        if (marks[i] == 0) {\n"
"            primes.push(i);\n"
"            let mut m = i * i;\n"
"            while (m <= limit) {\n"
"                marks[m] = 1;\n"
"                m += i;\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    return primes;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sieve\");\n"
"    let primes = sieve(100);\n"
"    log.info(f\"{primes.len()} primes up to 100, last={primes[primes.len() - 1]}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"fn sieve(limit: i32) -> Vec<i32> {\n"
"    let mut marks = Vec<u8>.filled(0, limit + 1);\n"
"    let primes: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();\n"
"    for (let i = 2; i <= limit; i += 1) {\n"
"        if (marks[i] == 0) {\n"
"            primes.push(i);\n"
"            let mut m = i * i;\n"
"            while (m <= limit) {\n"
"                marks[m] = 1;\n"
"                m += i;\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    return primes;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sieve\");\n"
"    let primes = sieve(100);\n"
"    log.info(f\"{primes.len()} primes up to 100, last={primes[primes.len() - 1]}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


