msgid ""
"`--check` prints `unformatted: <file>` and exits `1` when a file needs changes, which makes it a clean CI gate. A file that does not parse is refused loudly rather than half-formatted."
msgstr ""
"`--check` 会在文件需要修改时打印 `unformatted: <file>` 并以 `1` 退出，这让它成为一道干净的 CI 门禁。解析不了的文件会被响亮地拒绝，而不是被格式化一半。"


#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:111
msgid "Inspect"
msgstr "检视"


#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:113
msgid ""
"`dump` compiles a single module and prints its structures — useful when a snippet behaves differently than you expect:"
msgstr "`dump` 编译单个模块并打印它的结构——当代码片段的表现与你预期不同时很有用："


#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:120
msgid ""
"`dump` runs the lone module through the frontend _without_ mounting the packages, so it is the tool for surface questions (\"what does this lower to?\") rather than whole-program runs. The playground's **AST** and **IR** panes show the same two views live — see [the playground](playground.md)."
msgstr ""
"`dump` 让这个孤立的模块走过前端，_不_挂载那些包，因此它是回答“表面问题”（“这段代码被 lower 成了什么？”）的工具，而不是运行整个程序的工具。Playground 的 **AST** 和 **IR** 面板实时展示同样的两个视图——参见 [Playground](playground.md)。"


