#: src/tutorial/values-and-variables.md:23
msgid ""
"There is no `null`, no `undefined`, and no character type. A `str` iterates as one-codepoint `str`s, and codepoints read as `u32` (`s.code()`, `s.code_at(i)`) — see [string slicing and views](../reference/string-views.md)."
msgstr ""
