#: src/tutorial/control-flow.md:364
msgid "Next: [functions, closures, and generics](functions.md)."
msgstr "下一章：[函数、闭包与泛型](functions.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:3
msgid ""
"Functions are declared with `fn`, values can be functions, and generic functions monomorphize at compile time — each instantiation gets its own specialized code. The details live in [the reference on functions, closures, and generics](../reference/functions-closures-generics.md)."
msgstr ""
"函数以 `fn` 声明，值可以是函数，泛型函数在编译期单态化——每个实例化都得到自己的专属代码。细节见[函数、闭包与泛型参考](../reference/functions-closures-generics.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:8
msgid "Declaring functions"
msgstr "声明函数"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:10
msgid ""
"Parameter and return types are always written. A function whose return type is omitted returns nothing:"
msgstr "参数类型与返回类型总是要写出来。省略返回类型的函数不返回任何东西："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:13
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use calc::{ Math };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"fn swap(mut xs: Vec<i32>, a: i32, b: i32) {\n"
"    let t = xs[a];\n"
"    xs[a] = xs[b];\n"
"    xs[b] = t;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn length(pt: Point) -> f64 {\n"
"    return Math.sqrt((pt.x * pt.x + pt.y * pt.y) as f64);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"fns\");\n"
"    let xs = Vec<i32>.from([1, 2, 3]);\n"
"    swap(xs, 0, 2);\n"
"    log.info(f\"first={xs[0]} length={length(Point { x: 3, y: 4 })}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use calc::{ Math };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"fn swap(mut xs: Vec<i32>, a: i32, b: i32) {\n"
"    let t = xs[a];\n"
"    xs[a] = xs[b];\n"
"    xs[b] = t;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn length(pt: Point) -> f64 {\n"
"    return Math.sqrt((pt.x * pt.x + pt.y * pt.y) as f64);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"fns\");\n"
"    let xs = Vec<i32>.from([1, 2, 3]);\n"
"    swap(xs, 0, 2);\n"
"    log.info(f\"first={xs[0]} length={length(Point { x: 3, y: 4 })}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:42
msgid ""
"A `mut` parameter (`fn step(mut p: Point)`) is the callee's permission to write through `p` — and because non-primitive values share, that means the caller's value. A plain parameter promises not to write through it."
msgstr ""
"`mut` 参数（`fn step(mut p: Point)`）是被调用方经由 `p` 写入的许可——由于非基本类型值是共享的，这意味着写入的是调用方的值。普通参数则承诺不经由它写入。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:47
msgid ""
"Recursion works as expected — functions are visible in their own bodies, and mutual recursion within a module needs no forward declaration."
msgstr "递归如预期工作——函数在自己的函数体内可见，模块内的相互递归不需要前置声明。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:51
msgid "Anonymous functions"
msgstr "匿名函数"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:53
msgid ""
"The closure spelling is an anonymous `fn` with a block body. There is no arrow shorthand — every closure states its parameter and return types, which is what lets it inhabit a first-class `fn` type:"
msgstr "闭包的写法是一个带块主体的匿名 `fn`。没有箭头简写——每个闭包都写明自己的参数与返回类型，这正是它能栖身于一等 `fn` 类型的原因："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:57
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"closures\");\n"
"    let add = fn (a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 { return a + b; };\n"
"\n"
"    let area_of = fn (r: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"        let sq = r * r;\n"
"        return sq * 3.14159265f32;\n"
"    };\n"
"\n"
"    add(1, 2);          // call it like any function\n"
"    log.info(f\"add={add(1, 2)} area={area_of(1)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"closures\");\n"
"    let add = fn (a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 { return a + b; };\n"
"\n"
"    let area_of = fn (r: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"        let sq = r * r;\n"
"        return sq * 3.14159265f32;\n"
"    };\n"
"\n"
"    add(1, 2);          // call it like any function\n"
"    log.info(f\"add={add(1, 2)} area={area_of(1)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:78
msgid "Function types are written `fn(P..) -> R` and appear anywhere a type does:"
msgstr "函数类型写作 `fn(P..) -> R`，并且可以出现在任何类型能出现的地方："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:81
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn apply(f: fn(i32) -> i32, v: i32) -> i32 {\n"
"    return f(v);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"fns\");\n"
"    let double = fn (x: i32) -> i32 { return x * 2; };\n"
"    log.info(f\"apply={apply(double, 21)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn apply(f: fn(i32) -> i32, v: i32) -> i32 {\n"
"    return f(v);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"fns\");\n"
"    let double = fn (x: i32) -> i32 { return x * 2; };\n"
"    log.info(f\"apply={apply(double, 21)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:99
msgid ""
"Closures capture the enclosing bindings — a closure body sees and can use the locals around it, including after the enclosing function would have returned, because captured cells stay alive as long as the closure does. Since non-primitives share, a capture of a `Vec` or a struct is a handle to the same cell: writes through the closure are visible to everyone else holding it."
msgstr ""
"闭包捕获外围的绑定——闭包体看得见、用得上周围的局部变量，甚至在外围函数本该返回之后依然可以，因为被捕获的单元与闭包活得一样久。由于非基本类型是共享的，捕获一个 `Vec` 或结构体得到的是指向同一个单元的句柄：经闭包做出的写入，对其他所有持有者都可见。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:106
#: src/reference/functions-closures-generics.md:71
msgid "Generics"
msgstr "泛型"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:108
msgid ""
"A generic function declares type parameters in angle brackets. Each concrete instantiation is compiled separately (monomorphized), so generics cost nothing at runtime:"
msgstr "泛型函数在尖括号里声明类型参数。每个具体实例化都单独编译（单态化），因此泛型在运行时零开销："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:112
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn first<T>(xs: [T], fallback: T) -> T {\n"
"    if (xs.len() == 0) {\n"
"        return fallback;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return xs[0];\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"generics\");\n"
"    let head = first([10, 20], -1);      // first<i32> — inferred\n"
"    let name = first([\"a\", \"b\"], \"?\");   // first<str> — a separate instance\n"
"    log.info(f\"head={head} name={name}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn first<T>(xs: [T], fallback: T) -> T {\n"
"    if (xs.len() == 0) {\n"
"        return fallback;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return xs[0];\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"generics\");\n"
"    let head = first([10, 20], -1);      // first<i32> — inferred\n"
"    let name = first([\"a\", \"b\"], \"?\");   // first<str> — a separate instance\n"
"    log.info(f\"head={head} name={name}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:134
msgid ""
"`T` is inferred from the arguments; you rarely spell `first<i32>(..)` explicitly. Two rules to know:"
msgstr "`T` 由实参推断；你很少需要显式写出 `first<i32>(..)`。有两条规则值得知道："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:137
msgid ""
"A bare `T` has **no methods** — you cannot call anything on a value whose type is just `T`. Pass concrete values in, or take a trait-typed parameter instead (next chapter)."
msgstr "裸的 `T` **没有任何方法**——你无法在类型仅为 `T` 的值上调用任何东西。要么传具体值进来，要么改用 trait 类型的参数（下一章）。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:140
msgid ""
"In v1 a _generic class_ in a parameter position does not unify — `fn sum(xs: Vec<i32>)` is fine, but a function generic over `T` taking `Vec<T>` is not yet the shape to reach for. Concrete instantiations cover most code."
msgstr ""
"在 v1 里，参数位置上的_泛型类_不做统一——`fn sum(xs: Vec<i32>)` 没问题，但对 `T` 泛型又接收 `Vec<T>` 的函数还不是值得选用的形状。具体实例化覆盖大多数代码。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:145
msgid "`requires` bounds"
msgstr "`requires` 约束"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:147
msgid "An inline `requires` bound gates which instantiations compile:"
msgstr "内联的 `requires` 约束限定哪些实例化可以编译："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:149
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Labeled {\n"
"    fn label(self) -> str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Tag { id: i32 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Labeled for Tag {\n"
"    fn label(self) -> str { return f\"tag-{self.id}\"; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn name<T requires Labeled>(x: T) -> str {\n"
"    let w: Labeled = x;     // the bound proves this widening\n"
"    return w.label();\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"bounds\");\n"
"    log.info(name(Tag { id: 7 }));\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Labeled {\n"
"    fn label(self) -> str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Tag { id: i32 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Labeled for Tag {\n"
"    fn label(self) -> str { return f\"tag-{self.id}\"; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn name<T requires Labeled>(x: T) -> str {\n"
"    let w: Labeled = x;     // the bound proves this widening\n"
"    return w.label();\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"bounds\");\n"
"    log.info(name(Tag { id: 7 }));\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:177
msgid ""
"The bound is _admission-only_: it checks at each call site that the concrete type satisfies the named trait (or union of traits), and it proves a `T`\\-typed value may be used as that trait type — it does not put methods on `T` itself. Union bounds admit any member:"
msgstr ""
"这个约束是_只管准入的_：它在每个调用点检查具体类型满足所写的 trait（或 trait 并集），并证明一个 `T` 类型的值可以用作那个 trait 类型——它不会把方法挂到 `T` 本身上。并集约束接受任何成员："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:186
msgid ""
"This is exactly how typed JSON entry points are spelled — `decodeJson<T requires JsonDeserialize>(s: str)` — see [errors and optionality](errors.md). Bounds and unions are covered fully in [the reference on type aliases and union bounds](../reference/type-aliases.md)."
msgstr ""
"类型化 JSON 入口的写法正是如此——`decodeJson<T requires JsonDeserialize>(s: str)`——参见[错误与可空性](errors.md)。约束与并集在[类型别名与并集约束参考](../reference/type-aliases.md)里完整覆盖。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:191
msgid "Free functions are the default idiom"
msgstr "自由函数是默认惯用法"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:193
msgid ""
"rut's records carry no methods (bodies are fields only; methods live in `impl` blocks — see [structs, enums, and classes](types.md)), so the everyday shape is small data plus free functions over it:"
msgstr ""
"rut 的记录不携带方法（主体只有字段；方法住在 `impl` 块里——参见[结构体、枚举与类](types.md)），因此日常的形状是小数据，外加作用于其上的自由函数："


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:197
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"fn nudged(pt: Point) -> Point {\n"
"    return Point { x: pt.x + 1, y: pt.y };\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"free-fns\");\n"
"    let p = nudged(Point { x: 2, y: 5 });\n"
"    log.info(f\"p.x={p.x} p.y={p.y}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"fn nudged(pt: Point) -> Point {\n"
"    return Point { x: pt.x + 1, y: pt.y };\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"free-fns\");\n"
"    let p = nudged(Point { x: 2, y: 5 });\n"
"    log.info(f\"p.x={p.x} p.y={p.y}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:217
msgid ""
"Reach for methods when something is genuinely _the receiver's_ behavior, and for trait impls — everything else is a plain function."
msgstr "当某件事确实是_接收者_的行为时才用方法，trait impl 也是如此——其余一切都是普通函数。"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:222
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn first<T>(xs: [T], fallback: T) -> T {\n"
"    if (xs.len() == 0) {\n"
"        return fallback;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return xs[0];\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn sum(xs: Vec<i32>) -> i32 {\n"
"    let mut total = 0;\n"
"    for (let x of xs) {\n"
"        total += x;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return total;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"closures\");\n"
"    let add = fn (a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 { return a + b; };\n"
"    let area_of = fn (r: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"        let sq = r * r;\n"
"        return sq * 3.14159265f32;\n"
"    };\n"
"    log.info(f\"add={add(1, 2)} area={area_of(1)} sum={sum(Vec<i32>.from([1, 2, 3]))}\");\n"
"\n"
"    let head = first([10, 20], -1);       // first<i32> — monomorphized\n"
"    let name = first([\"a\", \"b\"], \"?\");    // first<str> — separate instance\n"
"    log.info(f\"head={head} name={name}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn first<T>(xs: [T], fallback: T) -> T {\n"
"    if (xs.len() == 0) {\n"
"        return fallback;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return xs[0];\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn sum(xs: Vec<i32>) -> i32 {\n"
"    let mut total = 0;\n"
"    for (let x of xs) {\n"
"        total += x;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return total;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"closures\");\n"
"    let add = fn (a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 { return a + b; };\n"
"    let area_of = fn (r: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"        let sq = r * r;\n"
"        return sq * 3.14159265f32;\n"
"    };\n"
"    log.info(f\"add={add(1, 2)} area={area_of(1)} sum={sum(Vec<i32>.from([1, 2, 3]))}\");\n"
"\n"
"    let head = first([10, 20], -1);       // first<i32> — monomorphized\n"
"    let name = first([\"a\", \"b\"], \"?\");    // first<str> — separate instance\n"
"    log.info(f\"head={head} name={name}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/functions.md:261
msgid "Next: [structs, enums, and classes](types.md)."
msgstr "下一章：[结构体、枚举与类](types.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:3
msgid "rut has three user-defined type forms, each with one job:"
msgstr "rut 有三种用户自定义类型形式，各司一职："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:5
msgid "**`enum`** — a small set of named constants."
msgstr "**`enum`**——一小批命名常量。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:6
msgid ""
"**`struct`** — an open data record: every field public, literal construction everywhere."
msgstr "**`struct`**——开放的数据记录：所有字段公开，随处可用字面量构造。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:8
msgid ""
"**`class`** — a sealed record: private fields, construction through class methods only."
msgstr "**`class`**——封闭的记录：字段私有，只能经由类方法构造。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:11
msgid ""
"In all three, **the type body is fields only** — every method lives in an `impl` block. A `fn` written inside a type body is a parse error. The reference pages are [structs](../reference/structs.md), [enums](../reference/enums.md), and [classes and constructors](../reference/classes.md)."
msgstr ""
"在这三者中，**类型主体只有字段**——每个方法都住在 `impl` 块里。写在类型主体里的 `fn` 是解析错误。参考页是[结构体](../reference/structs.md)、[枚举](../reference/enums.md)与[类与构造器](../reference/classes.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:20
msgid ""
"An enum is a distinct named type over integer constants. No payloads, no methods, no computed members — where another language would use a union of literal strings, rut uses an enum:"
msgstr "枚举是建立在整型常量之上的一个独立命名类型。没有载荷，没有方法，没有计算型成员——换作别的语言会在字面量字符串的并集上做文章的地方，rut 用枚举："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:24
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"enum Light { Green, Yellow, Red }\n"
"\n"
"enum Direction { Up = 1, Down, Left, Right }   // 1, 2, 3, 4\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"enums\");\n"
"    log.info(f\"{Light.Green} {Direction.Left} {Direction.Right}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"enum Light { Green, Yellow, Red }\n"
"\n"
"enum Direction { Up = 1, Down, Left, Right }   // 1, 2, 3, 4\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"enums\");\n"
"    log.info(f\"{Light.Green} {Direction.Left} {Direction.Right}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:41
msgid ""
"Members are the enum's values and are spelled qualified: `Light.Green`. Explicit initializers set where the numbering starts; the rest continue from there."
msgstr "成员就是枚举的值，书写时带限定：`Light.Green`。显式初始化器设定编号从哪里开始；其余成员从那里继续。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:45
msgid ""
"`when` over an enum must be exhaustive — every member, or an `else` arm (see [control flow and when](control-flow.md)). Enums render as their member name in format strings."
msgstr ""
"对枚举的 `when` 必须穷尽——覆盖每个成员，或带一个 `else` 分支（参见[控制流与 when](control-flow.md)）。枚举在格式化字符串里渲染为成员名。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:49
msgid "Structs — open records"
msgstr "结构体——开放的记录"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:51
msgid ""
"Declare with `struct`, construct with a literal — anywhere in a function body, nested inside other literals. There is no `new`:"
msgstr "用 `struct` 声明，用字面量构造——函数体内的任何位置，或嵌在其他字面量里。没有 `new`："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:54
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point {\n"
"    x: f32;\n"
"    y: f32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Rect {\n"
"    min: Point;\n"
"    max: Point;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Style {\n"
"    color: u32 = 0xff00ff;      // field initializer: literals may omit it\n"
"    width: f32 = 1;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"structs\");\n"
"    let p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };                    // every field, by name\n"
"    let s = Style {};                                // defaults fill the rest\n"
"    let r = Rect { min: Point { x: 0, y: 0 }, max: p };\n"
"    log.info(f\"r.max.x={r.max.x} width={s.width}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point {\n"
"    x: f32;\n"
"    y: f32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Rect {\n"
"    min: Point;\n"
"    max: Point;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Style {\n"
"    color: u32 = 0xff00ff;      // field initializer: literals may omit it\n"
"    width: f32 = 1;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"structs\");\n"
"    let p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };                    // every field, by name\n"
"    let s = Style {};                                // defaults fill the rest\n"
"    let r = Rect { min: Point { x: 0, y: 0 }, max: p };\n"
"    log.info(f\"r.max.x={r.max.x} width={s.width}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:85
msgid ""
"All fields are public, always — member visibility in a struct is a compile error. Privacy is what classes are for."
msgstr "所有字段永远公开——给结构体成员标注可见性是编译错误。私有正是类存在的意义。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:88
msgid ""
"**Structs share.** A struct value is a handle to a heap cell: assignment, arguments, and returns all pass the handle, and a write through any alias is visible through all of them. Writing needs a `mut` binding or `mut` parameter:"
msgstr ""
"**结构体共享。**结构体值是指向堆单元的句柄：赋值、实参和返回传递的都是句柄，经由任何别名做出的写入，经所有别名都可见。写入需要 `mut` 绑定或 `mut` 参数："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:93
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sharing\");\n"
"    let mut p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };\n"
"    let q = p;              // q and p name ONE cell\n"
"    p.x = 4;                // q.x is 4 now\n"
"    log.info(f\"q.x={q.x} same cell: {q == p}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sharing\");\n"
"    let mut p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };\n"
"    let q = p;              // q and p name ONE cell\n"
"    p.x = 4;                // q.x is 4 now\n"
"    log.info(f\"q.x={q.x} same cell: {q == p}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:111
msgid ""
"`==` on struct values is **cell identity** — `q == p` is true (one cell), `p == Point { x: 4, y: 2 }` is false (a different cell). To compare field by field, write a function."
msgstr ""
"结构体值上的 `==` 是**单元同一性**——`q == p` 为 true（同一个单元），`p == Point { x: 4, y: 2 }` 为 false（另一个单元）。想逐字段比较，就写一个函数。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:115
msgid ""
"Recursive shapes are legal — a record may name itself through a nullable field, because `?Node` is one word:"
msgstr "递归的形状是合法的——记录可以经由可空字段指涉自身，因为 `?Node` 就是一个词："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:118
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Node {\n"
"    value: i32;\n"
"    left: ?Node;\n"
"    right: ?Node;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn count(n: ?Node) -> i32 {\n"
"    let mut c = 1;\n"
"    if (n.left != nil) { c += count(n.left); }\n"
"    if (n.right != nil) { c += count(n.right); }\n"
"    return c;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"nodes\");\n"
"    let n = Node {\n"
"        value: 1,\n"
"        left: Node { value: 2, left: nil, right: nil },\n"
"        right: nil,\n"
"    };\n"
"    log.info(f\"count={count(n)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Node {\n"
"    value: i32;\n"
"    left: ?Node;\n"
"    right: ?Node;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn count(n: ?Node) -> i32 {\n"
"    let mut c = 1;\n"
"    if (n.left != nil) { c += count(n.left); }\n"
"    if (n.right != nil) { c += count(n.right); }\n"
"    return c;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"nodes\");\n"
"    let n = Node {\n"
"        value: 1,\n"
"        left: Node { value: 2, left: nil, right: nil },\n"
"        right: nil,\n"
"    };\n"
"    log.info(f\"count={count(n)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:149
msgid "Classes — sealed records"
msgstr "类——封闭的记录"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:151
msgid ""
"A class adds two things to a struct: module-private fields and construction gated through class methods. There is no `constructor` keyword, no `new` operator, and no outside literal — the only way to build a class value from outside is to call a class method that chooses to. (Cleanup hooks are not a class privilege: implement `Disposal` for either shape, and the engine calls `dispose` when the value's cell refcount reaches zero — see [Rc, dispose, and identity](../reference/rc-dispose-identity.md).)"
msgstr ""
"类在结构体之上加两样东西：模块私有的字段，以及经由类方法把守的构造。没有 `constructor` 关键字、没有 `new` 运算符、也没有外部字面量——从外部构建类值的唯一途径，是调用一个愿意为你构建的类方法。（清理钩子并不是类的特权：为任一形态实现 `Disposal`，引擎就会在该值的单元引用计数归零时调用 `dispose`——参见[Rc、dispose 与同一性](../reference/rc-dispose-identity.md)。）"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:160
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Counter {\n"
"    n: i32 = 0;             // module-private — the class's business\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Counter {\n"
"    pub fn new() -> Self {                 // the construction surface\n"
"        return Self { };                   // the class-private literal\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn press(mut self) {\n"
"        self.n = self.n.wrapping_add(1);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn count(self) -> i32 { return self.n; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"counter\");\n"
"    let c = Counter.new();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    log.info(f\"count={c.count()}\");      // 2\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Counter {\n"
"    n: i32 = 0;             // module-private — the class's business\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Counter {\n"
"    pub fn new() -> Self {                 // the construction surface\n"
"        return Self { };                   // the class-private literal\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn press(mut self) {\n"
"        self.n = self.n.wrapping_add(1);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn count(self) -> i32 { return self.n; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"counter\");\n"
"    let c = Counter.new();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    log.info(f\"count={c.count()}\");      // 2\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:192
msgid "The pieces:"
msgstr "组成部分如下："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:194
msgid ""
"**A class method is just a function without `self`.** `Rect.new(w, h)`, `Version.parse(s)`, `Rect.from_square(s)` — any no-`self` method returning `Self` is a constructor. `new` is a convention, not syntax."
msgstr ""
"**类方法就是不带 `self` 的函数。**`Rect.new(w, h)`、`Version.parse(s)`、`Rect.from_square(s)`——任何不带 `self` 且返回 `Self` 的方法都是构造器。`new` 是约定，不是语法。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:197
msgid ""
"**The `Self { .. }` literal is class-private** — legal anywhere in the class's own impl block, never outside. This is the seal."
msgstr "**`Self { .. }` 字面量是类私有的**——在类自己的 impl 块内的任何地方都合法，出了它就再也不合法。这就是封闭。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:199
msgid ""
"**Instance methods spell `self` explicitly** as the first parameter; `mut self` marks methods that write. There is no `this`, no static methods, no `get`/`set` syntax — a computed property is a method (`c.count()`)."
msgstr ""
"**实例方法把 `self` 显式写成第一个参数**；`mut self` 标记会写入的方法。没有 `this`，没有静态方法，没有 `get`/`set` 语法——计算属性就是一个方法（`c.count()`）。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:203
msgid ""
"**Construction is validation.** A constructor is an ordinary function — it can check arguments and refuse:"
msgstr "**构造即验证。**构造器是一个普通函数——它可以检查实参并拒绝："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:206
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Rect {\n"
"    w: f32;\n"
"    h: f32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Rect {\n"
"    pub fn new(w: f32, h: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        if (w <= 0 || h <= 0) {\n"
"            panic(\"Rect: negative extents\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        return Self { w: w, h: h };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn from_square(s: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        return Rect.new(s, s);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn area(self) -> f32 { return self.w * self.h; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rect\");\n"
"    let r = Rect.new(3, 4);\n"
"    let sq = Rect.from_square(2);\n"
"    log.info(f\"area={r.area()} square={sq.area()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Rect {\n"
"    w: f32;\n"
"    h: f32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Rect {\n"
"    pub fn new(w: f32, h: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        if (w <= 0 || h <= 0) {\n"
"            panic(\"Rect: negative extents\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        return Self { w: w, h: h };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn from_square(s: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        return Rect.new(s, s);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn area(self) -> f32 { return self.w * self.h; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rect\");\n"
"    let r = Rect.new(3, 4);\n"
"    let sq = Rect.from_square(2);\n"
"    log.info(f\"area={r.area()} square={sq.area()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:241
msgid ""
"A _try_\\-constructor answers the nullable — `nil` is a failed validation, not a crash:"
msgstr "_try_ 构造器以可空作答——`nil` 是一次验证失败，不是崩溃："


#: src/tutorial/types.md:244
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"impl Version {\n"
"    pub fn parse(s: str) -> ?Version {\n"
"        // ... split \"1.2\" — on failure:\n"
"        return nil;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"impl Version {\n"
"    pub fn parse(s: str) -> ?Version {\n"
"        // ... split \"1.2\" — on failure:\n"
"        return nil;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:253
msgid ""
"**No inheritance.** There is no `extends`, no `super`, no overriding. Code sharing is composition (hold a helper in a field) or free functions; polymorphism is traits — the next chapter."
msgstr ""
"**没有继承。**没有 `extends`，没有 `super`，没有覆写。代码共享靠组合（把辅助对象放在字段里）或自由函数；多态靠 trait——下一章。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:257
msgid "Visibility recap"
msgstr "可见性小结"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:259
msgid "Struct members: public, always."
msgstr "结构体成员：永远公开。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:260
msgid ""
"Class members: unannotated is module-private; `pub` exposes to importers (also `pub(mod)`, `pub(super)`, `pub(self)`)."
msgstr "类成员：不标注即模块私有；`pub` 对导入方可见（另有 `pub(mod)`、`pub(super)`、`pub(self)`）。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:262
msgid ""
"The types themselves follow the same rule: `pub class Vec<T>` is importable, a bare `class Helper` stays in its module. See [modules and packages](modules.md)."
msgstr ""
"类型本身遵循同一条规则：`pub class Vec<T>` 可被导入，裸的 `class Helper` 则留在其模块内。参见[模块与包](modules.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:266
msgid "Struct or class?"
msgstr "结构体还是类？"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:268
msgid ""
"Default to a struct: data in, data out, shared like every other value. Reach for a class when the type has rules that construction must enforce, holds private state that outsiders must not read, or owns a resource that needs explicit cleanup."
msgstr ""
"默认选结构体：数据进、数据出，像其他一切值一样共享。当类型带有构造时必须强制执行的规则、持有外人不得读取的私有状态、或拥有需要显式清理的资源时，才选类。"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:275
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Counter {\n"
"    n: i32 = 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Counter {\n"
"    pub fn new() -> Self {\n"
"        return Self { };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn press(mut self) {\n"
"        self.n = self.n.wrapping_add(1);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn count(self) -> i32 { return self.n; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"class Rect {\n"
"    w: f32;\n"
"    h: f32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Rect {\n"
"    pub fn new(w: f32, h: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        if (w <= 0 || h <= 0) {\n"
"            panic(\"Rect: negative extents\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        return Self { w: w, h: h };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn from_square(s: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        return Rect.new(s, s);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn area(self) -> f32 { return self.w * self.h; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"classes\");\n"
"    let c = Counter.new();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    let r = Rect.new(3, 4);\n"
"    let sq = Rect.from_square(2.0f32);\n"
"    log.info(f\"count={c.count()} area={r.area()} square={sq.area()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Counter {\n"
"    n: i32 = 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Counter {\n"
"    pub fn new() -> Self {\n"
"        return Self { };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn press(mut self) {\n"
"        self.n = self.n.wrapping_add(1);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn count(self) -> i32 { return self.n; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"class Rect {\n"
"    w: f32;\n"
"    h: f32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Rect {\n"
"    pub fn new(w: f32, h: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        if (w <= 0 || h <= 0) {\n"
"            panic(\"Rect: negative extents\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        return Self { w: w, h: h };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn from_square(s: f32) -> Self {\n"
"        return Rect.new(s, s);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn area(self) -> f32 { return self.w * self.h; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"classes\");\n"
"    let c = Counter.new();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    c.press();\n"
"    let r = Rect.new(3, 4);\n"
"    let sq = Rect.from_square(2.0f32);\n"
"    log.info(f\"count={c.count()} area={r.area()} square={sq.area()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/types.md:329
msgid "Next: [traits and impl blocks](traits.md)."
msgstr "下一章：[trait 与 impl 块](traits.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:3
msgid ""
"A trait declares a set of methods; a type joins the trait by writing an impl block. Satisfaction is **nominal** — the impl block is the only admission. A type whose members all happen to match a trait's shapes is still not an instance of it until someone writes the block. The full dispatch story is in [the reference on traits](../reference/traits.md) and [traits and dispatch](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)."
msgstr ""
"trait 声明一组方法；类型通过写一个 impl 块来加入 trait。满足是**名义上的**——impl 块是唯一准入。某个类型的成员即便碰巧全都长得符合一个 trait 的形状，在有人写下那个块之前，它也不是该 trait 的实例。完整的分派故事见 [trait 参考](../reference/traits.md)与[trait 与分派](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:10
msgid "Declaring a trait"
msgstr "声明 trait"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:12
msgid ""
"Traits declare method signatures — no bodies, no default implementations, no fields:"
msgstr "trait 只声明方法签名——没有方法体，没有默认实现，没有字段："


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:22
msgid ""
"Methods spell their receiver `self` explicitly, like every rut method. Anything that looks like a property is a method: declare `fn count(self) -> i32;`, not a field."
msgstr ""
"方法与每个 rut 方法一样，显式写出接收者 `self`。任何看起来像属性的东西都是方法：声明 `fn count(self) -> i32;`，而不是字段。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:26
msgid "Implementing a trait"
msgstr "实现 trait"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:28
msgid ""
"`impl Trait for Type { .. }` registers the pair. Every method must match the trait's signature exactly; extra methods don't belong here (put those in an inherent block). Trait impl methods carry no `pub` — they are as visible as the trait."
msgstr ""
"`impl Trait for Type { .. }` 登记这一对组合。每个方法都必须与 trait 的签名完全一致；额外的方法不属于这里（把它们放进固有块）。trait impl 的方法不带 `pub`——它们的可见性与 trait 一致。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:33
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"    fn name(self) -> str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Circle { r: f64 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Circle {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return 3.14159 * self.r * self.r; }\n"
"    fn name(self) -> str { return \"circle\"; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"traits\");\n"
"    let c = Circle { r: 1.0 };\n"
"    log.info(f\"{c.name()}={c.area()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"    fn name(self) -> str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Circle { r: f64 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Circle {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return 3.14159 * self.r * self.r; }\n"
"    fn name(self) -> str { return \"circle\"; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"traits\");\n"
"    let c = Circle { r: 1.0 };\n"
"    log.info(f\"{c.name()}={c.area()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:59
msgid "Rules worth knowing:"
msgstr "几条值得知道的规则："


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:61
msgid ""
"**One impl per (trait, type) pair, program-wide.** A duplicate is a link error."
msgstr "**每个（trait, 类型）组合全程序只能有一个 impl。**重复是链接错误。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:63
msgid ""
"**Placement:** an impl may live in a module of the trait's package or the type's package — at least one side must be yours. You cannot implement two foreign types to each other."
msgstr "**位置：**impl 可以放在 trait 所在包或类型所在包的模块里——至少有一侧必须属于你。你不能给两个外部类型互相实现。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:66
msgid ""
"**An empty impl block is legal** and acts as a marker: `impl Serializable for Point {}` says \"this type is in\" when the trait has no required methods."
msgstr ""
"**空 impl 块是合法的**，并可充当标记：当 trait 没有必需方法时，`impl Serializable for Point {}` 表示“该类型已加入”。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:69
msgid ""
"**Primitives can implement traits too** (in the trait's own package or module) — the standard library uses this to give integer widths a common internal interface."
msgstr "**基本类型也可以实现 trait**（在 trait 自己的包或模块内）——标准库正是用它给各个整数宽度提供了一个共通的内部接口。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:73
msgid "Inherent impls"
msgstr "固有 impl"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:75
msgid ""
"`impl Type { .. }` — no trait — is where a type's own methods live: class methods like `new`, instance methods, helpers. It compiles only in the module that declares the type."
msgstr ""
"`impl Type { .. }`——不带 trait——是类型自身方法的家：`new` 这类类方法、实例方法、辅助方法。它只在声明该类型的模块里编译。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:79
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
