#: src/tutorial/traits.md:256
msgid ""
"`is` answers the question; it changes nothing — there is no narrowing and no downcast through a trait. A trait-typed value is used through its trait's methods; if you need the erased-storage version — a value whose type is _forgotten_ until recovered — that is `opaque`, covered in [errors and optionality](errors.md) and [the reference on opaque](../reference/opaque.md)."
msgstr ""
"`is` 只回答问题，不改变任何东西——既没有窄化，也没有经由 trait 的向下转型。trait 类型的值经由其 trait 的方法来使用；如果你需要擦除存储的版本——一个在被取回之前_忘记_自身类型的值——那就是 `opaque`，见[错误与可空性](errors.md)与 [opaque 参考](../reference/opaque.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:263
msgid "Bounds connect traits to generics"
msgstr "约束把 trait 与泛型连接起来"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:265
msgid ""
"`fn name<T requires Labeled>(x: T)` admits exactly the instantiations whose concrete type has an impl of `Labeled` — see [functions, closures, and generics](functions.md). The bound is what makes widening legal inside the body: `let w: Labeled = x;`."
msgstr ""
"`fn name<T requires Labeled>(x: T)` 只接受具体类型拥有 `Labeled` impl 的那些实例化——参见[函数、闭包与泛型](functions.md)。正是这个约束让函数体内的加宽合法：`let w: Labeled = x;`。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:270
msgid "Making your type iterable"
msgstr "让你的类型可迭代"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:272
msgid ""
"A type becomes a `for..of` target by implementing the builtin `Iterator<E>` contract with its single resumption member (`Iterator` is core's import-gated `pub builtin` trait — an `impl` names it, so bring it in with `use core::{ Iterator }`; the builtin sequences themselves never need it):"
msgstr ""
"一个类型通过实现内置的 `Iterator<E>` 契约——及其唯一的恢复成员——成为 `for..of` 的目标（`Iterator` 是 core 的导入把守 `pub builtin` trait——`impl` 块会点名它，因此用 `use core::{ Iterator }` 把它带进来；内置序列本身从不需要它）："


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:278
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use core::{ Iterator };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct CountUp { n: i32 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Iterator<i32> for CountUp {\n"
"    fn __iterate(self, emit: fn(i32) -> bool) {\n"
"        for (let i = 1; i <= self.n; i += 1) {\n"
"            if (!emit(i)) { return; }   // false = stop\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"iter\");\n"
"    let ups = CountUp { n: 4 };\n"
"    let got: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();   // shared: survives the loop's captures\n"
"    for (let v of ups) {\n"
"        got.push(v);\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"n={got.len()} first={got[0]} last={got[got.len()-1]}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rutuse core::{ Iterator };use pouch::{ Vec };use ink::{ Logger };struct CountUp { n: i32 }impl Iterator<i32> for CountUp {    fn __iterate(self, emit: fn(i32) -> bool) {        for (let i = 1; i <= self.n; i += 1) {            if (!emit(i)) { return; }   // false = stop        }    }}pub fn main() {    let log = Logger.new(\"iter\");    let ups = CountUp { n: 4 };    let got: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();   // shared: survives the loop's captures    for (let v of ups) {        got.push(v);    }    log.info(f\"n={got.len()} first={got[0]} last={got[got.len()-1]}\");}```"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:308
msgid ""
"`for (let v of it)` desugars to `it.__iterate(emit)` with a synthetic closure. One consequence to know: the loop body's captures are taken at the desugar, so reassigning an enclosing _scalar_ inside the loop mutates a copy, not the original. Accumulate through something shared instead — `vec.push(v)` — or have the loop body act on values it can see directly."
msgstr ""
"`for (let v of it)` 会脱糖为带合成闭包的 `it.__iterate(emit)`。有一个需要知道的后果：循环体的捕获发生在脱糖之时，因此在循环内重新赋值外围的_标量_，改的是副本而不是原件。要累积，就通过某个共享的东西——`vec.push(v)`——或者让循环体作用于它能直接看到的值。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:315
msgid ""
"The builtin sequences (`[T]`, `Vec<T>`, `str`, `bytes`) iterate without the trait — their loops are fused, never a per-element call."
msgstr "内置序列（`[T]`、`Vec<T>`、`str`、`bytes`）无需这个 trait 即可迭代——它们的循环是融合的，绝不是逐元素调用。"


#: src/tutorial/traits.md:320
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"    fn name(self) -> str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Circle { r: f64 }\n"
"struct Square { side: f64 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Circle {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return 3.14159 * self.r * self.r; }\n"
"    fn name(self) -> str { return \"circle\"; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Square {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.side * self.side; }\n"
"    fn name(self) -> str { return \"square\"; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn describe(s: Shape) -> str {\n"
"    return f\"{s.name()}={s.area()}\";\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"traits\");\n"
"\n"
"    let c: Shape = Circle { r: 1.0 };\n"
"    log.info(describe(c));\n"
"\n"
"    let sq = Square { side: 2.0 };\n"
"    log.info(f\"is shape: {sq is Shape}\");\n"
"\n"
"    let mut shapes: Vec<Shape> = Vec.new();\n"
"    shapes.push(Circle { r: 1.0 });\n"
"    shapes.push(Square { side: 3.0 });\n"
"    let mut total: f64 = 0.0;\n"
"    for (let s of shapes) {\n"
"        total += s.area();\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"total={total} n={shapes.len()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
