#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:112
msgid "Erasure and cleanup"
msgstr "擦除与清理"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:114
msgid ""
"`opaque(v)` seals any value for recovery with `opaque.downcast<T>(o) -> ?T` — see [errors and optionality](errors.md). Implementing `Disposal` for a type gives it cleanup code that runs when its cell's refcount reaches zero, and `Weak.new(v)` holds a non-keeping reference (`upgrade() -> ?T`, `nil` once the referent died) — the memory stories live in [the Rc heap and destructors](../reference/rc-heap.md) and [weak references](../reference/weak-refs.md)."
msgstr ""
"`opaque(v)` 封存任意值，供日后以 `opaque.downcast<T>(o) -> ?T` 取回——参见[错误与可空性](errors.md)。为一个类型实现 `Disposal`，就给了它一段在单元引用计数归零时运行的清理代码；`Weak.new(v)` 则持有一个不保活的引用（`upgrade() -> ?T`，所指者死亡后为 `nil`）——内存的故事见 [Rc 堆与析构器](../reference/rc-heap.md)与[弱引用](../reference/weak-refs.md)。"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:123
msgid "The builder is a package"
msgstr "构建器是一个包"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:125
msgid ""
"Core has no string-building class: the growable builder lives in the `strbuild` package ([the stdlib reference](../reference/stdlib.md#strbuild--the-builder)) — `use strbuild::{ StringBuilder }`. For the common accumulator shape you need no builder at all: `out = f\"{out}{t}\"` appends in place, linear in the total output."
msgstr ""
"core 没有字符串构建类：可增长的构建器住在 `strbuild` 包里（[标准库参考](../reference/stdlib.md#strbuild--the-builder)）——`use strbuild::{ StringBuilder }`。对常见的累加器形状，你完全不需要构建器：`out = f\"{out}{t}\"` 就地追加，总输出量级为线性。"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:132
msgid "One gated name"
msgstr "唯一需要显式启用的名字"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:134
msgid ""
"`NAN` is core's single constant, deliberately name-explicit: `use core::{ NAN };`. The float constants live in `calc`."
msgstr "`NAN` 是 core 唯一的常量，刻意要求显式点名：`use core::{ NAN };`。浮点常量住在 `calc` 里。"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:137
msgid "`pouch` — the growable sequence"
msgstr "`pouch`——可增长序列"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:139
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"pouch\");\n"
"    let mut xs: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();         // or Vec.with_capacity(64)\n"
"    xs.push(10);                              // amortized O(1)\n"
"    let v = Vec<f32>.filled(0.0, 1024);       // n slots of one value\n"
"    let w = Vec<i32>.from([1, 2, 3]);         // from a fixed array (copies)\n"
"    let x = xs[0];                            // indexing\n"
"    xs[0] = 42;                               // needs a `mut` binding\n"
"    let last = xs.pop();                      // removes + returns; traps if empty\n"
"    let n = xs.len();\n"
"    let mut total = 0;\n"
"    for (let e of w) {                        // iteration\n"
"        total += e;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"x={x} last={last} len-after-pop={n} filled={v.len()} total={total}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"pouch\");\n"
"    let mut xs: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();         // or Vec.with_capacity(64)\n"
"    xs.push(10);                              // amortized O(1)\n"
"    let v = Vec<f32>.filled(0.0, 1024);       // n slots of one value\n"
"    let w = Vec<i32>.from([1, 2, 3]);         // from a fixed array (copies)\n"
"    let x = xs[0];                            // indexing\n"
"    xs[0] = 42;                               // needs a `mut` binding\n"
"    let last = xs.pop();                      // removes + returns; traps if empty\n"
"    let n = xs.len();\n"
"    let mut total = 0;\n"
"    for (let e of w) {                        // iteration\n"
"        total += e;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"x={x} last={last} len-after-pop={n} filled={v.len()} total={total}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:165
msgid ""
"`Vec<u8>` is the mutable byte builder: `push` bytes, then `freeze()` into the immutable `bytes`. `xs.as_array()` copies the live elements into a fixed `[T]`. A `slice(from, to)` window is compiler-lowered — an O(1) view that writes through to the parent vector."
msgstr ""
"`Vec<u8>` 是可变的字节构建器：`push` 进字节，然后 `freeze()` 成不可变的 `bytes`。`xs.as_array()` 把存活的元素复制进一个定长 `[T]`。`slice(from, to)` 窗口由编译器下降实现——一个写穿透到父向量的 O(1) 视图。"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:170
msgid "`nmapset` — keyed collections"
msgstr "`nmapset`——键控集合"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:172
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use nmapset::{ HashMap, HashSet };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"nmapset\");\n"
"    let mut counts: HashMap<str, i32> = HashMap.new();\n"
"    let fresh = counts.put(\"rut\", 1);          // answers true when the key was NEWLY added\n"
"    let mut n = 0;\n"
"    let hit = counts.get(\"rut\");   // ?i32 — nil means absent\n"
"    if (hit != nil) { n = hit + 1; }\n"
"    let there = counts.has(\"rut\");             // membership\n"
"    let gone = counts.remove(\"runs\");         // answers whether it was there\n"
"    let size = counts.len();\n"
"\n"
"    let mut seen: HashSet<str> = HashSet.new();\n"
"    let first = seen.put(\"x\");     // true — newly added\n"
"    let again = seen.put(\"x\");     // false\n"
"    log.info(f\"fresh={fresh} n={n} has={there} removed={gone} len={size}\");\n"
"    log.info(f\"first={first} again={again}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use nmapset::{ HashMap, HashSet };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"nmapset\");\n"
"    let mut counts: HashMap<str, i32> = HashMap.new();\n"
"    let fresh = counts.put(\"rut\", 1);          // answers true when the key was NEWLY added\n"
"    let mut n = 0;\n"
"    let hit = counts.get(\"rut\");   // ?i32 — nil means absent\n"
"    if (hit != nil) { n = hit + 1; }\n"
"    let there = counts.has(\"rut\");             // membership\n"
"    let gone = counts.remove(\"runs\");         // answers whether it was there\n"
"    let size = counts.len();\n"
"\n"
"    let mut seen: HashSet<str> = HashSet.new();\n"
"    let first = seen.put(\"x\");     // true — newly added\n"
"    let again = seen.put(\"x\");     // false\n"
"    log.info(f\"fresh={fresh} n={n} has={there} removed={gone} len={size}\");\n"
"    log.info(f\"first={first} again={again}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:200
msgid ""
"Keys come from a fixed set — integers, `bool`, `str`, `bytes` (no floats: they have no stable equality contract) — hashed by the host; a user-defined key escapes by encoding canonically to `bytes`. A hit returns the stored cell, not a copy. There is no iteration surface: maps and sets answer questions, they don't walk."
msgstr ""
"键来自一个固定集合——整数、`bool`、`str`、`bytes`（没有浮点数：它们没有稳定的相等契约）——由宿主做哈希；用户自定义的键以规范编码成 `bytes` 的方式破例。命中返回的是存储的单元，不是副本。没有迭代表面：map 和 set 回答问题，不做遍历。"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:206
msgid "`strbuild` — the string builder"
msgstr "`strbuild`——字符串构建器"


#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:208
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use strbuild::{ StringBuilder };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"strbuild\");\n"
"    let n = 3;\n"
"    let mut b = StringBuilder.new();     // or StringBuilder.with_cap(1024)\n"
"    b.append(\"count: \");\n"
"    b.append_code(33);                   // one codepoint\n"
"    b.append(f\" up to {n}\");             // appends are amortized O(1)\n"
"    let s = b.build();                   // the ONE materialization; builder keeps its buffer\n"
"    log.info(s);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
