#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:376
msgid ""
"That completes the tutorial. From here, the [core concepts](../core-concepts/design-goals.md) explain _why_ the language is shaped the way it is, and the [reference](../reference/lexical-structure.md) pins down every rule."
msgstr ""
"教程到此完成。从这里出发，[核心概念](../core-concepts/design-goals.md)解释这门语言_为何_被塑造成如今的形状，[参考](../reference/lexical-structure.md)则钉牢每一条规则。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:3
msgid ""
"rut is a small, statically typed, embeddable scripting language with Rust-flavored syntax, implemented in Rust. It is designed to be the scripting layer of host applications — UI apps in particular — in the role a JavaScript engine usually plays: a safe, hot-reloadable language that drives the host's object graph."
msgstr ""
"rut 是一门小型、静态类型、可嵌入的脚本语言，语法带 Rust 风格，用 Rust 实现。它被设计为宿主应用的脚本层——尤其是 UI 应用——扮演通常由 JavaScript 引擎承担的角色：一门安全、可热重载的语言，驱动宿主的对象图。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:9
msgid ""
"The difference is structural, not cosmetic. In an embedded JS engine the host's types are erased (`Element`, `Store` are empty interfaces; the real types exist only in `.d.ts` files and get \"recovered\" by convention), cancellation is emulated on top of promises, and every value crossing the bridge is re-parsed and re-coerced by hand. rut is built so those three problems cannot arise: **types are kept at runtime**, **coroutines are natively poll-based**, and **host values have deterministic lifetimes**."
msgstr ""
"差异是结构性的，不是表面文章。在嵌入式 JS 引擎里，宿主的类型被擦除（`Element`、`Store` 是空接口；真实类型只存在于 `.d.ts` 文件中，靠约定\"恢复\"回来），取消是在 promise 之上模拟的，而每一个跨越桥的值都要手工重新解析、重新转换。rut 的构建方式让这三个问题根本无从产生：**类型在运行时保留**，**协程原生基于 poll**，**宿主值拥有确定性的生命周期**。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:18
msgid "The pillars"
msgstr "支柱"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:20
msgid ""
"**Fully static, reified types.** There is no dynamic typing, no `any`, no gradual typing. Every value's exact type is known to the compiler and carried at runtime — type tests, checked erasure, and host-boundary checks all read the same runtime truth. See [reified types and layouts](reified-types.md)."
msgstr ""
"**完全静态、具体化的类型。**没有动态类型，没有 `any`，没有渐进类型。每个值的确切类型为编译器所知，并在运行时携带——类型测试、受检擦除与宿主边界检查读取的都是同一份运行时事实。参见[具体化类型与布局](reified-types.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:26
msgid ""
"**Types make code faster.** The bytecode is typed, generics monomorphize, and primitive buffers stay flat: a fixed array of `f32` is a packed `f32` buffer, not an array of boxed numbers. There is no JIT and none is needed — the code shape a JS JIT exists to speculate on (polymorphic property loads) does not exist in rut."
msgstr ""
"**类型让代码更快。**字节码是类型化的，泛型会单态化，原始类型缓冲区保持扁平：一个定长的 `f32` 数组就是一块打包的 `f32` 缓冲区，而不是装箱数字组成的数组。没有 JIT，也不需要 JIT——JS JIT 赖以投机优化的代码形态（多态属性加载）在 rut 里根本不存在。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:32
msgid ""
"**Everything is a value — with two honest regimes.** Primitives move by value; every composite (`str`, `bytes`, records, arrays, trait objects, erasure boxes) is a reference-counted cell whose handle copies in O(1). Sharing is the default and visible; there is no hidden copying. See [everything is a value](everything-is-a-value.md)."
msgstr ""
"**一切皆值——且只有两种如实的体制。**原始类型按值移动；每个复合类型（`str`、`bytes`、记录、数组、trait 对象、擦除盒）都是引用计数单元，复制的是它的句柄，O(1) 完成。共享是默认且可见的；不存在隐藏的复制。参见[一切皆值](everything-is-a-value.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:38
msgid ""
"**Poll-based coroutines.** `async`/`await` compiles to cold state machines with Rust-style poll semantics: a future that nobody drives costs nothing, and cancellation drops the state machine at its suspension point. No promises, no microtask queue. See [the async model](async-model.md)."
msgstr ""
"**基于 poll 的协程。**`async`/`await` 编译为带 Rust 风格 poll 语义的冷状态机：无人驱动的 future 分文不费，取消则在暂停点丢弃状态机。没有 promise，没有微任务队列。参见[异步模型](async-model.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:44
msgid ""
"**Reference counting; no collector.** Objects die the moment their last reference goes away, so destructors are deterministic — host resources (threads, sockets, textures) release at a knowable point, not \"sometime at GC\". Strong cycles leak by design; weak references are the first-class answer. See [memory](memory.md)."
msgstr ""
"**引用计数；没有收集器。**对象在最后一个引用消失的那一刻死亡，因此析构是确定性的——宿主资源（线程、套接字、纹理）在一个可知的时点释放，而不是\"GC 某时某刻\"。强循环引用按设计就会泄漏；弱引用才是一等公民的答案。参见[内存](memory.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:50
msgid ""
"**No JIT.** All optimization happens ahead of time: fold, inline, monomorphize, emit typed bytecode. What you run is what you compiled — predictable startup, predictable per-op cost, no tiering."
msgstr "**没有 JIT。**一切优化都提前发生：折叠、内联、单态化，产出类型化字节码。你运行的就是你编译的——启动可预期、每操作成本可预期、没有分层编译。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:54
msgid ""
"**Embeddable by contract.** The host registers native functions whose Rust signatures _are_ the declared surface; every crossing is type-checked against reified types, and the host owns the event loop, the fuel budget, and the clock. See [the host boundary](host-boundary.md) and [the bytecode VM](the-vm.md)."
msgstr ""
"**以契约方式嵌入。**宿主注册原生函数，其 Rust 签名_就是_所声明的接口；每次跨越都针对具体化类型做类型检查，而事件循环、燃料预算与时钟都归宿主所有。参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)与[字节码 VM](the-vm.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:60
msgid "Why not JavaScript"
msgstr "为什么不用 JavaScript"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:62
msgid ""
"The case against shipping a JS engine — not just this or that implementation — is fourfold, and each item has a structural answer:"
msgstr "反对内置 JS 引擎的理由——不针对某个具体实现，而是针对整类引擎——有四条，每一条都有一个结构层面的回答："


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:65
msgid ""
"**History debt compounds.** Two nullish values, coercing `==`, `typeof null`, implicit semicolons: each is a permanent liability the ecosystem re-implements forever. rut starts from a closed, small grammar — absence is `nil` on a nullable type, errors are values, and the handful of reserved words each name what to write instead. Nothing legacy can accrete."
msgstr ""
"**历史债务复利式累积。**两个表示\\\"空\\\"的值、会做转换的 `==`、`typeof null`、隐式分号：每一条都是永久性的负担，生态系统要永远为之重新实现补丁。rut 从一个封闭的小语法出发——缺失即可空类型上的 `nil`，错误是值，仅有的几个保留字各自指明该写什么。任何遗留物都无从沉积。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:72
msgid ""
"**Conformance means implementing the world.** A compliant engine needs `BigInt`, `Intl`, `Date`'s quirks, microtask ordering — thousands of person-hours before user code runs. rut's built-in contract is deliberately tiny: primitives, sequences, channels, string building. Everything else is library — maps and sets, JSON, logging, and the host's own domain are ordinary packages, several of them written _in rut_ and swappable."
msgstr ""
"**符合规范等于实现整个世界。**一个合规引擎需要 `BigInt`、`Intl`、`Date` 的种种怪癖、微任务顺序——在用户代码能跑起来之前就要投入数千人时。rut 的内置契约刻意保持极小：原始类型、序列、通道、字符串构建。其余一切都是库——map 与 set、JSON、日志以及宿主自身的领域都是普通的包，其中几个就是_in rut_ 写成的，而且可替换。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:80
msgid ""
"**Too slow without a JIT.** Interpreter-only JS runs one to two orders of magnitude slower, because a JS engine's speed _is_ its JIT. rut's no-JIT stance is viable only because the language is statically typed: calls bind statically whenever the call site names one concrete type, and dynamic dispatch is a checked vtable hop that happens only where the program actually erases types."
msgstr ""
"**没有 JIT 就太慢。**纯解释执行的 JS 慢一到两个数量级，因为 JS 引擎的速度_就是_它的 JIT。rut 的无 JIT 立场之所以可行，恰恰因为这门语言是静态类型的：只要调用点指明了一个具体类型，调用就静态绑定；动态分派则是一次经过检查的 vtable 跳转，只发生在程序真正擦除类型的地方。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:87
msgid ""
"**Too much memory.** JS values are boxes — per-object headers, tagged pointers, boxed array elements, collector overhead. rut's answer is layout: untagged 8-byte slots, record payloads as slot arrays, flat primitive buffers, and reference counting with no collector pass on the hot path."
msgstr ""
"**太占内存。**JS 的值都是盒子——每对象头部、带标签的指针、装箱的数组元素、收集器开销。rut 的答案是布局：无标签的 8 字节槽位、以槽数组存放的记录载荷、扁平的原始类型缓冲区，以及热路径上没有收集器扫描的引用计数。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:93
msgid "What \"no dynamic typing\" leaves you"
msgstr "\"没有动态类型\"给你留下什么"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:95
msgid "Erasure is never silent — it is spelled and checked:"
msgstr "擦除从不悄悄发生——它被明确写出并接受检查："


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:97
msgid ""
"**Trait-typed values** (`d: Drawable`) for polymorphism. Dispatch is dynamic only where a value may be one of several concrete types, and a trait-typed value still carries its exact class at runtime."
msgstr ""
"**trait 类型的值**（`d: Drawable`）用于多态。只有当值可能是若干具体类型之一时，分派才是动态的；而且 trait 类型的值在运行时仍携带其确切的类。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:100
msgid ""
"**The `opaque` box** (`opaque(v)`, `opaque.downcast<T>(o)`) for storage. Erasure mints a checked box; recovery checks the runtime type and yields `nil` on a mismatch — never a silent wrong-type read."
msgstr ""
"**`opaque` 盒**（`opaque(v)`、`opaque.downcast<T>(o)`）用于存储。擦除铸造一个经过检查的盒；恢复则检查运行时类型，不匹配时给出 `nil`——绝不会悄悄读出错误类型的值。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:104
msgid ""
"JSON-shaped data, heterogeneous collections, and `any`\\-shaped host APIs all route through these two doors, which is what keeps \"every value has a runtime type\" true without giving up dynamism where it earns its keep."
msgstr ""
"JSON 形状的数据、异构集合以及 `any`\\-形状的宿主 API 都经由这两扇门——\"每个值都有运行时类型\"因此保持为真，同时在动态性真正物有所值之处，它也未被放弃。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:108
msgid "The execution model"
msgstr "执行模型"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:115
msgid ""
"**One thread per VM.** A `Vm` instance runs on one thread with one heap and no atomics; workers are separate VMs communicating by typed message passing."
msgstr ""
"**每个 VM 一个线程。**一个 `Vm` 实例运行在一个线程上，拥有一套堆，不使用原子操作；worker 是彼此独立的 VM，通过类型化的消息传递通信。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:118
msgid ""
"**The host owns time.** The VM exposes stepping verbs — drain the ready queue, expire timers, poll with a deadline — plus op budgets and interrupt callbacks. A UI host drives script between frames and stays responsive; a test host virtualizes the clock and gets fully deterministic schedules."
msgstr ""
"**时间归宿主所有。**VM 暴露一组步进动词——排空就绪队列、让到期的定时器触发、带截止时间的 poll——外加操作预算与中断回调。UI 宿主在帧间驱动脚本并保持响应；测试宿主虚拟化时钟，得到完全确定性的调度。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:123
msgid ""
"**Traps stop at the boundary.** A panic in script (overflow, nil deref) unwinds as a `Trap` value to the host call — rut code never catches one. Bugs become host-visible errors with a script backtrace, not corrupted state."
msgstr ""
"**陷阱止步于边界。**脚本中的 panic（溢出、对 nil 解引用）会以 `Trap` 值的形式沿栈展开到宿主调用——rut 代码永远捕获不到它。bug 变成宿主可见、带脚本回溯的错误，而不是被破坏的状态。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:128 src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:143
#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:239 src/core-concepts/memory.md:204
msgid "What this buys you"
msgstr "这给你带来什么"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:130
msgid ""
"If you are **writing scripts**: assignments never deep-copy; cleanup runs when the last reference dies; a miss is `nil`, a failure is a returned `err` string, and a crash is a loud trap with a real stack trace. If you are **embedding**: you declare your API once in a rut declaration file, bind it with typed Rust closures, and the compiler plus the load-time verifier reject every mismatched shape before any script runs — there is no bridge boilerplate to maintain."
msgstr ""
"如果你在**写脚本**：赋值从不深拷贝；清理在最后一个引用消亡时运行；未命中是 `nil`，失败是一个返回的 `err` 字符串，崩溃则是伴随真实栈回溯的响亮陷阱。如果你在**做嵌入**：你在 rut 声明文件里一次性声明 API，用带类型的 Rust 闭包绑定它，编译器加上加载期校验器会在任何脚本运行之前拒绝每一个不匹配的形状——没有任何需要维护的桥接样板。"


#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:138
msgid ""
"The rest of this section walks each pillar in depth; the tutorial shows the day-to-day syntax, and the reference pins down exact rules."
msgstr "本节其余部分将逐一深入每根支柱；教程展示日常语法，参考手册钉死精确规则。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:3
msgid ""
"rut's type system has one spine: **every name binds a value**, and there are exactly two ways a value can exist. Primitives and `fn` values are _immediate_ — moved by copying their bits. Every other type is a _cell_ — a heap object whose **handle** is what gets copied. That single split explains assignment, parameter passing, equality, and what `bytes.clone()` is for."
msgstr ""
"rut 的类型系统有一条主干：**每个名字绑定的都是值**，而值只有两种存在方式。原始类型与 `fn` 值是_立即的_——通过复制其比特位来移动。其余每种类型都是_单元_——一种堆对象，被复制的是它的**句柄**。仅这一条分界就解释了赋值、传参、相等判断，以及 `bytes.clone()` 存在的意义。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:10
msgid "The two regimes"
msgstr "两种体制"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:12
msgid "immediate"
msgstr "立即"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:12
msgid "cells"
msgstr "单元"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:14
msgid "types"
msgstr "类型"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:14
msgid "`u8..u64`, `i8..i64`, `f32`, `f64`, `bool`, `fn` values"
msgstr "`u8..u64`、`i8..i64`、`f32`、`f64`、`bool`、`fn` 值"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:14
msgid ""
"`str`, `bytes`, `struct` and `class` records, `[T]` arrays, enums, trait objects, `opaque` boxes, `?T` boxes, closures' captured cells"
msgstr ""
"`str`、`bytes`、`struct` 与 `class` 记录、`[T]` 数组、枚举、trait 对象、`opaque` 盒、`?T` 盒、闭包捕获的单元"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:15
msgid "assignment"
msgstr "赋值"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:15
msgid "copies the bits"
msgstr "复制比特位"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:15
msgid "copies the handle (O(1))"
msgstr "复制句柄（O(1)）"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:16
msgid "mutation"
msgstr "变更"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:16
msgid "n/a — write the variable"
msgstr "不适用——直接写入变量"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:16
msgid "visible through every alias"
msgstr "经由每个别名都可见"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:17
msgid "`==`"
msgstr "`==`"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:17
msgid "by value"
msgstr "按值"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:17
msgid "`str`/`bytes`: by content; everything else: identity"
msgstr "`str`/`bytes` 按内容；其余一切按身份"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:19
msgid ""
"There is no third regime. No type is \"sometimes copied, sometimes shared\": a `struct` value never silently deep-copies, a `str` never silently aliases. The regime is a property of the _type_, known at compile time, and the compiler emits the right move for it."
msgstr ""
"没有第三种体制。没有任何类型\"有时复制、有时共享\"：`struct` 值从不悄悄深拷贝，`str` 也从不悄悄别名化。体制是_类型_的属性，编译期即知，编译器会为它生成正确的移动指令。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:24
msgid "Sharing is the law for cells"
msgstr "共享是单元的法则"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:26
msgid ""
"`let b = a` on any cell type is one handle move: the new binding retains the cell, the old binding releases it. Passing a million-element array to a function retains once. A loop binding iterates the _stored_ elements, not copies of them."
msgstr ""
"对任何单元类型写 `let b = a` 只是一次句柄移动：新绑定保留单元，旧绑定释放它。把一个百万元素的数组传给函数只保留一次。循环绑定迭代的是_存储的_元素，而不是它们的副本。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:31
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let mut p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };\n"
"    let q = p;          // q and p name ONE cell\n"
"    p.x = 4;            // q.x is 4 now — sharing is the law\n"
"    log.info(f\"q.x = {q.x}\");   // read through the other alias\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let mut p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };\n"
"    let q = p;          // q and p name ONE cell\n"
"    p.x = 4;            // q.x is 4 now — sharing is the law\n"
"    log.info(f\"q.x = {q.x}\");   // read through the other alias\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:49
msgid ""
"Mutation through an alias is visible through all of them, in both directions. What gates _writing_ is the `mut`\\-binding rule — a binding must be declared `mut` to be written through — never the sharing itself. Sharing is always safe: a handle keeps its referent alive, so nothing dangles, and there is no borrow checker because there are no loans."
msgstr ""
"经由别名做出的变更，会沿所有别名可见，双向皆然。真正把守_写入_的是 `mut`\\-绑定规则——绑定必须声明为 `mut` 才能通过它写入——而绝不是共享本身。共享始终安全：句柄会让其引用对象保活，因此没有任何东西悬空；没有借用检查器，因为根本不存在借用。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:55
msgid ""
"If you want a value that aliases nothing, you build one: a literal, a constructor, a copy of the fields you need. The language has exactly one copy escape hatch — `bytes.clone()`, a one-shot deep copy of a binary buffer, for interop hand-offs. There is no generic `clone`: a divergent value of any other type is unreachable by construction, which is what makes aliasing something you can reason about locally."
msgstr ""
"如果你想要一个不与任何东西别名的值，就亲手造一个：字面量、构造器，或者按需复制字段。这门语言恰好有一个复制逃生口——`bytes.clone()`，对二进制缓冲区做一次性深拷贝，服务于互操作交接。没有泛型 `clone`：任何其他类型的发散值在构造上都不可达，这正是别名可以被局部推理的原因。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:62
#: src/reference/builtin-generic-types.md:46
msgid "`?T` — the nullable"
msgstr "`?T` —— 可空类型"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:64
msgid ""
"Absence is `nil` on a nullable type, spelled as a prefix on the type: `?T` is \"a `T` or `nil`\". `?` applies to the type term that follows, so `[?T]` is an array of nullables while `?[T]` is a nullable array, and `??T` chains (and unwraps transitively at use)."
msgstr ""
"缺失即可空类型上的 `nil`，写作类型上的前缀：`?T` 是\"一个 `T` 或 `nil`\"。`?` 作用于其后的类型项，因此 `[?T]` 是可空数组——元素可空——而 `?[T]` 是可空数组本身，`??T` 则可链式叠加（并在使用时传递式解包）。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:69
msgid ""
"The coercions are one line: **`T → ?T` boxes; `?T → T` derefs.** The box is a fresh one-slot cell that _aliases_ the value's cell — boxing a record shares it, boxing a primitive copies its bits. The deref is implicit at every value position: field access, method calls, indexing, iteration, arithmetic all read through the box."
msgstr ""
"这些转换一行就能说清：**`T → ?T` 装盒；`?T → T` 解引用。**盒是一个全新的一槽单元，_别名_值所在的单元——装盒一个记录就是共享它，装盒一个原始类型则复制其比特位。解引用在每个值位置都是隐式的：字段访问、方法调用、索引、迭代、算术，全都透过盒读取。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:75
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct User { id: i64; name: str }\n"
"\n"
"fn lookup(id: i64) -> ?User {\n"
"    if (id == 7) { return User { id: 7, name: \"ada\" }; }\n"
"    return nil;             // a miss is nil, nothing else\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let u = lookup(7);                // ?User\n"
"    log.info(f\"u.name = {u.name}\");   // auto-deref when non-nil\n"
"    let missing = lookup(8);\n"
"    log.info(f\"miss is nil: {missing == nil}\");   // guard where absence is expected\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct User { id: i64; name: str }\n"
"\n"
"fn lookup(id: i64) -> ?User {\n"
"    if (id == 7) { return User { id: 7, name: \"ada\" }; }\n"
"    return nil;             // a miss is nil, nothing else\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let u = lookup(7);                // ?User\n"
"    log.info(f\"u.name = {u.name}\");   // auto-deref when non-nil\n"
"    let missing = lookup(8);\n"
"    log.info(f\"miss is nil: {missing == nil}\");   // guard where absence is expected\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:99
msgid ""
"A `nil` reaching a value use traps (`NilDeref`) — never a silent read. Guard with `u == nil` where absence is expected; the trap is the bug-catcher, not the semantics. A miss is `nil` and nothing else: a lookup that finds nothing returns `?V`, and callers compare against `nil`."
msgstr ""
"抵达值用途的 `nil` 会触发陷阱（`NilDeref`）——绝不会悄悄读出一个值。在预期可能缺失之处用 `u == nil` 设守卫；陷阱是抓 bug 的工具，而不是语义本身。未命中就是 `nil`，别无他物：找不到结果的查找返回 `?V`，调用方与 `nil` 比较。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:105
msgid "`==` is honest about the regime"
msgstr "`==` 对体制如实相告"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:107
msgid "Primitives compare **by value**."
msgstr "原始类型**按值**比较。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:108
msgid "`str` compares **by content** (codepoints); `bytes` by octets."
msgstr "`str` 按**内容**（码点）比较；`bytes` 按字节（octet）比较。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:109
msgid ""
"Everything else compares **by identity** — two bindings are equal exactly when they name the same cell."
msgstr "其余一切**按身份**比较——两个绑定相等，当且仅当它们指名同一个单元。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:112
msgid ""
"Identity is the only equality full sharing can defend: two separately built `[1, 2]` arrays are two cells, so `[1,2] == [1,2]` is `false`. Content comparison is a loop over fields, written where content is the contract. The one place identity quietly behaves like value equality: enum variants are immortal singletons, so `Flavor.Sour == Flavor.Sour` is `true`."
msgstr ""
"身份是完全共享唯一能捍卫的相等：两个分别构建的 `[1, 2]` 数组是两个单元，因此 `[1,2] == [1,2]` 是 `false`。内容比较是一个遍历字段的循环，写在内容才是契约的地方。身份唯一一处悄悄表现得像值相等的地方：枚举成员是不朽的单例，所以 `Flavor.Sour == Flavor.Sour` 是 `true`。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:119
msgid "The answer channel: a pair"
msgstr "应答通道：对偶"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:121
msgid ""
"There is no exception type and no `Result` monad. Failures are data in the second element of a record — `(value, err)` — with one documented convention:"
msgstr "没有异常类型，也没有 `Result` 单子。失败是对偶——`(value, err)`——第二个元素里的数据，配一条成文的约定："


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:125
msgid "an **empty err plus a value** is success;"
msgstr "**err 为空且带值**即成功；"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:126
msgid "an **empty err plus `nil`** means \"not found\";"
msgstr "**err 为空且为 `nil`** 意为\"未找到\"；"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:127
msgid "a **non-empty err** means \"failed\"."
msgstr "**err 非空**即为\"失败\"。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:129
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn parse_hex(s: str) -> (bytes, str) {\n"
"    if (s.len() % 2 != 0) {\n"
"        return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: odd-length input\");\n"
"    }\n"
"    let n = s.len() / 2;\n"
"    let mut buf: [u8] = [0u8; n];\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < n; i += 1) {\n"
"        let hi = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2));\n"
"        let lo = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2 + 1));\n"
"        if (hi < 0 || lo < 0) {\n"
"            return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: not a digit\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        buf[i] = ((hi * 16) + lo) as u8;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return (bytes.from(buf), \"\");       // (data, \"\") on success\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn hex_digit(c: u32) -> i64 {\n"
"    if (c >= 48 && c <= 57) { return (c - 48) as i64; }   // '0'..'9'\n"
"    if (c >= 97 && c <= 102) { return (c - 87) as i64; }  // 'a'..'f'\n"
"    return -1;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"4869\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); return; }   // propagate\n"
"    log.info(f\"ok: {raw.decode()} ({raw.len()} bytes)\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"486\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); }           // the failure channel\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn parse_hex(s: str) -> (bytes, str) {\n"
"    if (s.len() % 2 != 0) {\n"
"        return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: odd-length input\");\n"
"    }\n"
"    let n = s.len() / 2;\n"
"    let mut buf: [u8] = [0u8; n];\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < n; i += 1) {\n"
"        let hi = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2));\n"
"        let lo = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2 + 1));\n"
"        if (hi < 0 || lo < 0) {\n"
"            return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: not a digit\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        buf[i] = ((hi * 16) + lo) as u8;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return (bytes.from(buf), \"\");       // (data, \"\") on success\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn hex_digit(c: u32) -> i64 {\n"
"    if (c >= 48 && c <= 57) { return (c - 48) as i64; }   // '0'..'9'\n"
"    if (c >= 97 && c <= 102) { return (c - 87) as i64; }  // 'a'..'f'\n"
"    return -1;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"4869\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); return; }   // propagate\n"
"    log.info(f\"ok: {raw.decode()} ({raw.len()} bytes)\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"486\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); }           // the failure channel\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:170
msgid ""
"The pair destructure in return position is free — the compiler fuses the mint away — so this shape costs nothing on hot paths. At the host boundary the same pair crosses field by field, which makes `entry fn -> (?T, err)` the standard answer a Rust embedder reads."
msgstr ""
"返回位置的对偶解构是免费的——编译器会把铸造融合掉——所以这种形状在热路径上分文不费。在宿主边界，同一个对偶逐字段跨越，这让 `entry fn -> (?T, err)` 成为 Rust 嵌入方一眼即懂的标准应答。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:175
msgid "Consequences you feel day to day"
msgstr "日常能感受到的后果"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:177
msgid ""
"**Reassignment is cheap.** Moving containers around — returning them, storing them, restructuring them — is handle traffic, not payload traffic. Algorithms that churn records and arrays pay aliasing, not copying."
msgstr "**重新赋值很便宜。**把容器搬来搬去——返回、存储、重组——是句柄流量，不是载荷流量。大量周转记录与数组的算法付出的是别名代价，而不是复制代价。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:181
msgid ""
"**Loop variables are fresh per iteration but share elements.** A `for (let x of xs)` loop hands you the stored element; writes through it mutate the sequence. Each iteration is a fresh _binding_."
msgstr ""
"**循环变量每轮都是新的，但共享元素。**`for (let x of xs)` 循环交给你的是存储的元素；通过它写入会改变序列本身。每一轮都是一个全新的_绑定_。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:184
msgid ""
"**Containers of primitives stay flat.** A fixed `[i32]` is a packed `i32` buffer; growable sequences of primitives store raw payloads with a one-byte nil tag — no per-element heap box."
msgstr ""
"**原始类型容器保持扁平。**定长 `[i32]` 就是一块打包的 `i32` 缓冲区；可增长的原始类型序列直接存储裸载荷，外加一个字节的 nil 标签——没有逐元素的堆盒。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:187
msgid ""
"**Erasure is a box.** `opaque(v)` mints an erasure box; recovery is `opaque.downcast<T>(o)`, checked against the runtime type. See [reified types](reified-types.md) and the reference on [`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md)."
msgstr ""
"**擦除是一个盒。**`opaque(v)` 铸造一个擦除盒；恢复靠 `opaque.downcast<T>(o)`，对照运行时类型检查。参见[具体化类型](reified-types.md)以及关于 [`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md) 的参考章节。"


#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:192
msgid ""
"The memory machinery under all of this — refcounts, deterministic destructors, weak references — is the next chapter's subject: [memory](memory.md). The exact rules live in the reference on [by-reference and nullable](../reference/by-reference-and-nullable.md)."
msgstr ""
"这一切底下的内存机制——引用计数、确定性析构、弱引用——是下一章的主题：[内存](memory.md)。精确规则见关于[按引用与可空](../reference/by-reference-and-nullable.md)的参考章节。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:3
msgid ""
"Types in rut are not a compile-time fiction. Every value's exact type is available at runtime — generics included: a `Cache<i32>` and a `Cache<str>` are _different types_ to the VM, with distinct identities and distinct method sets. This chapter explains where that reified reality lives, what it is used for, and how values are actually laid out."
msgstr ""
"rut 的类型不是编译期的虚构。每个值的确切类型在运行时可得——泛型也包括在内：对 VM 而言，`Cache<i32>` 和 `Cache<str>` 是_不同的类型_，有各自独立的身份和各自的方法集。本章讲清这种具体化的实在存于何处、用来做什么，以及值究竟是如何布局的。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:10
msgid "The mental model"
msgstr "心智模型"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:12
msgid ""
"Think of the VM as keeping a **type table**: one descriptor per instantiated type — its kind, its field list, its trait impls, and for composites the method tables its instances point at. Every heap cell's header names an entry in that table. A value never \"forgets\" its type, because its type is one field read away."
msgstr ""
"把 VM 想成在维护一张**类型表**：每个实例化的类型一个描述符——它的类别、字段列表、trait impl，复合类型还有其实例指向的方法表。每个堆单元的头部都指名该表中的一个条目。值绝不会\"忘记\"自己的类型，因为读一个字段就能拿到它。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:18
msgid ""
"Types themselves are not first-class script values — you cannot put a type in a variable or write a function over types. What you get is the language-facing _surfaces_ of reification:"
msgstr "类型本身不是一等公民的脚本值——你不能把类型放进变量，也不能写以类型为对象的函数。你能得到的，是具体化面向语言的几个_表面_："


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:22
msgid ""
"**`is` type tests** — `x is Circle` (exact) and `x is Drawable` (capability: does this value's type have a registered impl?)."
msgstr "**`is` 类型测试**——`x is Circle`（确切类型）与 `x is Drawable`（能力：这个值的类型是否注册了 impl？）。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:24
msgid ""
"**Checked erasure** — `opaque.downcast<T>(o)` reads the box's runtime type and recovers the payload, or `nil` on a mismatch."
msgstr "**受检擦除**——`opaque.downcast<T>(o)` 读取盒的运行时类型并取回载荷，不匹配则得到 `nil`。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:26
msgid ""
"**Host-boundary checks** — native functions declare parameter types once; every call is checked against them."
msgstr "**宿主边界检查**——原生函数一次性声明参数类型；每次调用都对照检查。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:28
msgid ""
"**Debugging and traces** — error messages, backtraces, and formatter output name real runtime types."
msgstr "**调试与追踪**——错误信息、回溯与格式化输出都指名真实的运行时类型。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:31
msgid "Why reification is load-bearing"
msgstr "为什么具体化是承重墙"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:33
msgid ""
"The reason rut can check everything cheaply is that the runtime type is always reachable:"
msgstr "rut 能低成本检查一切，原因是运行时类型永远可达："


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:36
msgid ""
"**The host boundary needs no coercion code.** A native fn declares `(Opaque, str, str) -> nil` once; the VM checks each argument's runtime type at the crossing. There is no bridge-side \"re-parse-and-pray\" layer, because a wrong-shaped call fails loudly at the boundary."
msgstr ""
"**宿主边界不需要转换代码。**原生 fn 一次性声明 `(Opaque, str, str) -> nil`；VM 在跨越处检查每个实参的运行时类型。桥那一侧不存在\"重新解析然后祈祷\"的层，因为形状错误的调用会在边界响亮地失败。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:41
msgid ""
"**Erasure is checked, not blind.** `opaque(v)` stamps the box; `opaque.downcast<T>` consults the stamp. A box answers type tests _by the box_ — `o is T` misses for every payload type — so the only way back to the payload is the checked recovery. Erasure without reification would be `any`; with reification it is a sealed box."
msgstr ""
"**擦除是受检的，不是盲目的。**`opaque(v)` 给盒盖章；`opaque.downcast<T>` 查验印章。盒回答类型测试时_以盒为准_——对每个载荷类型 `o is T` 都不命中——所以回到载荷的唯一途径是受检恢复。没有具体化的擦除就是 `any`；有了具体化，它是一个密封的盒。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:46
msgid ""
"**Distinct instantiations.** `Vec<f32>` and `Vec<f64>` are different types everywhere — in the type table, in method resolution, at the host boundary. Nothing about a generic's type argument is erased."
msgstr ""
"**不同的实例化互不相同。**`Vec<f32>` 和 `Vec<f64>` 在任何地方都是不同的类型——类型表里、方法解析里、宿主边界上。泛型类型实参的任何信息都不会被擦除。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:49
msgid ""
"**Serialization and tooling.** Reflection walks the same descriptors, which is how userland JSON encoding is complete without annotations or macros on your types."
msgstr "**序列化与工具链。**反射遍历的正是同一批描述符，用户态的 JSON 编码因此无需在类型上加注解或宏就已然完备。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:53
msgid "Slots: the untagged hot path"
msgstr "槽位：无标签的热路径"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:55
msgid ""
"Inside the VM, registers and record fields are **untagged 8-byte slots**. The bytecode is typed — every register's static type is recorded in the function's signature and re-verified at load — so hot paths carry no type tags at all:"
msgstr ""
"在 VM 内部，寄存器和记录字段都是**无标签的 8 字节槽位**。字节码是类型化的——每个寄存器的静态类型都记录在函数签名中，并在加载时重新校验——所以热路径上完全不带类型标签："


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:63
msgid ""
"// ints, bool: the canonical scalar width\n"
msgstr ""
"// 整数、bool：规范的标量宽度\n"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:64
msgid ""
"// floats: f32 widened\n"
msgstr ""
"// 浮点数：f32 宽化\n"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:65
msgid ""
"// every non-primitive: a cell handle\n"
msgstr ""
"// 每个非原始类型：一个单元句柄\n"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:69
msgid ""
"A primitive is its bits; a composite is a handle to a cell. The tagged world — a value that carries its type with it — exists only at the host boundary, where Rust code that cannot trust static types receives checked, typed values."
msgstr ""
"原始类型就是它的比特位；复合类型是指向单元的句柄。带标签的世界——值随身携带自己的类型——只存在于宿主边界：那里运行的是无法信任静态类型的 Rust 代码，接收的是经过检查、带类型的值。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:74
msgid "Record layout: one slot per field"
msgstr "记录布局：每个字段一个槽位"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:76
msgid ""
"Both `struct` and `class` values live in a cell: a header (refcount + type id), a pointer to the type's vtable when the type has methods, and the payload — **a slot array, one untagged slot per field, in declaration order**."
msgstr ""
"`struct` 和 `class` 值都住在一个单元里：一个头部（引用计数 + 类型 id）、一个指向类型 vtable 的指针（当该类型有方法时），以及载荷——**一个槽数组，按声明顺序每字段一个无标签槽位**。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:81
msgid ""
"Primitive fields are widened into their slot; composite fields are cell handles."
msgstr "原始类型字段宽化后放入槽位；复合类型字段是单元句柄。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:83
msgid ""
"Visibility, generic parameters, and impl blocks elsewhere add _nothing_ — the payload depends only on the field list."
msgstr "可见性、泛型参数以及别处的 impl 块都_不_占分毫——载荷只取决于字段列表。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:85
msgid ""
"Field access is by index; there are no hidden members and no inheritance, so there is no base-class prefix and nothing to walk."
msgstr "字段访问按索引进行；没有隐藏成员，也没有继承，因此没有基类前缀，也无需遍历什么。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:87
msgid ""
"Fixed arrays of primitives (`[f32]`) keep their elements **flat and packed** at machine width — the one place values live inline. Growable sequences are rut-library classes over such arrays."
msgstr ""
"原始类型的定长数组（`[f32]`）让元素以机器宽度**扁平且紧实**地存放——这是值唯一内联存在的地方。可增长序列是 rut 库在这类数组之上实现的类。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:91
msgid "Consequences:"
msgstr "由此带来的后果："


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:93
msgid ""
"`size_of`/`align_of` do not exist, deliberately. Layout is an implementation detail, not an API — rut has no C-ABI struct surface for hosts to mirror. Hosts see records only through the checked boundary (see [the host boundary](host-boundary.md))."
msgstr ""
"`size_of`/`align_of` 被刻意省去。布局是实现细节，不是 API——rut 没有可供宿主镜像的 C-ABI 结构体表面。宿主只能透过受检边界看见记录（参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)）。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:97
msgid ""
"A record's memory cost is its field count times 8 bytes plus the cell header, which is exactly what the heap budget charges."
msgstr "一条记录的内存开销是字段数乘 8 字节再加单元头部，而这正是堆预算所计费的。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:99
msgid ""
"Widening a value to a trait type allocates nothing: the trait-typed value _is_ the same cell, reinterpreted through its vtable."
msgstr "把值宽化为 trait 类型不分配任何东西：trait 类型的值_就是_同一个单元，只是透过其 vtable 重新解释。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:102
msgid "Vtables: one per type, attached at construction"
msgstr "vtable：每个类型一张，构造时挂接"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:104
msgid ""
"A cell's vtable is filled when the value is constructed and never changes. It names the exact type and holds one entry per trait method the type implements, keyed by a global (trait instantiation, method) id — `Slice<Point>` and `Slice<str>` have separate slot sets, because they are separate trait instantiations."
msgstr ""
"单元的 vtable 在值构造时填好，此后不再改变。它指明确切类型，并为该类型实现的每个 trait 方法持有一个条目，以全局的（trait 实例化，方法）id 为键——`Slice<Point>` 和 `Slice<str>` 拥有各自独立的槽位集，因为它们是彼此独立的 trait 实例化。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:110
msgid "A call through a trait object is two loads and an indirect jump:"
msgstr "透过 trait 对象的调用是两次加载加一次间接跳转："


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:119
msgid ""
"An inherent method call — `c.area()` on a concrete `c` — compiles to a direct call with no table involved. The dispatch rules that choose between the two are the subject of the next chapter, [traits and dispatch](traits-and-dispatch.md)."
msgstr ""
"固有方法调用——在具体的 `c` 上调用 `c.area()`——编译为直接调用，不涉及任何表。在两者之间做出选择的分派规则是下一章的主题：[trait 与分派](traits-and-dispatch.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:124
msgid "Type tests, lowered"
msgstr "类型测试的下层形态"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:126
msgid "Every type test is a small, pure read:"
msgstr "每个类型测试都是一次小型、纯粹的读取："


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:128
msgid ""
"**Concrete test** (`d is Circle`): load the value's runtime type id, compare. When the receiver's static type already answers, the compiler folds it to a constant."
msgstr "**具体类型测试**（`d is Circle`）：加载值的运行时类型 id，比较。当接收者的静态类型已能作答时，编译器将其折叠为常量。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:131
msgid ""
"**Trait probe** (`x is Drawable`): load the type id, scan the descriptor's registered impl list. Pure in its inputs, so repeated probes deduplicate and invariant ones hoist."
msgstr ""
"**trait 探测**（`x is Drawable`）：加载类型 id，扫描描述符中已注册的 impl 列表。输入是纯的，因此重复的探测会去重，不变的探测会被外提。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:134
msgid ""
"**Downcast** (`opaque.downcast<T>(o)`): the same type-id compare, followed by the guarded payload extract."
msgstr "**向下转型**（`opaque.downcast<T>(o)`）：同样的类型 id 比较，随后是带守卫的载荷提取。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:137
msgid ""
"There is no `type_of(x)` returning a manipulable value and no runtime layout introspection — the descriptors serve the VM, the checks, and tooling, not userland metaprogramming. Reflection over data (walking fields to serialize) is a library facility built on the same tables; see the reference on [reflection](../reference/reflection.md)."
msgstr ""
"这里没有返回可操纵值的 `type_of(x)`，也没有运行时布局内省——描述符服务于 VM、各项检查与工具链，而不是用户态元编程。对数据做反射（遍历字段以序列化）是一个建立在同一批表之上的库设施；参见关于[反射](../reference/reflection.md)的参考章节。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:145
msgid ""
"Type errors are **runtime facts, not conventions**: a host call, a downcast, or a trait probe is checked against the same table the VM dispatches through."
msgstr "类型错误是**运行时事实，而不是约定**：宿主调用、向下转型或 trait 探测，对照的都是 VM 分派所用的同一张表。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:148
msgid ""
"**One runtime truth per value** — the vtable that answers dispatch is the same one that answers `is`."
msgstr "**每个值只有一份运行时事实**——回答分派的 vtable 与回答 `is` 的是同一张。"


#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:150
msgid ""
"The tag-free hot path keeps the interpreter's arithmetic and field traffic at raw slot speed while reification costs only what the program's dynamic features actually use."
msgstr "无标签的热路径让解释器的算术和字段流量保持裸槽位速度，而具体化只收程序动态特性真正用到的那部分费用。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:3
msgid ""
"A trait in rut is a **named contract**: a list of method signatures that a type can implement — by name, in an impl block. Satisfaction is nominal: the impl block is the admission, and nothing else. A type whose members happen to match a trait's shapes is _not_ an implementor; some module must say `impl I for T`."
msgstr ""
"rut 中的 trait 是一份**有名有姓的契约**：一列方法签名，类型可以按名实现——写进 impl 块。满足关系是名义上的：impl 块就是准入凭证，别无其他。成员碰巧长得像某个 trait 形状的类型_并不是_实现者；必须有某个模块写下 `impl I for T`。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:9
msgid "The shape of a trait"
msgstr "trait 的形状"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:11
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Point {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.x as f64; }\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64) { }    // the impl must list every trait method\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"traits\");\n"
"    let p = Point { x: 3, y: 4 };\n"
"    log.info(f\"area = {p.area()}\");     // a concrete receiver: static\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Point {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.x as f64; }\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64) { }    // the impl must list every trait method\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"traits\");\n"
"    let p = Point { x: 3, y: 4 };\n"
"    log.info(f\"area = {p.area()}\");     // a concrete receiver: static\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:37
msgid ""
"**Methods only, no bodies.** A trait declares signatures — no fields, no properties, and no default implementations, ever. One member kind means one dispatch candidate per call; a default body would be a second candidate with a resolution law of its own."
msgstr ""
"**只有方法，没有方法体。**trait 声明签名——没有字段，没有属性，也永远没有默认实现。成员只有一种，意味着每次调用只有一个分派候选；默认方法体会成为第二个候选，并自带一套独立的解析法则。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:41
msgid ""
"**Two impl forms.** `impl T { .. }` defines the type's _inherent_ methods and may live only in the module that declares `T`. `impl I for T { .. }` defines a trait implementation; its methods are exactly the trait's, with no `pub` (they are as visible as the trait)."
msgstr ""
"**两种 impl 形式。**`impl T { .. }` 定义类型的_固有_方法，且只能存在于声明 `T` 的模块里。`impl I for T { .. }` 定义一个 trait 实现；其方法与 trait 的完全一致，不带 `pub`（它们的可见性与 trait 相同）。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:45
msgid ""
"**One impl per pair, program-wide.** Two modules implementing the same trait for the same type is a link error that names both. The impl registry — merged when modules link — is the single source of truth for \"who implements what\"."
msgstr ""
"**每对组合全程序只有一个 impl。**两个模块为同一类型实现同一 trait 是一个链接错误，会同时点名双方。impl 注册表——在模块链接时合并——是\"谁实现了什么\"的唯一事实来源。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:49
msgid ""
"**Placement is pair-local.** A trait impl may live in the trait's package or the type's package — at least one side of every `(trait, type)` pair must be yours. Implementing two foreign types' pairing is rejected outright; there is no orphan rule beyond that."
msgstr ""
"**放置位置对组合局部。**trait impl 可以放在 trait 所在的包或类型所在的包——每个 `(trait, type)` 组合至少有一侧属于你自己。实现两个外部类型的组合会被直接拒绝；除此之外没有别的孤儿规则。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:53
msgid ""
"**Any nominal type can be a target** — classes, structs, and even primitives (`impl MyTrait for i32` registers like any other impl). Traits may be generic (`Wrap<T>`, `Iterator<E>`); each instantiation has its own identity and its own method slots, and an impl may be parameterized by the target's own type parameters — `impl Encode<T> for Store<T>` registers a template that serves every instantiation, unless a concrete impl shadows it."
msgstr ""
"**任何名义类型都可以作为目标**——类、结构体，甚至原始类型（`impl MyTrait for i32` 像其他 impl 一样注册）。trait 可以是泛型的（`Wrap<T>`、`Iterator<E>`）；每个实例化都有自己的身份和自己的方法槽位，而且 impl 可以由目标自身的类型参数参数化——`impl Encode<T> for Store<T>` 注册的是一个服务所有实例化的模板，除非某个具体 impl 将其遮蔽。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:61
msgid ""
"Type bodies are **fields only** — a `fn` inside a `struct` or `class` body is a parse error. Every method, inherent or trait, lives in an impl block."
msgstr ""
"类型体**只放字段**——`struct` 或 `class` 体内出现 `fn` 是解析错误。每个方法，无论固有还是 trait，都住在 impl 块里。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:65
msgid "Trait-typed values"
msgstr "trait 类型的值"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:67
msgid ""
"A trait name in type position is the bare name — there is no object-type keyword:"
msgstr "类型位置上的 trait 名就是裸名字——没有对象类型关键字："


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:70
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Circle { r: f64 }\n"
"struct UnitSquare { side: f64 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Circle {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return 3.14159265358979 * self.r * self.r; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for UnitSquare {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.side * self.side; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Canvas { log: Logger }\n"
"\n"
"impl Canvas {\n"
"    fn render(self, a: f64) { self.log.info(f\"blitted a shape of area {a}\"); }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn blit(g: Canvas, s: Shape) { g.render(s.area()); }   // a parameter over any Shape\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"shapes\");\n"
"    let g = Canvas { log: log };\n"
"    let mut mixed: Vec<Shape> = Vec.new();   // heterogeneous storage\n"
"    mixed.push(Circle { r: 1.0 });\n"
"    mixed.push(UnitSquare { side: 2.0 });\n"
"    for (let s of mixed) { blit(g, s); }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Circle { r: f64 }\n"
"struct UnitSquare { side: f64 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Circle {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return 3.14159265358979 * self.r * self.r; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for UnitSquare {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.side * self.side; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Canvas { log: Logger }\n"
"\n"
"impl Canvas {\n"
"    fn render(self, a: f64) { self.log.info(f\"blitted a shape of area {a}\"); }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn blit(g: Canvas, s: Shape) { g.render(s.area()); }   // a parameter over any Shape\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"shapes\");\n"
"    let g = Canvas { log: log };\n"
"    let mut mixed: Vec<Shape> = Vec.new();   // heterogeneous storage\n"
"    mixed.push(Circle { r: 1.0 });\n"
"    mixed.push(UnitSquare { side: 2.0 });\n"
"    for (let s of mixed) { blit(g, s); }\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:112
msgid ""
"A trait-typed value is a reference to a real cell that still carries its exact class. Widening a concrete value to a trait it implements is implicit on assignment and argument passing, allocates nothing, and is gated by exactly one question: does the registry hold an `impl I for T`? There is no top type to widen to, and intersection types (`A & B`) are ruled out by design — when you need both contracts, declare a trait that spells both."
msgstr ""
"trait 类型的值是指向真实单元的引用，而且仍携带其确切的类。把具体值宽化到它实现的某个 trait，在赋值和传参时隐式发生，不分配任何东西，只受一个问题把守：注册表里有没有 `impl I for T`？没有可宽化的顶类型，交集类型（`A & B`）也被设计排除——当你同时需要两份契约时，就声明一个把两者都写明的 trait。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:120
msgid "Dispatch: the two-rule law"
msgstr "分派：两条规则的法则"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:122
msgid ""
"Every method call compiles under one of exactly two rules, fixed at compile time as a property of the _call site_:"
msgstr "每个方法调用都恰好按两条规则之一编译，编译期即固定，是_调用点_的属性："


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:125
msgid ""
"**Static** — the call site names exactly one concrete type. The call binds directly to that type's method, no table involved:"
msgstr "**静态**——调用点指名恰好一个具体类型。调用直接绑定到该类型的方法，不涉及任何表："


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:127
msgid "a concrete receiver (`c.area()` on `c: Circle`);"
msgstr "具体接收者（`c: Circle` 上的 `c.area()`）；"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:128
msgid ""
"a trait-typed local whose single concrete origin the compiler tracked (`let d: Shape = Point { .. }; d.area()`);"
msgstr "编译器跟踪到唯一具体来源的 trait 类型局部变量（`let d: Shape = Point { .. }; d.area()`）；"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:130
msgid ""
"a trait-typed _parameter_ — the function specializes per concrete argument at monomorphization, so a trait parameter is effectively an implicit generic bound;"
msgstr "trait 类型的_参数_——函数在单态化时按具体实参特化，所以 trait 参数实际上是一个隐式的泛型约束；"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:133
msgid "inside monomorphized generics."
msgstr "单态化的泛型内部。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:134
msgid ""
"**Vtable** — the receiver is trait-typed with multiple possible concrete origins:"
msgstr "**vtable**——接收者是 trait 类型，且可能有多个具体来源："


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:136
msgid "elements of a heterogeneous container (`Vec<Shape>`);"
msgstr "异构容器的元素（`Vec<Shape>`）；"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:137
msgid "trait-typed field and element loads (the cell may hold any implementor);"
msgstr "trait 类型的字段与元素加载（单元里可能装着任何实现者）；"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:139
msgid ""
"branch-merged bindings (`if` arms carrying different concretes into one trait-typed variable)."
msgstr "分支合并的绑定（`if` 各分支把不同的具体类型汇入同一个 trait 类型变量）。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:142
msgid ""
"The origin analysis is conservative: any merge, indirection, or cross-function flow counts as multiple. Mis-analysis cannot produce wrong code — an uncertain origin costs one vtable hop, never a wrong static bind. And the same descriptor that answers vtable calls answers `is` probes: one runtime truth per value."
msgstr ""
"来源分析是保守的：任何合并、间接或跨函数流动都按\"多个\"计。误判不会产生错误代码——来源不确定的代价只是一次 vtable 跳转，绝不会错误地静态绑定。而回答 vtable 调用的描述符同样回答 `is` 探测：每个值只有一份运行时事实。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:148
msgid "Type tests"
msgstr "类型测试"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:150
msgid ""
"`expr is Type` yields a `bool` and is total — it never traps. Two probes, one keyword:"
msgstr "`expr is Type` 产出 `bool` 且是全函数——它从不触发陷阱。两个探测，一个关键字："


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:153
msgid ""
"**Concrete RHS**: is the value's exact type `T`? (No inheritance — a single id compare.)"
msgstr "**具体类型右侧**：值的确切类型是不是 `T`？（没有继承——一次单独的 id 比较。）"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:155
msgid ""
"**Trait RHS**: does the value's exact type have a registered impl? A capability probe, usable on any value (`k is Hashable`)."
msgstr "**trait 右侧**：值的确切类型有没有注册 impl？这是一次能力探测，可用于任何值（`k is Hashable`）。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:158
msgid ""
"`is` has no flow-sensitive effects: a true probe does not narrow `x`. When the static type already answers, the probe folds at compile time. Trait-typed values cannot be downcast to a concrete type at all — if you need `Circle`\\-specific behavior behind a `Drawable`, put that behavior in the trait. The one recovery path for erased values is the explicit `opaque` box (see the reference on [`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md))."
msgstr ""
"`is` 没有流敏感效应：探测为真不会收窄 `x`。当静态类型已能作答时，探测在编译期折叠。trait 类型的值完全不能向下转型到具体类型——如果你需要在 `Drawable` 背后做 `Circle`\\-特定的行为，就把那个行为放进 trait。被擦除的值唯一的恢复路径是显式的 `opaque` 盒（见关于 [`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md) 的参考章节）。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:166
msgid "Visibility: the use-both gate"
msgstr "可见性：use 双侧闸门"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:168
msgid ""
"Calling a trait method requires **both** names in scope: the type (by declaration or `use`) _and_ the trait (`use`). Inherent methods need only the type. A call that matches a registered impl whose trait no `use` brings in is an error — \"use `I` to call its methods on `T`\" — so an added trait method can never silently change what someone else's call site means."
msgstr ""
"调用 trait 方法要求**两个**名字都在作用域内：类型（靠声明或 `use`）_以及_ trait（靠 `use`）。固有方法只要类型在即可。如果一次调用匹配到某个已注册 impl，但其 trait 没有被任何 `use` 引入，就是错误——\"use `I` 才能在 `T` 上调用它的方法\"——因此新增一个 trait 方法永远不可能悄悄改变别人调用点的含义。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:175 src/reference/traits.md:167
msgid "The iteration protocol"
msgstr "迭代协议"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:177
msgid ""
"A type is iterable when it implements the builtin `Iterator<E>` trait (a `pub builtin` core name — an `impl` block names it, so the module imports it, `use core::{ Iterator }`):"
msgstr ""
"一个类型实现了内置的 `Iterator<E>` trait 时即可迭代（`Iterator` 是 core 的 `pub builtin` 名字——`impl` 块点名它，因此模块要导入它，`use core::{ Iterator }`）："


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:181
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use core::{ Iterator };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class CountUp {\n"
"    n: i32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Iterator<i32> for CountUp {\n"
"    fn __iterate(self, emit: fn(i32) -> bool) {\n"
"        for (let i = 1; i <= self.n; i += 1) {\n"
"            if (!emit(i)) { return; }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"iter\");\n"
"    for (let v of CountUp { n: 3 }) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"tick {v}\");\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(\"done\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rutuse core::{ Iterator };use ink::{ Logger };class CountUp {    n: i32;}impl Iterator<i32> for CountUp {    fn __iterate(self, emit: fn(i32) -> bool) {        for (let i = 1; i <= self.n; i += 1) {            if (!emit(i)) { return; }        }    }}pub fn main() {    let log = Logger.new(\"iter\");    for (let v of CountUp { n: 3 }) {        log.info(f\"tick {v}\");    }    log.info(\"done\");}```"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:213
msgid ""
"`for (let v of it) { body }` desugars to `it.__iterate(emit)` with a synthetic closure: the body runs, then `emit` returns `true`; `break` returns `false`. The loop variable is the closure's parameter — a fresh binding per iteration by construction. The builtin sequences (`[T]`, `str`, `bytes`, and the standard growable `Vec`) keep fused index loops instead; they never pay a per-element call."
msgstr ""
"`for (let v of it) { body }` 会脱糖为带合成闭包的 `it.__iterate(emit)`：先跑循环体，然后 `emit` 返回 `true`；`break` 则返回 `false`。循环变量是闭包的参数——按构造每轮迭代都是全新绑定。内置序列（`[T]`、`str`、`bytes` 以及标准的可增长 `Vec`）则保留融合的索引循环；它们从不为每个元素付一次调用。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:220
msgid "Engine contracts are traits too"
msgstr "引擎契约也是 trait"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:222
msgid ""
"The async machinery is spelled as builtin traits — `Future<T>` and `RunContext` — which the engine _names_ but does not close: a hand-written type can `impl Future<nil> for MyFuture` through the same registry as any other impl and be driven by the same loop. Like `Iterator`, both are `pub builtin` core names: the engine's weave never needs the import, but source that spells the names does (`use core::{ Future, RunContext }`). See [the async model](async-model.md) and the worked example in [04 — Custom async](../examples/04-custom-async.md)."
msgstr ""
"异步机制拼写成内置 trait——`Future<T>` 与 `RunContext`——引擎_点名_它们但不对它们封闭：手写类型可以像任何其他 impl 一样，经同一个注册表 `impl Future<nil> for MyFuture`，并由同一个循环驱动。与 `Iterator` 一样，两者都是 `pub builtin` 的 core 名字：引擎的织造从不需要导入，而拼写了名字的源码需要（`use core::{ Future, RunContext }`）。参见[异步模型](async-model.md)与 [04 — 自定义异步](../examples/04-custom-async.md)中的完整示例。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:232
msgid "Equality is not a trait"
msgstr "相等不是 trait"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:234
msgid ""
"`==` is builtin and cannot be opted into or out of: primitives compare by value, `str`/`bytes` by content, everything else by cell identity. Field-wise comparison is a loop you write, or the map packages' own key rules. See [everything is a value](everything-is-a-value.md)."
msgstr ""
"`==` 是内置的，不能选择加入或退出：原始类型按值比较，`str`/`bytes` 按内容，其余一切按单元身份。逐字段比较是你自己写的循环，或者 map 包自带的键规则。参见[一切皆值](everything-is-a-value.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:241
msgid ""
"**Nominal satisfaction** keeps the registry exact: capability probes, widening, and vtable fills all read one table, so casts stay cheap and runtime identities stay meaningful."
msgstr "**名义满足**让注册表保持精确：能力探测、宽化、vtable 填充读取的都是同一张表，因此转型保持廉价，运行时身份保持有意义。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:244
msgid ""
"**The two-rule law** makes dispatch predictable: you can tell, per call site, whether you are paying a hop."
msgstr "**两条规则的法则**让分派可预测：对每个调用点，你都能说出自己是否在付一次跳转的钱。"


#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:246
msgid ""
"**Placement rules** keep coherence decidable across packages without a global uniqueness proof — one of the pair is always local."
msgstr "**放置规则**让跨包的连贯性可判定，无需全局唯一性证明——组合中总有一侧是本地的。"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:3
msgid ""
"rut's concurrency is **pull-based**, built on one noun: `Future<T>`. Calling an `async fn` runs nothing — it produces a cold future. The future runs when something _drives_ it: an `await` inside another async fn, or a launch into the VM's queue. There are no promises, no microtask queue, and no implicit scheduling: **the host owns time**, and nothing runs unless the driving loop runs it."
msgstr ""
"rut 的并发是**拉取式**的，建立在一个名词之上：`Future<T>`。调用 `async fn` 什么也不运行——它产出一个冷 future。future 在有什么东西_驱动_它时才运行：另一个 async fn 里的 `await`，或一次进入 VM 队列的启动。没有 promise，没有微任务队列，没有隐式调度：**时间归宿主所有**，驱动循环不运行它，它就不运行。"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:10
msgid "Pull, not push"
msgstr "拉取，而非推送"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:12
msgid "push (promises)"
msgstr "推（promise）"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:12
msgid "pull (rut futures)"
msgstr "拉（rut future）"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:14 src/reference/async.md:12
msgid "created"
msgstr "创建时机"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:14
msgid "starts on the next microtask"
msgstr "在下一个微任务启动"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:14
msgid "cold — nothing runs until awaited or launched"
msgstr "冷——被 await 或被启动之前什么都不运行"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:15
msgid "idle cost"
