#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:153
msgid ""
"`Completer<T>` is a small shared cell: `complete(v)`/`fail(msg)` are callable from any thread (atomics plus a mutex — the VM stays single-threaded), `fail`'s message becomes the trap **at the await**, and an optional abort closure runs when the script cancels a pending future (late results are then simply discarded). The macro registers the whole row family the weave drives — start, probe, take, cancel — and the load-time check verifies the expansion against the declaration, so a decl and its bodies cannot drift apart. IO written with plain `async`/`await` Rust maps onto this naturally: the work leaves the VM, and completion is one enqueue back into the ready queue."
msgstr ""
"`Completer<T>` 是一个小的共享单元：`complete(v)`/`fail(msg)` 可从任意线程调用（原子操作加互斥锁——VM 保持单线程），`fail` 的消息**在 await 处**变成陷阱；当脚本取消一个挂起的 future 时，可选的中止闭包会运行（迟到的结果随后被直接丢弃）。这个宏注册织造所驱动的整行族——start、probe、take、cancel——加载期检查则对照声明校验展开结果，声明与函数体因此不可能漂移分离。用普通 `async`/`await` Rust 写的 IO 自然映射到此：工作离开 VM，完成就是一次重新入队，回到就绪队列。"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:164
msgid "Structured concurrency, honestly"
msgstr "结构化并发，如实相告"


#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:166
msgid ""
"The language today keeps the vocabulary deliberately small: launch, abort, and await. Racing (`await select { .. }`) and joining a launched future (`await handle`) parse but are compile-gated — the diagnostics name them as future work, and structured scopes (a block that cancels its children on exit) are the same story. What exists now is already enough to structure real programs — the launch/abort receipt gives you explicit ownership of background work, and drop-based cancellation gives it a clean off switch — but nothing in the model silently cancels siblings on your behalf. See the reference on [async and await](../reference/async.md), [tasks](../reference/tasks.md), and the [host futures bridge](../reference/host-futures.md); the [GitHub viewer CLI](../examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md) example shows a full program living inside this loop."
msgstr ""
"这门语言今天刻意保持很小的词汇表：launch、abort 和 await。竞速（`await select { .. }`）与 join 已启动的 future（`await handle`）能解析但被编译期闸住——诊断把它们标为未来工作，结构化作用域（一个在退出时取消其子任务的块）也是同样的情况。现有机制已足以组织真实的程序——launch/abort 回执让你对后台工作拥有显式所有权，基于 drop 的取消给了它一个干净的开关——但模型中没有任何东西会替你悄悄取消兄弟任务。参见关于[异步与 await](../reference/async.md)、[任务](../reference/tasks.md)与[宿主 future 桥](../reference/host-futures.md)的参考章节；[GitHub 查看器 CLI](../examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md) 示例展示了一个完整程序如何活在这个循环里。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:3
msgid ""
"rut's memory management is **reference counting with deterministic destructors and no collector**. An object is destroyed the moment its last strong reference goes away — at a knowable statement, not \"at some future GC\". The cost is honesty about cycles: a strong cycle never reaches zero, so it lives until the VM is torn down. rut makes that a stated rule and ships `Weak<T>` as the first-class answer, instead of hiding it behind a collector."
msgstr ""
"rut 的内存管理是**引用计数加确定性析构器，没有收集器**。对象在最后一个强引用消失的那一刻被销毁——落在一条可知的语句上，而不是\"将来某次 GC\"。代价是对循环引用的如实相告：强循环引用永远不会减到零，因此它活到 VM 被拆毁为止。rut 把这一点写成明文规则，并把 `Weak<T>` 作为一等公民的答案交付，而不是把它藏在收集器背后。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:11
msgid "Everything is a cell"
msgstr "一切皆单元"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:13
msgid ""
"Every non-primitive value — strings, byte buffers, arrays, records, enums, trait objects, erasure boxes, nullable boxes, coroutine frames — is a heap cell. Each cell starts with a header: a refcount, a type id, and a few flags. The counts are plain integers: a VM runs on one thread with one heap, workers are separate VMs, and nothing is ever shared between them, so there are no atomics anywhere in the heap."
msgstr ""
"每个非原始类型的值——字符串、字节缓冲、数组、记录、枚举、trait 对象、擦除盒、可空盒、协程帧——都是一个堆单元。每个单元以一个头部开始：引用计数、类型 id 和几个标志位。计数就是普通整数：一个 VM 运行在一个线程上、拥有一套堆，worker 是彼此独立的 VM，两者之间永不共享任何东西，所以整个堆中没有任何原子操作。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:20
msgid ""
"Because assignments and passes copy _handles_, not payloads, the refcount traffic is exactly the aliasing the program performs:"
msgstr "由于赋值与传参复制的是_句柄_而非载荷，引用计数的流量恰好就是程序实施的别名数量："


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:23
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Node { next: ?Node }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"cells\");\n"
"    let a: ?Node = Node { next: nil };\n"
"    let b = a;              // one retain\n"
"    log.info(f\"a == b: {a == b}\");   // one cell — it dies when the LAST of a, b goes away\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Node { next: ?Node }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"cells\");\n"
"    let a: ?Node = Node { next: nil };\n"
"    let b = a;              // one retain\n"
"    log.info(f\"a == b: {a == b}\");   // one cell — it dies when the LAST of a, b goes away\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:40
msgid ""
"The compiler knows every register's static type, so it emits ref-aware moves only where references flow; scalar code pays nothing. Function boundaries do the paired inc/dec; a flat primitive buffer's element traffic is plain slot moves."
msgstr ""
"编译器知道每个寄存器的静态类型，因此只在引用流动之处生成引用感知的移动；标量代码分文不费。函数边界完成成对的增/减；扁平原始类型缓冲区的元素流量就是普通的槽位移动。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:45
msgid "Deterministic destruction"
msgstr "确定性析构"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:47
msgid "When a count reaches zero, destruction runs in a fixed order:"
msgstr "计数归零时，析构按固定顺序运行："


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:49
msgid ""
"**Weak boxes null first, then `dispose`.** A type implementing the `Disposal` trait gets its `dispose(mut self, cx: DisposalContext)` called — the engine pins the dying cell, queues the call, and the interpreter drains the queue at call boundaries. One impl per type; `use core::{ Disposal, DisposalContext }` brings the pair in. Fields release after the body returns."
msgstr ""
"**弱盒先置空，然后 `dispose`。**实现了 `Disposal` trait 的类型，其 `dispose(mut self, cx: DisposalContext)` 会被调用——引擎钉住垂死的单元，把调用排入队列，解释器在调用边界排空队列。每个类型一个 impl；`use core::{ Disposal, DisposalContext }` 把这一对带入作用域。字段在函数体返回之后释放。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:55
msgid ""
"**Fields release in declaration order**, recursively — a dying record's strings, arrays, and boxes release their own references, so nothing is pinned until VM shutdown just because its owner died."
msgstr "**字段按声明顺序释放**，递归进行——垂死记录的字符串、数组和盒各自释放自己的引用，因此不会有什么仅仅因为其主人死亡就被钉到 VM 关机。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:58
msgid ""
"**Host opaques run their Rust `Drop` at the same point.** A host handle registered by the embedder releases its socket, texture, or thread when the last script reference disappears — never \"someday at GC\" (see [the host boundary](host-boundary.md))."
msgstr ""
"**宿主 opaque 在同一时点运行它们的 Rust `Drop`。**嵌入方注册的宿主句柄在最后一个脚本引用消失时释放它的套接字、纹理或线程——绝不是\"GC 某天\"（参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)）。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:63
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use core::{ Disposal, DisposalContext };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Connection {\n"
"    url: str;\n"
"    log: Logger;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Connection {\n"
"    fn open(url: str, log: Logger) -> Connection {\n"
"        return Connection { url: url, log: log };\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Disposal for Connection {\n"
"    fn dispose(mut self, cx: DisposalContext) {\n"
"        self.log.info(f\"closed {self.url}\");\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let conn = Connection.open(\"tcp://edge\", log);\n"
"    log.info(\"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use core::{ Disposal, DisposalContext };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Connection {\n"
"    url: str;\n"
"    log: Logger;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Connection {\n"
"    fn open(url: str, log: Logger) -> Connection {\n"
"        return Connection { url: url, log: log };\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Disposal for Connection {\n"
"    fn dispose(mut self, cx: DisposalContext) {\n"
"        self.log.info(f\"closed {self.url}\");\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let conn = Connection.open(\"tcp://edge\", log);\n"
"    log.info(\"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:91
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\n"
"closed tcp://edge\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\n"
"closed tcp://edge\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:96
msgid ""
"Compare this with finalizer-based designs: there is no finalizer that \"may run later or never\", no flush phase, and no resource whose release time you cannot point at in your own code."
msgstr ""
"与基于 finalizer 的设计比较一下：没有\"可能晚点运行或永远不运行\"的 finalizer，没有冲刷阶段，也没有任何释放时间在你自己的代码里指不出来对的资源。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:100
msgid "Two edge rules worth knowing:"
msgstr "两条值得知道的边界规则："


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:102
msgid ""
"**Refcount overflow pins.** If a counter would exceed its maximum, the object is deliberately immortalized (and logged) rather than wrapping — the same rule Swift uses."
msgstr "**引用计数溢出即钉死。**如果某个计数器即将超过最大值，对象会被刻意永生化（并记入日志），而不是回绕——Swift 用的也是同一条规则。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:105
msgid ""
"**Weak boxes null first.** When a cell with weak watchers dies, every `Weak` box to it is nulled _before_ any user code runs — a dispose body that calls `upgrade()` sees `nil`, deterministically."
msgstr ""
"**弱盒先置空。**当一个带有弱观察者的单元死亡时，指向它的每个 `Weak` 盒都会在任何用户代码运行_之前_被置空——调用 `upgrade()` 的 dispose 函数体确定性地看到 `nil`。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:109 src/reference/rc-dispose-identity.md:87
msgid "Weak references"
msgstr "弱引用"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:111
msgid ""
"`Weak.new(v)` mints a `Weak<T>` over `v`'s cell that **never keeps anything alive**; `w.upgrade()` answers `?T` — the retained referent, or `nil` once it died. Construction is the class-method form, admission is checked (reference types only — `Weak<i32>` diagnoses), and `Weak.new(nil)` traps."
msgstr ""
"`Weak.new(v)` 在 `v` 的单元上构造一个 `Weak<T>`，它**永远不让任何东西保活**；`w.upgrade()` 回答 `?T`——被保留的引用对象，或它死掉之后的 `nil`。构造是类方法形式，准入受检查（仅限引用类型——`Weak<i32>` 会被诊断），`Weak.new(nil)` 触发陷阱。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:117
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Model {\n"
"    name: str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"class View {\n"
"    model: ?Model;\n"
"    observer: ?Weak<Model>;      // a back-pointer that closes no cycle\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let mut m = Model { name: \"doc\" };\n"
"    let v = View { model: nil, observer: Weak.new(m) };   // observe without owning\n"
"    log.info(f\"holding {m.name}; the view holds only a weak edge\");\n"
"    m = Model { name: \"next\" };   // the old cell's last strong reference dies here\n"
"    log.info(f\"upgrade() answers nil: {v.observer.upgrade() == nil}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Model {\n"
"    name: str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"class View {\n"
"    model: ?Model;\n"
"    observer: ?Weak<Model>;      // a back-pointer that closes no cycle\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let mut m = Model { name: \"doc\" };\n"
"    let v = View { model: nil, observer: Weak.new(m) };   // observe without owning\n"
"    log.info(f\"holding {m.name}; the view holds only a weak edge\");\n"
"    m = Model { name: \"next\" };   // the old cell's last strong reference dies here\n"
"    log.info(f\"upgrade() answers nil: {v.observer.upgrade() == nil}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:144
msgid ""
"The two shapes that cause accidental cycles — **back-pointers** (child → parent) and **caches** (a table that should not extend lifetimes) — are exactly what `Weak` is for. A path through a `Weak` does not close a strong cycle."
msgstr ""
"造成意外循环引用的两种形状——**回指指针**（child → parent）与**缓存**（不该延长生命周期的表）——恰好就是 `Weak` 的用武之地。经过 `Weak` 的路径不会闭合强循环引用。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:149
msgid "The cycle policy"
msgstr "循环引用策略"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:151
msgid ""
"**A strong cycle is a leak — deterministically.** Its members live until the VM is dropped; no collector ever runs, no pass interrupts execution, and destructor ordering never surprises you. Guidance is lint-level, not runtime:"
msgstr ""
"**强循环引用就是泄漏——确定性的泄漏。**它的成员活到 VM 被 drop 为止；收集器从不运行，没有任何阶段会打断执行，析构顺序也从不让你意外。指导是 lint 级的，不是运行时的："


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:156
msgid ""
"resource-holding types (types with `Disposal` impls or host handles) must not participate in strong cycles;"
msgstr "持有资源的类型（带 `Disposal` impl 或宿主句柄的类型）不得参与强循环引用；"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:158
msgid "parent/child and observer shapes take `Weak` back-pointers;"
msgstr "父/子与观察者形状采用 `Weak` 回指指针；"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:159
msgid "pure-data cycles are harmless — they cost only memory."
msgstr "纯数据的循环引用无害——它们只花费内存。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:161
msgid ""
"You are not left alone with the rule: debug builds assert refcount discipline (retain/release pairing, no underflow, no double free), and at teardown the VM emits a **leak report** — surviving objects grouped by type with allocation sites — which is the primary tool for hunting accidental cycles. Behavior is fully deterministic, so a leak reproduces exactly."
msgstr ""
"这条规则并非让你独自面对：调试构建会断言引用计数纪律（保留/释放配对、无下溢、无双重释放），而 VM 在拆除时会输出一份**泄漏报告**——按类型分组、带分配位置的存活对象清单——它是猎捕意外循环引用的首要工具。行为完全确定，因此泄漏可以精确复现。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:168
msgid "The self-managed heap"
msgstr "自管堆"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:170
msgid ""
"Host code may use `std` freely, but every byte backing a rut value is allocated through the VM's own heap manager. The discipline is the point, not the allocator:"
msgstr "宿主代码可以随意使用 `std`，但支撑 rut 值的每一个字节都经由 VM 自己的堆管理器分配。要点在纪律，而不在分配器："


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:174
msgid ""
"**Cells** come from fixed-size arena chunks with freelists; a dead slot is reused by the next mint."
msgstr "**单元**来自带空闲列表的定长 arena 块；死槽位会被下一次铸造复用。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:176
msgid ""
"**Variable-size payloads** (string octets, array element runs) live in size-classed blocks that never move; in-place geometric growth keeps append loops linear, and freelists recycle the common sizes."
msgstr "**可变尺寸载荷**（字符串字节、数组元素段）住在按尺寸分级的块里，永不移动；就地几何增长让追加循环保持线性，空闲列表回收常见尺寸。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:179
msgid ""
"**Immortal singletons** — interned string literals, enum variants — live in a slab freed only at VM drop, carrying the \"no refcount\" sentinel."
msgstr "**不朽单例**——驻留的字符串字面量、枚举成员——住在只在 VM drop 时释放的 slab 里，携带\"无引用计数\"哨兵。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:182
msgid ""
"**Nothing compacts.** The heap never moves cells, which is precisely what lets the boundary hand Rust zero-copy views into buffers (see [the host boundary](host-boundary.md))."
msgstr ""
"**永不压缩。**堆从不移动单元，这正是边界能把指向缓冲区的零拷贝视图交到 Rust 手里的原因（参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)）。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:186
msgid "Why self-manage instead of using the host's allocator?"
msgstr "为什么自管，而不用宿主的分配器？"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:188
msgid ""
"**Budgets.** An embedder can say \"this script gets N bytes\" and get a clean, resumable out-of-memory trap instead of an OS abort. `vm.heap_usage()` is exact because every allocation is accounted."
msgstr ""
"**预算。**嵌入方可以说\"这个脚本只有 N 字节\"，然后得到一个干净、可恢复的内存耗尽陷阱，而不是操作系统级的中止。`vm.heap_usage()` 是精确的，因为每次分配都被记账。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:191
msgid ""
"**Teardown.** `Vm::drop` frees the whole heap in slab units after the leak report; nothing per-object leaks past the VM — important for wasm pages and plugin hosts that spawn and kill scripts."
msgstr ""
"**拆除。**`Vm::drop` 在泄漏报告之后按 slab 单位释放整个堆；没有任何按对象的东西泄漏出 VM 之外——这对会反复生成、杀掉脚本的 wasm 页面和插件宿主很重要。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:194
msgid ""
"**Leak reporting** walks the VM's own headers, which requires the VM's own headers everywhere."
msgstr "**泄漏报告**遍历的是 VM 自己的头部，这要求处处都是 VM 自己的头部。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:197
msgid ""
"The budget check runs _before_ any write — a failed allocation leaves the heap byte-identical — and traps resumably: raise the limit and continue, or drop references and retry. See the reference on [resource limits](../reference/resource-limits.md) for the full knob set, and [the bytecode VM](the-vm.md) for how budgets interleave with execution."
msgstr ""
"预算检查在任何写入_之前_运行——失败的分配让堆保持逐字节相同——而且陷阱可恢复：调高限额继续，或者丢掉引用再试。完整的旋钮清单见关于[资源限制](../reference/resource-limits.md)的参考章节；预算如何与执行交织，见[字节码 VM](the-vm.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:206
msgid ""
"**Deterministic resource release** — the property the whole design is organized around. If your script opened something, the closing statement is knowable."
msgstr "**确定性的资源释放**——整个设计围绕它组织。如果你的脚本打开了什么，关闭它的语句是可知的。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:209
msgid ""
"**No pauses.** There is no collection pass; destruction happens inline at release-to-zero, so nothing ever interrupts a frame."
msgstr "**没有停顿。**没有收集阶段；析构在计数释放到零时就地发生，所以没有任何东西会打断一帧。"


#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:211
msgid ""
"**A small, honest mental model.** Sharing is by reference, copies are built explicitly (see [everything is a value](everything-is-a-value.md)), lifetimes are refcounts, and the one thing refcounts cannot do — cycles — is a documented rule with a first-class tool."
msgstr ""
"**一个小而诚实的心智模型。**共享靠引用，副本靠显式构建（参见[一切皆值](everything-is-a-value.md)），生命周期就是引用计数，而引用计数唯一做不到的事——循环引用——是一条成文规则配一件一等工具。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:3
msgid ""
"rut exists to be embedded. The host — a Rust program — owns a VM, declares its API once in rut source, binds the implementations with typed Rust closures, and drives everything. The design rule for the whole boundary: **the type system does the checking, not your bridge code.** There is no argument re-parsing, no `as number`, no \"trust-me\" coercion — a value crossing either direction is checked against a reified runtime type, and a mismatch is a loud error naming both sides."
msgstr ""
"rut 生而为嵌入。宿主——一个 Rust 程序——拥有一台 VM，在 rut 源码里一次性声明自己的 API，用带类型的 Rust 闭包绑定实现，然后驱动一切。整个边界的设计规则：**做检查的是类型系统，而不是你的桥接代码。**没有实参重新解析，没有 `as number`，没有\"信我\"式强转——双向跨越的值都对照具体化运行时类型检查，不匹配就是一个点名双方的响亮错误。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:12
msgid "The embedding model"
msgstr "嵌入模型"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:17
msgid "\"app:gfx\""
msgstr "\"app:gfx\""


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:17
msgid "\"gfx.d.rut\""
msgstr "\"gfx.d.rut\""


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:21
msgid "\"app:gfx::newCanvas\""
msgstr "\"app:gfx::newCanvas\""


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:24
msgid ""
"// the join: every declared row must have a binding, and vice versa —\n"
"// verified BEFORE any script runs\n"
msgstr ""
"// 接合：每一条声明的行都必须有绑定，反之亦然——\n"
"// 在任何脚本运行之前校验\n"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:30
msgid ""
"// an entry point\n"
msgstr ""
"// 一个入口点\n"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:31
msgid ""
"// drive async work to idle\n"
msgstr ""
"// 把异步工作驱动到空闲\n"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:34
msgid "The declaration file (a _host package_) spells the surface in rut:"
msgstr "声明文件（一个_宿主包_）用 rut 写下接口："


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:41
msgid ""
"and the load-time join rejects three wiring bugs as panics — an embedder mistake, never a script diagnostic: a declared row with no binding, a binding with no declaration, and signature drift. \"Mount what you bind\": an embedder that mounts a package declares its rows and must bind them."
msgstr ""
"加载期接合会把三种接线错误当作 panic 拒绝——那是嵌入方的失误，绝不是脚本诊断：声明了行却没有绑定、有绑定却没有声明，以及签名漂移。\"挂载什么就绑定什么\"：挂载一个包的嵌入方声明了它的行，就必须绑定它们。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:47 src/reference/value-boundary.md:10
msgid "The crossing set"
msgstr "可跨越集合"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:49
msgid ""
"What may cross is a **compile-time property of the surface**, not a runtime negotiation:"
msgstr "什么可以跨越，是**接口的编译期属性**，不是运行时协商："


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:52
msgid "**Parameters**: the primitives, `str`, `bytes`, and `opaque`."
msgstr "**参数**：原始类型、`str`、`bytes` 与 `opaque`。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:53
msgid ""
"**Returns**: the same set _plus_ the answer optionals `?str`, `?bytes`, `?opaque` — `Option<String>`, `Option<Vec<u8>>`, and the opaque handles mint the nullable box, with `None` as the flat `nil`."
msgstr ""
"**返回**：同一个集合_加上_应答可空类型 `?str`、`?bytes`、`?opaque`——`Option<String>`、`Option<Vec<u8>>` 与 opaque 句柄会铸造可空盒，`None` 就是扁平的 `nil`。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:56
msgid ""
"**Tuples** cross field by field, which makes the error convention — `(value, err)` — a first-class entry answer. The two channels stay distinct by law: a _returned_ `err` is data the host reads and acts on; a _panic_ is drift and arrives on the trap channel, never filling an err field."
msgstr ""
"**对偶**逐字段跨越，这让错误约定——`(value, err)`——成为一等公民的入口应答。两条通道依律保持区分：_返回的_ `err` 是宿主读取并处置的数据；_panic_ 是漂移，走陷阱通道抵达，绝不会填进 err 字段。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:62
msgid ""
"Everything else — user structs and classes, `Vec`s, trait-typed values, closures — stays inside the VM. A declaration that violates the set is a compile error at the declaration, not a failed call at 2 a.m. There is no `any`: a polymorphic crossing seals its value in an erasure box (`opaque(v)` at the call, `opaque.downcast<T>` after), checked, never silent — see [reified types](reified-types.md)."
msgstr ""
"其余一切——用户的 struct 与 class、`Vec`、trait 类型的值、闭包——都留在 VM 内部。违反该集合的声明在声明处就是编译错误，而不是凌晨两点的失败调用。没有 `any`：多态跨越把它的值封进擦除盒（调用处 `opaque(v)`，之后 `opaque.downcast<T>`），受检、绝不无声——参见[具体化类型](reified-types.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:69
msgid "The currency is typed Rust"
msgstr "通货是带类型的 Rust"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:71
msgid ""
"On the Rust side the boundary speaks ordinary Rust types. Each type declares the rut type it binds against and converts checked:"
msgstr "在 Rust 一侧，边界说的是普通的 Rust 类型。每种类型声明它绑定到的 rut 类型，并受检转换："


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:74
msgid ""
"**Borrow, don't copy.** `&str` and `&[u8]` parameters read the VM's buffers zero-copy. The borrow is call-scoped — the type system makes smuggling it past the return a compile error."
msgstr ""
"**借用，不复制。**`&str` 与 `&[u8]` 参数零拷贝地读取 VM 的缓冲区。借用以调用为作用域——类型系统会让把它偷运过返回点成为编译错误。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:77
msgid ""
"**Copy on purpose.** Owned `String`/`Vec<u8>` parameters are the explicit \"I keep this data\" choice."
msgstr "**有意地复制。**拿到所有权的 `String`/`Vec<u8>` 参数是\"我要留下这份数据\"的显式选择。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:79
msgid ""
"**`Opaque<T>`** is the typed view of a host handle: an 8-byte store handle the host holds and passes back; the payload stays host-owned (`Box<dyn Any>` plus an optional finalize hook)."
msgstr ""
"**`Opaque<T>`** 是宿主句柄的带类型视图：一个 8 字节的存储句柄，宿主持有并回传；载荷保持宿主所有（`Box<dyn Any>` 加一个可选的 finalize 钩子）。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:83
msgid ""
"**Borrow guards** make the zero-copy views safe while script runs: a borrowed object is flagged, and script-side mutation through a re-entrant call traps with `borrowed by host` instead of racing. Guards clear on return. This is sound forever because the heap never moves objects (see [memory](memory.md))."
msgstr ""
"**借用守卫**让零拷贝视图在脚本运行期间安全：被借用的对象会被标记，脚本一侧经由重入调用做出的变更将以 `borrowed by host` 触发陷阱，而不是形成数据竞争。守卫在返回时清除。它永远健全，因为堆从不移动对象（参见[内存](memory.md)）。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:89
msgid "Wrapping host state: the class-in-rut pattern"
msgstr "包装宿主状态：rut 类模式"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:91
msgid ""
"There is no \"host class\". Native state crosses as an `opaque` handle and a rut class wraps it — ordinary source the compiler can see and optimize around:"
msgstr "没有\"宿主类\"。原生状态以 `opaque` 句柄跨越，rut 类包裹它——编译器看得见、也能围绕它优化的普通源码："


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:105
msgid ""
"Every method is exactly one host call — the same crossing a magic host class would have paid — but the wrapper can also carry impl blocks, validation, and convenience the native side never needed to know about. The payoff for keeping the boundary this small: host resources die deterministically. When the wrapper's last reference goes, the handle's refcount hits zero and the payload's Rust `Drop` runs _at that point_ — sockets and textures close on script schedule, not at some future collection."
msgstr ""
"每个方法恰好就是一次宿主调用——魔法宿主类同样要付的跨越——但包装器还能承载 impl 块、校验，以及原生一侧从不需要知道的便利。边界保持这样小的回报：宿主资源确定性地死亡。包装器的最后一个引用消失时，句柄的引用计数归零，载荷的 Rust `Drop` _在那一刻_运行——套接字与纹理按脚本的日程关闭，而不是在将来某次收集中。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:114
msgid "Host functions are rows, dispatched by slot"
msgstr "宿主函数是行，按槽位分派"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:116
msgid ""
"Each declared row gets a stable slot id at compile time; calls compile to slot dispatch, so names are binding-time labels only — renaming a Rust-side binding target fails the join instead of silently rebinding. The surface grammar is small:"
msgstr ""
"每条声明的行在编译期得到一个稳定的槽位 id；调用编译为槽位分派，所以名字只是绑定期的标签——重命名 Rust 侧的绑定目标会让接合失败，而不是悄悄重绑。表面语法很小："


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:121
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"host fn name(params) -> T;        // concrete signature; no generics —\n"
"                                  // a generic has no shape to check\n"
"host struct Name { fields };      // flat record of crossing fields\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"host fn name(params) -> T;        // concrete signature; no generics —\n"
"                                  // a generic has no shape to check\n"
"host struct Name { fields };      // flat record of crossing fields\n"
"```"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:127
msgid ""
"`builtin` declarations (the engine's own fns, classes, and traits — `str` methods, `Weak`, `Future`) are engine surface: the embedder cannot spell them, and users implement their traits with ordinary impl blocks. Async rows (`pub host async fn`) are declared like any row and expand into a small row family the driving loop uses — the embedder binds them with one closure per future; see [the async model](async-model.md)."
msgstr ""
"`builtin` 声明（引擎自己的 fn、类和 trait——`str` 方法、`Weak`、`Future`）是引擎表面：嵌入方写不出它们，用户用普通 impl 块实现它们的 trait。异步行（`pub host async fn`）与任何行一样声明，并展开为驱动循环所用的一小组行族——嵌入方为每个 future 绑定一个闭包；参见[异步模型](async-model.md)。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:135
msgid "Re-entrancy, traps, budgets"
msgstr "重入、陷阱、预算"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:137
msgid ""
"A native fn receives a context that may call **back into rut** (`vm.call`) — nested calls run under the same budget on a fresh frame stack."
msgstr "原生 fn 收到的上下文可以**回调进 rut**（`vm.call`）——嵌套调用在同一预算下、崭新的一套帧栈上运行。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:140
msgid ""
"Native code runs **outside the op budget**: the host is trusted to be fast, or to hand back a future instead of blocking. A trap raised inside a native fn propagates to the host as an `Err(Trap)` with the native frame visible in the backtrace."
msgstr ""
"原生代码运行在**操作预算之外**：宿主被信任为快，或者会交还一个 future 而不是阻塞。原生 fn 内部抛出的陷阱以 `Err(Trap)` 传播到宿主，原生帧在回溯中可见。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:144
msgid ""
"Traps are catchable **only at the boundary** — script never catches one. That is what keeps panics loud and state uncorrupted."
msgstr "陷阱**只能在边界**被捕获——脚本永远捕获不到。正是这一点让 panic 保持响亮、状态保持完好。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:147
msgid "What was deliberately left out"
msgstr "刻意留下的空白"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:149
msgid ""
"No C ABI. There is no `register_struct`, no `size_of`, no pointer mirroring of record layouts: records are slot arrays internal to the VM, and a host sees them only through the checked crossing. The few bytes you give up to the checked boundary buy the property that makes embedding pleasant — every mismatch is a named, typed, load-time diagnostic instead of a runtime mystery."
msgstr ""
"没有 C ABI。没有 `register_struct`，没有 `size_of`，没有对记录布局的指针镜像：记录是 VM 内部的槽数组，宿主只能透过受检跨越看见它们。你在受检边界上让出的那几个字节，换来的是让嵌入舒心的性质——每个不匹配都是一个指名道姓、带类型、加载期的诊断，而不是运行时的谜团。"


#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:156
msgid ""
"The full details live in the reference: [embedding and native modules](../reference/embedding.md), [the value boundary and borrows](../reference/value-boundary.md), [host fns and declaration files](../reference/host-fns.md), and the withdrawn C-struct experiment recorded at [repr(C) interop](../reference/repr-c.md)."
msgstr ""
"全部细节住在参考手册里：[嵌入与原生模块](../reference/embedding.md)、[值边界与借用](../reference/value-boundary.md)、[宿主 fn 与声明文件](../reference/host-fns.md)，以及记录在 [repr(C) 互操作](../reference/repr-c.md)的已撤回 C 结构体实验。"


#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:3
msgid ""
"Everything a rut program becomes is a **typed bytecode** executed by a register VM. There is no JIT, no interpreter tiering, no runtime speculation: the compiler does all optimization ahead of time, and what runs is exactly what was compiled. This chapter is the tour of that artifact — the instruction set, the module binary, the load-time verification, and the interpreter's execution and budgeting model."
msgstr ""
"rut 程序最终成为的一切，就是由寄存器 VM 执行的**类型化字节码**。没有 JIT，没有解释器分层，没有运行时投机：编译器提前完成一切优化，运行的就是编译过的东西。本章导览这个产物——指令集、模块二进制、加载期校验，以及解释器的执行与预算模型。"


