msgid ""
"New to the language: read [00 — Todolist](00-todolist.md) and [01 — Sort](01-sort.md) for the embedding shape, then [The playground corpus](playground-corpus.md) for the language surface in small doses. For the web story, [05 — Todolist web](05-todolist-web.md) is the centerpiece and [06 — GitHub viewer CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md) is the networking counterpart. [03 — Plugin](03-plugin.md) is the one to study for packaging and module loading, and [04 — Custom async](04-custom-async.md) for what the future trait looks like from user code."
msgstr ""
"语言新手：先读[00 — 待办清单](00-todolist.md)和[01 — 排序](01-sort.md)了解嵌入形态，再读[Playground 语料](playground-corpus.md)小口尝语言表面。Web 这条线，[05 — Web 待办清单](05-todolist-web.md)是主角，[06 — GitHub 查看器 CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md)是它的网络对应物。打包与模块加载要研究的是[03 — 插件](03-plugin.md)；future trait 从用户代码看长什么样，看[04 — 自定义异步](04-custom-async.md)。"


#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:3
msgid ""
"The first runnable host example, and the template for the rest of the chapter: a Rust program embeds rut, compiles a rut **library** (there is no `main` in it), and drives the library through its `entry fn` surface. The split is two files — `todolist.rut` owns the data and the logic as a `TodoList` class with full CRUD; `src/main.rs` owns the session: compile, verify, then a scripted conversation of `vm.call`s. The one-sentence design rule: **the host owns the session, rut owns the data.**"
msgstr ""
"第一个可运行的宿主示例，也是本章其余部分的模板：一个 Rust 程序嵌入 rut，编译一个 rut **库**（其中没有 `main`），并经由其 `entry fn` 接口驱动这个库。划分是两个文件——`todolist.rut` 作为一个带完整 CRUD 的 `TodoList` 类，掌管数据与逻辑；`src/main.rs` 掌管会话：编译、校验，然后是一段按脚本进行的 `vm.call` 对话。一句话设计规则：**宿主拥有会话，rut 拥有数据。**"


