#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:39
msgid ""
"`examples/00-todolist/todolist.rut` — the type body is fields only; methods live in an inherent `impl` block ([Structs](../reference/structs.md), [Classes and constructors](../reference/classes.md)). Unannotated members are module-private. The block below is the class verbatim — `new`, `add`, and `remove` — closed with a `main` so it runs on its own; the example file itself has no `main` — it is a library the host drives through its `entry fn` surface:"
msgstr ""
"`examples/00-todolist/todolist.rut` —— 类型体只有字段；方法住在固有 `impl` 块里（[结构体](../reference/structs.md)、[类与构造器](../reference/classes.md)）。未加注解的成员是模块私有的。下面的代码块是原封不动的类——`new`、`add` 与 `remove`——补了一个 `main` 收尾让它能独立运行；示例文件本身没有 `main`——它是一个由宿主经 `entry fn` 接口驱动的库："


#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:48
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"struct Todo {\n"
"    id: i32;\n"
"    title: str;\n"
"    done: bool = false;      // field initializer — `done` may be omitted\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub class TodoList {\n"
"    items: Vec<Todo>;         // unannotated members = module-private\n"
"    next_id: i32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl TodoList {\n"
"    pub fn new() -> Self {\n"
"        return Self { items: Vec.new(), next_id: 1 };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    // ---- CREATE ----\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn add(mut self, title: str) -> i32 {\n"
"        let id = self.next_id;\n"
"        self.items.push(Todo { id: id, title: title });\n"
"        self.next_id += 1;\n"
"        return id;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    // ---- DELETE ----\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn remove(mut self, id: i32) -> bool {\n"
"        let kept: Vec<Todo> = Vec.new();\n"
"        let mut removed = false;\n"
"        for (let t of self.items) {\n"
"            when (t.id == id) {\n"
"                true -> { removed = true; },   // drop the row\n"
"                else -> { kept.push(t); },     // keep everything else\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"        if (removed) {\n"
"            self.items = kept;\n"
"        }\n"
"        return removed;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"todos\");\n"
"    let mut list = TodoList.new();\n"
"    list.add(\"implement the VM\");\n"
"    list.add(\"ship the demo\");\n"
"    let first = list.remove(1);\n"
"    let second = list.remove(1);\n"
"    log.info(f\"remove(#1) = {first}, again = {second}, left: {list.items.len()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"struct Todo {\n"
"    id: i32;\n"
"    title: str;\n"
"    done: bool = false;      // field initializer — `done` may be omitted\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub class TodoList {\n"
"    items: Vec<Todo>;         // unannotated members = module-private\n"
"    next_id: i32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl TodoList {\n"
"    pub fn new() -> Self {\n"
"        return Self { items: Vec.new(), next_id: 1 };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    // ---- CREATE ----\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn add(mut self, title: str) -> i32 {\n"
"        let id = self.next_id;\n"
"        self.items.push(Todo { id: id, title: title });\n"
"        self.next_id += 1;\n"
"        return id;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    // ---- DELETE ----\n"
"\n"
"    pub fn remove(mut self, id: i32) -> bool {\n"
"        let kept: Vec<Todo> = Vec.new();\n"
"        let mut removed = false;\n"
"        for (let t of self.items) {\n"
"            when (t.id == id) {\n"
"                true -> { removed = true; },   // drop the row\n"
"                else -> { kept.push(t); },     // keep everything else\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"        if (removed) {\n"
"            self.items = kept;\n"
"        }\n"
"        return removed;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"todos\");\n"
"    let mut list = TodoList.new();\n"
"    list.add(\"implement the VM\");\n"
"    list.add(\"ship the demo\");\n"
"    let first = list.remove(1);\n"
"    let second = list.remove(1);\n"
"    log.info(f\"remove(#1) = {first}, again = {second}, left: {list.items.len()}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:110
msgid ""
"Note `mut self`: writing through a class handle requires a `mut` binding head, the same law [01 — Sort](01-sort.md) exercises on plain vecs — `add` and `remove` both declare it. `remove` filters through a `when`: the matching row is dropped, everything else is kept, and the list is rewritten only if something was actually removed. The read side (not shown) is ordinary code — `len`, `title_of` (which returns `\"\"` for a miss; the example pairs it with `has_title` because there is no `?.` sugar), and a `render` built from f-strings."
msgstr ""
"注意 `mut self`：经由类句柄写入需要 `mut` 绑定头，与 [01 — 排序](01-sort.md)在普通 vec 上演练的是同一条法则——`add` 与 `remove` 都声明了它。`remove` 透过一个 `when` 过滤：匹配的行被丢弃，其余全部保留，只有真的删掉了东西才重写列表。读取一侧（未展示）是普通代码——`len`、`title_of`（未命中返回 `\"\"`；示例把它与 `has_title` 配对，因为没有 `?.` 语法糖），以及一个用 f-string 搭出的 `render`。"


#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:119
msgid "The handle: one opaque box around the world"
msgstr "句柄：一个包住世界的 opaque 盒"


#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:121
msgid ""
"Instances of `TodoList` can never cross into Rust — the crossing set admits primitives, `str`, `bytes`, and `opaque` only, and `entry fn` signatures are checked against that rule **at compile time** (see [the host boundary](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md)). So the library boxes its whole container once and the host holds the handle:"
msgstr ""
"`TodoList` 的实例永远无法跨入 Rust——可跨越集合只接纳原始类型、`str`、`bytes` 与 `opaque`，而 `entry fn` 签名**在编译期**对照这条规则检查（参见[宿主边界](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md)）。所以库把整个容器一次性装盒，宿主持有句柄："


#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:127
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"struct Lists {\n"
"    lists: Vec<TodoList>;    // handle = index; handles stay stable while held\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn at(c: opaque, h: u32) -> TodoList {\n"
"    let lists = opaque.downcast<?Lists>(c);\n"
"    return lists.lists[h as i32];\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"entry fn createContainer() -> opaque {\n"
"    let ls: ?Lists = Lists { lists: Vec.new() };\n"
"    return opaque(ls);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"entry fn create(c: opaque) -> u32 {\n"
"    let k = opaque.downcast<?Lists>(c);\n"
"    k.lists.push(TodoList.new());\n"
"    return (k.lists.len() - 1) as u32;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"struct Lists {\n"
"    lists: Vec<TodoList>;    // handle = index; handles stay stable while held\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn at(c: opaque, h: u32) -> TodoList {\n"
"    let lists = opaque.downcast<?Lists>(c);\n"
"    return lists.lists[h as i32];\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"entry fn createContainer() -> opaque {\n"
"    let ls: ?Lists = Lists { lists: Vec.new() };\n"
"    return opaque(ls);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"entry fn create(c: opaque) -> u32 {\n"
"    let k = opaque.downcast<?Lists>(c);\n"
"    k.lists.push(TodoList.new());\n"
"    return (k.lists.len() - 1) as u32;\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:149
msgid ""
"Two things to take away. First, `entry fn` marks the host-callable surface — distinct from `pub`, which is use-visibility for other rut modules and carries no crossing limits ([Modules and visibility](../reference/modules-and-visibility.md)). Second, erasure is the `opaque(v)` type-call and recovery is `opaque.downcast<T>(o) -> ?T` — a wrong box answers `nil`, never a trap ([opaque — erasure and downcast](../reference/opaque.md)). The internal helper `at` is an ordinary `fn` and may speak in full types."
msgstr ""
"有两点值得带走。第一，`entry fn` 标记的是宿主可调用接口——与 `pub` 不同，后者是面向其他 rut 模块的使用可见性，不携带任何跨越限制（[模块与可见性](../reference/modules-and-visibility.md)）。第二，擦除就是 `opaque(v)` 类型调用，恢复是 `opaque.downcast<T>(o) -> ?T`——错误的盒回答 `nil`，绝不触发陷阱（[opaque — 擦除与向下转型](../reference/opaque.md)）。内部辅助函数 `at` 是普通 `fn`，可以用完整类型说话。"


