#: src/examples/01-sort.md:35
msgid ""
"The fuel column is the demo's quiet joke: quick \\< insertion \\< selection \\< bubble, exactly as the textbooks promise — and the VM counts it for you."
msgstr ""
"燃料那一列是这个演示不动声色的玩笑：quick \\< insertion \\< selection \\< bubble，与教科书的承诺分毫不差——而且 VM 替你把它数了出来。"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:41
msgid "One opaque bank; the data never leaves rut"
msgstr "一个 opaque 银行；数据永不离开 rut"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:43
msgid ""
"`Vec<i32>` cannot cross the host boundary, so `create()` boxes a `Bank` in an `opaque` and the host holds the handle — the [00 — Todolist](00-todolist.md) pattern again. Results come back three ways, all crossing-shaped. `serialize` below is verbatim, plus a `main` that boxes a small bank the way `create()` does, so the block runs on its own:"
msgstr ""
"`Vec<i32>` 无法跨越宿主边界，所以 `create()` 把一个 `Bank` 装进 `opaque`，宿主持有句柄——又是[00 — 待办清单](00-todolist.md)的模式。结果以三种方式回来，全是跨越的形状。下面的 `serialize` 是原文照录，再加一个像 `create()` 那样给小银行装盒的 `main`，让代码块能独立运行："


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:50
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"struct Bank {\n"
"    data: ?Vec<i32>;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"entry fn serialize(c: opaque) -> str {\n"
"    let b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let xs = b.data;\n"
"    let mut out = \"[\";\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < xs.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"        if (i > 0) {\n"
"            out = f\"{out}, \";\n"
"        }\n"
"        out = f\"{out}{xs[i]}\";\n"
"    }\n"
"    return f\"{out}]\";\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sort\");\n"
"    let bank: ?Bank = Bank { data: Vec<i32>.from([5, 2, 9, 2]) };\n"
"    let c = opaque(bank);\n"
"    log.info(f\"serialized: {serialize(c)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"struct Bank {\n"
"    data: ?Vec<i32>;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"entry fn serialize(c: opaque) -> str {\n"
"    let b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let xs = b.data;\n"
"    let mut out = \"[\";\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < xs.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"        if (i > 0) {\n"
"            out = f\"{out}, \";\n"
"        }\n"
"        out = f\"{out}{xs[i]}\";\n"
"    }\n"
"    return f\"{out}]\";\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sort\");\n"
"    let bank: ?Bank = Bank { data: Vec<i32>.from([5, 2, 9, 2]) };\n"
"    let c = opaque(bank);\n"
"    log.info(f\"serialized: {serialize(c)}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:83
msgid ""
"`serialize` is the workhorse: a whole result crosses as **one JSON array string**, so the host asserts an entire sort in one compare. `get(c, i)` / `has(c, i)` read element-by-element, and `is_sorted(c)` returns the verdict."
msgstr ""
"`serialize` 是干重活的：整个结果以**一个 JSON 数组字符串**跨越，宿主一次比较就能断言一整趟排序。`get(c, i)` / `has(c, i)` 逐元素读取，`is_sorted(c)` 给出判定。"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:88
msgid "The dispatcher: `when` on strings, errors as values"
msgstr "分派器：对字符串的 `when`，错误即值"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:90
msgid ""
"Every algorithm sits behind a single string-keyed entry. Unknown names are an ordinary value, not a trap — the empty string means success:"
msgstr "每个算法都坐在一个按字符串为键的入口背后。未知名是普通值，不是陷阱——空字符串表示成功："


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:93
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"entry fn sort(c: opaque, algo: str) -> str {\n"
"    let b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let mut unknown = false;\n"
"    when (algo) {\n"
"        \"insertion\" -> { insertion_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        \"bubble\"    -> { bubble_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        \"selection\" -> { selection_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        \"quick\"     -> { quicksort(b.data, 0, b.data.len() - 1); },\n"
"        \"merge\"     -> { merge_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        else        -> { unknown = true; },\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (unknown) {\n"
"        return f\"unknown algorithm: {algo}\";\n"
"    }\n"
"    return \"\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"entry fn sort(c: opaque, algo: str) -> str {\n"
"    let b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let mut unknown = false;\n"
"    when (algo) {\n"
"        \"insertion\" -> { insertion_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        \"bubble\"    -> { bubble_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        \"selection\" -> { selection_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        \"quick\"     -> { quicksort(b.data, 0, b.data.len() - 1); },\n"
"        \"merge\"     -> { merge_sort(b.data); },\n"
"        else        -> { unknown = true; },\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (unknown) {\n"
"        return f\"unknown algorithm: {algo}\";\n"
"    }\n"
"    return \"\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:112
msgid ""
"`when` with string-literal arms is the general dispatch idiom — see [Control flow and when](../reference/control-flow.md)."
msgstr "带字符串字面量分支的 `when` 是通用的分派惯用法——参见[控制流与 when](../reference/control-flow.md)。"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:115
msgid "Deterministic input in one call"
msgstr "一次调用拿到确定性输入"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:117
msgid ""
"`fill` replaces the bank with `n` pseudo-random values from a linear-congruential generator, so sizing a benchmark input is one host round-trip, not one per element. The u32 math must **wrap**, and rut makes that explicit — plain `*` traps on overflow. The entry is verbatim (the `Bank` inlined so the block compiles alone), with a `main` that fills and prints what one call produces:"
msgstr ""
"`fill` 用线性同余生成器产生的 `n` 个伪随机值替换银行的内容，于是给基准测试定输入尺寸只需一次宿主往返，而不是每元素一次。u32 数学必须**回绕**，rut 把这一点写得明明白白——普通 `*` 在溢出时触发陷阱。入口是原文照录（`Bank` 内联进来让代码块独立编译），配一个填充并打印单次调用产出的 `main`："


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:124
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"struct Bank { data: ?Vec<i32>; }   // inlined from above — the block runs alone\n"
"\n"
"entry fn fill(c: opaque, n: u32, seed: u32) {\n"
"    let mut b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let fresh: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();\n"
"    let mut x = seed | 1;         // the LCG needs an odd state\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < n as i32; i += 1) {\n"
"        x = (x.wrapping_mul(1664525)).wrapping_add(1013904223);\n"
"        fresh.push((x % 1000) as i32);\n"
"    }\n"
"    b.data = fresh;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sort\");\n"
"    let bank: ?Bank = Bank { data: nil };\n"
"    let c = opaque(bank);\n"
"    fill(c, 8, 42);\n"
"    let b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let xs = b.data;\n"
"    let mut out = \"\";\n"
"    for (let x of xs) {\n"
"        out = f\"{out} {x}\";\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"fill(8, seed=42):{out}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"struct Bank { data: ?Vec<i32>; }   // inlined from above — the block runs alone\n"
"\n"
"entry fn fill(c: opaque, n: u32, seed: u32) {\n"
"    let mut b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let fresh: Vec<i32> = Vec.new();\n"
"    let mut x = seed | 1;         // the LCG needs an odd state\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < n as i32; i += 1) {\n"
"        x = (x.wrapping_mul(1664525)).wrapping_add(1013904223);\n"
"        fresh.push((x % 1000) as i32);\n"
"    }\n"
"    b.data = fresh;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"sort\");\n"
"    let bank: ?Bank = Bank { data: nil };\n"
"    let c = opaque(bank);\n"
"    fill(c, 8, 42);\n"
"    let b = opaque.downcast<?Bank>(c);\n"
"    let xs = b.data;\n"
"    let mut out = \"\";\n"
"    for (let x of xs) {\n"
"        out = f\"{out} {x}\";\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"fill(8, seed=42):{out}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:160
msgid ""
"The wrapping family (`wrapping_mul`, `wrapping_add`, `wrapping_shl`) is the honest spelling of two's-complement arithmetic — the [playground corpus](playground-corpus.md) has a whole `checked-arith` case on the contrast."
msgstr ""
"回绕家族（`wrapping_mul`、`wrapping_add`、`wrapping_shl`）是二进制补码算术的如实拼法——[Playground 语料](playground-corpus.md)里有一整个 `checked-arith` 案例专门对比。"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:165
msgid "Recursion under fuel"
msgstr "燃料之下的递归"


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:167
msgid ""
"Quicksort partitions in place; merge sort builds out-of-place halves and merges back through the shared handle. Both are plain recursive fns — the call-frame stack is the VM's, counted by the same fuel budget ([the bytecode VM](../core-concepts/the-vm.md)):"
msgstr ""
"快速排序就地分区；归并排序构建非就地的两半，再透过共享句柄归并回来。两者都是普通的递归 fn——调用帧栈就是 VM 的，按同一份燃料预算计费（[字节码 VM](../core-concepts/the-vm.md)）："


#: src/examples/01-sort.md:183
msgid ""
"Note the `mut xs` parameter heads: vecs are handles, so an in-place swap inside a call is shared with the bank — but **writing** through the handle requires the `mut` binding head, while mere reads (and `push`) do not. That asymmetry is the mut-binding law, and every algorithm in this file declares it ([Modules and visibility](../reference/modules-and-visibility.md))."
msgstr ""
"注意 `mut xs` 参数头：vec 是句柄，所以调用内部的一次就地交换与银行共享——但**写入**句柄需要 `mut` 绑定头，而单纯的读取（以及 `push`）不需要。这个不对称就是 mut 绑定法则，本文件里每个算法都声明了它（[模块与可见性](../reference/modules-and-visibility.md)）。"


