#: src/examples/02-digest.md:53
msgid "The integer surface is enough for real algorithms"
msgstr "整数表面足以支撑真实算法"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:55
msgid ""
"`digest.rut` runs on hex literals, `u32`/`u64`, the wrapping family, and signedness-correct shifts. CRC-32 is the compact showcase — table-free, bitwise, and exactly the textbook loop. The entry is pure rut — no host, no manifest — so it runs on its own, here checked against the algorithm's canonical test value:"
msgstr ""
"`digest.rut` 跑在十六进制字面量、`u32`/`u64`、回绕家族和符号正确的移位上。CRC-32 是紧凑的展示品——无表、逐位、与教科书循环一模一样。入口是纯 rut——没有宿主、没有清单——所以它能独立运行，这里对照该算法的规范测试值："


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:61
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn crc32(data: bytes) -> u32 {\n"
"    let mut crc: u32 = 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"    for (let b of data) {\n"
"        crc = crc ^ b as u32;\n"
"        for (let k = 0; k < 8; k += 1) {\n"
"            if ((crc & 1) == 1) {\n"
"                crc = (crc >> 1) ^ 0xEDB88320u32;\n"
"            } else {\n"
"                crc = crc >> 1;\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    return crc ^ 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"crc\");\n"
"    let vector = \"123456789\".encode();   // the canonical CRC-32 test vector\n"
"    log.info(f\"crc32(vector) = {crc32(vector)} — check value 0xCBF43926: {crc32(vector) == 0xCBF43926u32}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn crc32(data: bytes) -> u32 {\n"
"    let mut crc: u32 = 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"    for (let b of data) {\n"
"        crc = crc ^ b as u32;\n"
"        for (let k = 0; k < 8; k += 1) {\n"
"            if ((crc & 1) == 1) {\n"
"                crc = (crc >> 1) ^ 0xEDB88320u32;\n"
"            } else {\n"
"                crc = crc >> 1;\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    return crc ^ 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"crc\");\n"
"    let vector = \"123456789\".encode();   // the canonical CRC-32 test vector\n"
"    log.info(f\"crc32(vector) = {crc32(vector)} — check value 0xCBF43926: {crc32(vector) == 0xCBF43926u32}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:90
msgid ""
"SHA-512 is the demanding one: its 64-bit rotations need `>>` to be a _logical_ shift on `u64` and `wrapping_shl` to truncate to the operand width. The FNV/djb2/sdbm trio, by contrast, deliberately never shifts a 64-bit word — `wrapping_mul`, `wrapping_add`, and `^` carry them, showing how far the primitive surface alone goes."
msgstr ""
"SHA-512 是最挑剔的那个：它的 64 位旋转需要 `>>` 在 `u64` 上是_逻辑_移位，需要 `wrapping_shl` 截断到操作数宽度。相比之下，FNV/djb2/sdbm 三件套刻意从不移位 64 位字——`wrapping_mul`、`wrapping_add` 与 `^` 撑起它们，展示了仅凭原始类型表面能走多远。"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:96
msgid "`bytes` crosses directly; `opaque` appears exactly once"
msgstr "`bytes` 直接跨越；`opaque` 恰好出现一次"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:98
msgid ""
"Byte payloads need no wrapper — `bytes` is in the crossing set, so `entry fn hex_enc(data: bytes) -> str` takes a host byte slice head-on ([primitive types](../reference/primitive-types.md)). The one erasure in the file is the recursive JSON tree: rut has no recursive dataclass, so the tree is a tagged union by hand with children boxed in `opaque` to break the recursion ([opaque — erasure and downcast](../reference/opaque.md)):"
msgstr ""
"字节载荷不需要包装器——`bytes` 在可跨越集合里，所以 `entry fn hex_enc(data: bytes) -> str` 迎面接下宿主的字节切片（[原始类型](../reference/primitive-types.md)）。文件中唯一一处擦除是递归的 JSON 树：rut 没有递归数据类，所以这棵树是手工打造的带标签联合，子节点装进 `opaque` 盒以打断递归（[opaque — 擦除与向下转型](../reference/opaque.md)）："


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:106
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"enum JTag { Null, False, True, Num, Str, Arr, Obj }\n"
"\n"
"struct Json {\n"
"    tag:  JTag;\n"
"    num: str;          // verbatim lexeme — exact round-trips, no\n"
"    str: str;          // float formatting anywhere in this file\n"
"    arr:  Vec<opaque>;\n"
"    keys: Vec<str>;\n"
"    vals: Vec<opaque>;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"enum JTag { Null, False, True, Num, Str, Arr, Obj }\n"
"\n"
"struct Json {\n"
"    tag:  JTag;\n"
"    num: str;          // verbatim lexeme — exact round-trips, no\n"
"    str: str;          // float formatting anywhere in this file\n"
"    arr:  Vec<opaque>;\n"
"    keys: Vec<str>;\n"
"    vals: Vec<opaque>;\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:119
msgid ""
"Storing numbers as their **verbatim lexemes** is what makes round-trips exact: `-3e2` decodes and re-encodes as `-3e2`, with no float formatting anywhere in the file."
msgstr "把数字按**原样词素**存储正是往返精确的原因：`-3e2` 解码再编码还是 `-3e2`，全文件没有任何浮点格式化。"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:123
msgid "The encode half rides the std `json` package"
msgstr "编码半边骑在 std `json` 包上"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:125
msgid ""
"The encode side is not private code: it is an `impl` of the std `json` package's serialization trait, driving the package's writer. This is the orphan rule's type-local case — json owns the trait, this file owns `Json`, so the pair is legal exactly here ([Traits and dispatch](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)):"
msgstr ""
"编码一侧不是私有代码：它是 std `json` 包序列化 trait 的一个 `impl`，驱动该包的 writer。这是孤儿规则的类型本地情形——json 拥有 trait，本文件拥有 `Json`，所以这个组合恰好在这里合法（[trait 与分派](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)）："


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:131
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"impl JsonSerialize for Json {\n"
"    fn encode(self, mut w: JsonWriter) -> ?EncodeJsonError {\n"
"        when (self.tag) {\n"
"            JTag.Null -> { w.write_raw(\"null\"); },\n"
"            JTag.False -> { w.write_raw(\"false\"); },\n"
"            JTag.True -> { w.write_raw(\"true\"); },\n"
"            JTag.Num -> { w.write_raw(self.num); },\n"
"            JTag.Str -> { w.write_str(self.str); },\n"
"            JTag.Arr -> {\n"
"                w.begin_array();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.arr.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    let ae: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.arr[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ae.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_array();\n"
"            },\n"
"            JTag.Obj -> {\n"
"                w.begin_object();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.keys.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    w.key(self.keys[i]);\n"
"                    let ve: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.vals[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ve.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_object();\n"
"            },\n"
"        }\n"
"        return nil;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"impl JsonSerialize for Json {\n"
"    fn encode(self, mut w: JsonWriter) -> ?EncodeJsonError {\n"
"        when (self.tag) {\n"
"            JTag.Null -> { w.write_raw(\"null\"); },\n"
"            JTag.False -> { w.write_raw(\"false\"); },\n"
"            JTag.True -> { w.write_raw(\"true\"); },\n"
"            JTag.Num -> { w.write_raw(self.num); },\n"
"            JTag.Str -> { w.write_str(self.str); },\n"
"            JTag.Arr -> {\n"
"                w.begin_array();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.arr.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    let ae: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.arr[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ae.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_array();\n"
"            },\n"
"            JTag.Obj -> {\n"
"                w.begin_object();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.keys.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    w.key(self.keys[i]);\n"
"                    let ve: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.vals[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ve.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_object();\n"
"            },\n"
"        }\n"
"        return nil;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:165
msgid ""
"The entry surface then hands the tree to `encodeJson` and flattens the `(str, err)` pair it answers. The decode half stays a private cursor parser (strings iterate as codepoints, so the source is split once into single-char strings and walked by index) — and every decode error is an honest string value, never a trap:"
msgstr ""
"入口接口随后把树交给 `encodeJson`，并把它回答的 `(str, err)` 对偶摊平。解码半边保持为一个私有的游标解析器（字符串按码点迭代，所以源串被一次性切成单字符字符串再按索引走）——而每个解码错误都是诚实的字符串值，绝不是陷阱："


#: src/examples/02-digest.md:171
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"hex_dec(\"zz\")   = \"hex: invalid character at index 0\"\n"
"b64_dec(\"!*\")   = \"base64: invalid character `!`\"\n"
"json_dec(\"{,}\") = \"json: expected a key string at index 1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"hex_dec(\"zz\")   = \"hex: invalid character at index 0\"\n"
"b64_dec(\"!*\")   = \"base64: invalid character `!`\"\n"
"json_dec(\"{,}\") = \"json: expected a key string at index 1\"\n"
"```"


