#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:80
msgid "The http face: build a request, await the send"
msgstr "http 面孔：构建请求，await 发送"


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:82
msgid ""
"The std `http` package is **async-only and unsuffixed**: only the operations that really wait are async points, everything else is sync construction sugar. The five verbs are build sugars (`get`/`post`/ `put`/`patch`/`del` — the DELETE verb spells `del` because `delete` is a removed word in rut's grammar; the wire still sees canonical `DELETE`), and `send(cx)` is THE async point, resolving **at headers** — the wire body stays unread ([the async model](../core-concepts/async-model.md)):"
msgstr ""
"std `http` 包**只异步且无后缀**：真正要等的操作才是异步点，其余一切都是同步的构建语法糖。五个动词都是构建糖（`get`/`post`/ `put`/`patch`/`del` ——DELETE 动词拼作 `del`，因为 `delete` 是 rut 语法里的被移除词；线上看到的仍是规范的 `DELETE`），而 `send(cx)` 是那个 THE 异步点，**在头部就**解析——线上主体保持未读（[异步模型](../core-concepts/async-model.md)）："


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:91
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"async fn do_list(cx: RunContext, client: HttpClient, owner: str, repo: str, rf: str) -> i32 {\n"
"    let url = f\"https://data.jsdelivr.com/v1/packages/gh/{owner}/{repo}@{rf}\";\n"
"    let resp = await client.get(url).build().send(cx);\n"
"    let err = map_response(resp, \"no such repo or ref\", \"data.jsdelivr.com\");\n"
"    if (err != nil) {\n"
"        let why: str = err;\n"
"        eprint(why);\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    let (tree, e) = decodeJsonBytes<Root>(await resp.body(cx));\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"async fn do_list(cx: RunContext, client: HttpClient, owner: str, repo: str, rf: str) -> i32 {\n"
"    let url = f\"https://data.jsdelivr.com/v1/packages/gh/{owner}/{repo}@{rf}\";\n"
"    let resp = await client.get(url).build().send(cx);\n"
"    let err = map_response(resp, \"no such repo or ref\", \"data.jsdelivr.com\");\n"
"    if (err != nil) {\n"
"        let why: str = err;\n"
"        eprint(why);\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    let (tree, e) = decodeJsonBytes<Root>(await resp.body(cx));\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:104
msgid ""
"`list` is the **drain** lane: one `body(cx)` await pulls the whole tree, and the JSON decode goes through the std `json` package's reader with `impl JsonDeserialize for Entry` in this file. Status mapping is one function: `status() == 0` is the reserved transport verdict, 404 names the host that was checked, 403 is the rate-limit note, anything else non-2xx is the bare status."
msgstr ""
"`list` 是**排空**链路：一次 `body(cx)` await 拉下整棵树，JSON 解码走 std `json` 包的 reader，配本文件里的 `impl JsonDeserialize for Entry`。状态映射只有一个函数：`status() == 0` 是保留的传输判定，404 点名被检查的宿主，403 是限流提示，其余非 2xx 就是裸状态码。"


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:111
msgid "The download: true streaming, chunk by chunk"
msgstr "下载：真正的流式，逐块进行"


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:113
msgid ""
"`download` walks a `ByteStream` — `next(cx)` answers one chunk per await (nil = EOF-or-failed; the sticky `error()` names which), and each chunk lands through the **sync** `append_file` host row. The destination is truncated once first, so a stale file never leaks its tail into a fresh download:"
msgstr ""
"`download` 走过一个 `ByteStream`——`next(cx)` 每次 await 回答一个块（nil = EOF 或失败；粘性的 `error()` 指明是哪种），每个块经由**同步的** `append_file` 宿主行落地。目标文件先被一次性截断，所以陈旧文件绝不会把尾巴漏进新下载："


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:119
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"    let stream = resp.byte_stream();\n"
"    let mut total: i32 = 0;\n"
"    while (true) {\n"
"        let c = await stream.next(cx);\n"
"        if (c == nil) {\n"
"            // EOF — or a mid-read failure? the sticky error names it\n"
"            let rerr = stream.error();\n"
"            if (rerr != nil) {\n"
"                let why: str = rerr;\n"
"                eprint(f\"rgh: {dest}: {why}\");\n"
"                return 1;\n"
"            }\n"
"            break;\n"
"        }\n"
"        let chunk: bytes = c;\n"
"        let werr: ?str = append_file(dest, chunk);\n"
"        if (werr != nil) {\n"
"            let why: str = werr;\n"
"            eprint(f\"rgh: {dest}: {why}\");\n"
"            return 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"        total += chunk.len();\n"
"    }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"    let stream = resp.byte_stream();\n"
"    let mut total: i32 = 0;\n"
"    while (true) {\n"
"        let c = await stream.next(cx);\n"
"        if (c == nil) {\n"
"            // EOF — or a mid-read failure? the sticky error names it\n"
"            let rerr = stream.error();\n"
"            if (rerr != nil) {\n"
"                let why: str = rerr;\n"
"                eprint(f\"rgh: {dest}: {why}\");\n"
"                return 1;\n"
"            }\n"
"            break;\n"
"        }\n"
"        let chunk: bytes = c;\n"
"        let werr: ?str = append_file(dest, chunk);\n"
"        if (werr != nil) {\n"
"            let why: str = werr;\n"
"            eprint(f\"rgh: {dest}: {why}\");\n"
"            return 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"        total += chunk.len();\n"
"    }\n"
"```"


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:145
msgid ""
"Bounded memory end to end, and every failure on the data path is a message plus an exit code — never a panic, never a trap. The lane's one-shot law is worth knowing: per response it is `body()` **xor** `byte_stream()`, and a late/second taker degrades (an empty drain, a dead reader) rather than trapping."
msgstr ""
"内存全程有界，数据路径上的每个失败都是一条消息加一个退出码——绝不是 panic，绝不是陷阱。这条链路的一次性法则值得知道：每个响应要么 `body()` 要么 `byte_stream()`，**二选一**；迟到者或第二名取用者会退化（空排空、失效 reader）而不是触发陷阱。"


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:151
msgid "The readbacks, on the response handle"
msgstr "读回，在响应句柄上"


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:153
msgid ""
"The `Response` class wraps the host's opaque handle with sync readbacks — status, the 2xx test, the transport text, and the sticky mid-read failure ([the std packages](../reference/stdlib.md)):"
msgstr ""
"`Response` 类用同步读回包装宿主的 opaque 句柄——状态、2xx 测试、传输文本，以及粘性的读取中途失败（[std 包](../reference/stdlib.md)）："


#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:158
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"impl Response {\n"
"    /// the HTTP status word — 0 means the transport failed (0 is never\n"
"    /// a real status; any real status, 4xx/5xx included, is not one)\n"
"    pub fn status(self) -> i32 { return http_status(self.r); }\n"
"\n"
"    /// the 2xx test\n"
"    pub fn ok(self) -> bool {\n"
"        let s = self.status();\n"
"        return s >= 200 && s < 300;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    /// the transport-failure text — nil unless status is 0\n"
"    pub fn transport_error(self) -> ?str { return http_err(self.r); }\n"
"\n"
"    /// the sticky mid-read failure — nil until one fails, then\n"
"    /// non-nil forever; meaningful after awaiting `body()`/`next()`\n"
"    pub fn read_error(self) -> ?str { return http_read_err(self.r); }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"impl Response {\n"
"    /// the HTTP status word — 0 means the transport failed (0 is never\n"
"    /// a real status; any real status, 4xx/5xx included, is not one)\n"
"    pub fn status(self) -> i32 { return http_status(self.r); }\n"
"\n"
"    /// the 2xx test\n"
"    pub fn ok(self) -> bool {\n"
"        let s = self.status();\n"
"        return s >= 200 && s < 300;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    /// the transport-failure text — nil unless status is 0\n"
"    pub fn transport_error(self) -> ?str { return http_err(self.r); }\n"
"\n"
"    /// the sticky mid-read failure — nil until one fails, then\n"
"    /// non-nil forever; meaningful after awaiting `body()`/`next()`\n"
"    pub fn read_error(self) -> ?str { return http_read_err(self.r); }\n"
"```"


