msgstr ""
"// high-water mark: vm.heap_peak()\n"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:42
msgid ""
"// live budget change\n"
msgstr ""
"// live budget change\n"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:46
msgid ""
"Every route that materializes a rut value goes through it: cell mint, `Vec` growth, string concatenation, frame-pool growth, `opaque` store inserts. **The contributor rule**: an allocation path that materializes a rut value and does not flow through `alloc` is a bug — the budget would not bind, `heap_usage` would lie, and the leak report would miss it."
msgstr ""
"每条实体化 rut 值的路径都经过它：单元铸造、`Vec` 增长、字符串拼接、帧池增长、`opaque` 存储插入。**贡献者法则**：一条实体化 rut 值却不流经 `alloc` 的分配路径是 bug —— 预算将不再约束，`heap_usage` 会说谎，泄漏报告会漏掉它。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:53
msgid ""
"Accounting checks run **before any write**: a failed allocation leaves the heap byte-identical to its state before the op, and the trap is resumable ([resource limits](resource-limits.md))."
msgstr ""
"记账检查**在任何写入之前**运行：一次失败的分配让堆与操作之前的状态字节级一致，且陷阱可恢复（[资源限制](resource-limits.md)）。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:57
msgid "Allocation strategy (v1)"
msgstr "分配策略（v1）"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:59
msgid ""
"**Fixed-size cell slots in the arena.** Cells are one fixed-size record carved from 1024-slot chunks with a free list; a dead slot is reused by the next mint. Reuse is invisible except in `heap_usage`."
msgstr ""
"**arena 中的定长单元槽。** 单元是从 1024 槽的块中刻出的定长记录，带一个空闲列表；死槽被下一次铸造复用。除了在 `heap_usage` 之中，复用是不可见的。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:62
msgid ""
"**The block store.** Every _variable-size_ payload — string octets, array element runs — lives in a block carved from size-classed pages the VM owns:"
msgstr "**块存储。** 每个可变大小载荷 —— 字符串字节、数组元素段 —— 都生活在从 VM 拥有的、按大小分类的页面中刻出的块里："


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:65
msgid ""
"Size classes 16 B … 2 KiB (multiples of 8); small blocks come from 32 KiB pages via per-class free lists plus a single-slot LIFO cache for the churn pattern (a temp dies, the same size is minted again)."
msgstr ""
"大小类别 16 B …… 2 KiB（8 的倍数）；小块来自 32 KiB 页，经由每类别空闲列表加上一个单槽 LIFO 缓存来服务反复创建的模式（一个临时值死亡，同样的大小再次被铸造）。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:68
msgid ""
"In-place growth within a class keeps append-accumulation loops linear; the block header carries the class-rounded capacity, so free re-derives the class with no side table."
msgstr "类别内的就地增长让追加累加循环保持线性；块头部携带按类别取整的容量，因此 free 无需旁表即可重新推导类别。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:71
msgid "Large blocks (> 2 KiB) get dedicated allocations, freed wholesale."
msgstr "大块（> 2 KiB）获得专用分配，整体释放。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:72
msgid ""
"Blocks are 1:1 with their cell (the cell is the counted unit) and **never move**, so a raw `&[u8]` into the store stays valid for the cell's life."
msgstr "块与其单元 1:1（单元是被计数的单位）且**绝不移动**，因此指向存储的裸 `&[u8]` 在单元的生命期内保持有效。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:75
msgid ""
"**Immortal singletons.** Interned string literals and dataless enum variants live in a slab freed only at `Vm` drop; they carry the `rc == 0` sentinel."
msgstr "**不朽单例。** 驻留的字符串字面量与无数据枚举变体生活在一个只在 `Vm` 丢弃时释放的 slab 中；它们携带 `rc == 0` 哨兵。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:78
msgid ""
"**The `opaque` store.** Every rut `opaque` value lives in a slab of two-kind entries (rut value / host payload) with its own borrow guards; entries charge their bytes on insert and refund on death, so the budget and the receipts stay honest."
msgstr ""
"**`opaque` 存储。** 每个 rut `opaque` 值生活在一个两类条目（rut 值 / 宿主载荷）的 slab 中，带有自己的借用守卫；条目在插入时记入字节账、在死亡时退款，因此预算与回执保持诚实。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:82
msgid ""
"**No compaction in v1.** Non-moving keeps host borrows into `Vec` buffers sound and freelists trivial."
msgstr "**v1 没有压缩。** 不移动让指向 `Vec` 缓冲的宿主借用保持健全，空闲列表保持平凡。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:84
msgid ""
"**Cells are addressed by raw pointer** in the slot word. A 32-bit handle design was prototyped and reverted on measurement: ref-heavy workloads paid +8–15% for the decode chain per slot read."
msgstr ""
"**单元以裸指针寻址**记录在槽字中。32 位句柄设计被原型化过，又因测量结果而回退：引用密集的工作负载在每次槽读取上为解码链付出 +8–15% 的代价。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:88
msgid "Deterministic teardown"
msgstr "确定性拆卸"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:90
msgid ""
"Teardown mirrors the destruction rules: the host drops its references, releases run inline ([the Rc heap](rc-heap.md)), and `Vm::drop` frees the survivors wholesale — leaked cycles included — after emitting the leak report. The heap never outlives the `Vm`, and no rut cell can outlive the heap."
msgstr ""
"拆卸镜像销毁规则：宿主丢弃自己的引用，release 内联运行（[Rc 堆](rc-heap.md)），`Vm::drop` 在发出泄漏报告之后整体释放幸存者 —— 泄漏的循环也在内。堆的寿命绝不超过 `Vm`，也没有任何 rut 单元能比堆活得更久。"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:99
msgid "\"used {} bytes (peak {})\""
msgstr "\"used {} bytes (peak {})\""


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:99
msgid ""
"// dropping `vm` frees every remaining slab\n"
msgstr ""
"// dropping `vm` frees every remaining slab\n"


#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:103
msgid ""
"Worker heaps are per-VM and charged to the child's own budget ([workers and channels](workers-and-channels.md))."
msgstr "worker 堆按 VM 隔离，记在子 VM 自己的预算上（[worker 与通道](workers-and-channels.md)）。"


#: src/reference/resource-limits.md:3
msgid ""
"Two knobs make rut safe for third-party code: a **heap budget** and **fuel**. Both are enforced as **resumable traps**, both are set at construction, and both bind on the VM's own accounting ([the VM heap](vm-heap.md)) — not on the OS."
msgstr ""
"两个旋钮让 rut 对第三方代码安全：**堆预算**与**燃料**。两者都作为**可恢复陷阱**强制执行，都在构造时设置，都绑定在 VM 自己的记账上（[VM 堆](vm-heap.md)）—— 而不是操作系统上。"


#: src/reference/resource-limits.md:10
msgid ""
"// None = unbounded ops\n"
msgstr ""
"// None = unbounded ops\n"


#: src/reference/resource-limits.md:11
