#: src/reference/host-futures.md:123
msgid ""
"`run_ready()` drains the ready queue, polls the parked host futures (each poll runs the `__yield` probe; a ready one is driven through `__take` and its awaiter re-enqueued), then drains again — one pass settles a completed host future end to end. `vm.pending_tasks()` counts ready frames, armed timers, and the host-pending set, so a worker that never completes keeps the loop alive — the flip side of best-effort cancellation."
msgstr ""
"`run_ready()` 排空就绪队列，轮询停放中的宿主 future（每次轮询运行 `__yield` 探针；就绪者经由 `__take` 被驱动，其 awaiter 重新入队），然后再排空一次——一趟就把一个已完成的宿主 future 端到端落定。`vm.pending_tasks()` 统计就绪帧、已布防定时器和宿主 pending 集，因此一个永不完成的 worker 会让循环一直活着——这是尽力而为取消的另一面。"


#: src/reference/host-futures.md:131
msgid ""
"The virtual clock works here too: drive with finite fuel and `vm.set_now` for deterministic tests ([resource limits](resource-limits.md))."
msgstr "虚拟时钟在这里同样适用：以有限燃料驱动并配合 `vm.set_now` 做确定性测试（[资源限制](resource-limits.md)）。"


#: src/reference/host-futures.md:135
msgid "In-tree users"
msgstr "树内使用者"


#: src/reference/host-futures.md:137
msgid ""
"The standard HTTP lane is a `register_async!` client: `http_send`, `http_body`, and `http_stream_next` are `pub host async fn` rows whose bodies park `Completer`s answered from reqwest worker threads (or the fixture lane's virtual clock). Mount it with `rut/http_host` + `rut/http`; the full walk-through is [the GitHub viewer example](../examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md)."
msgstr ""
"标准 HTTP 链路就是一个 `register_async!` 客户端：`http_send`、`http_body`、`http_stream_next` 都是 `pub host async fn` 行，它们的体停放一些 `Completer`，由 reqwest 的 worker 线程（或夹具链路的虚拟时钟）应答。用 `rut/http_host` + `rut/http` 挂载它；完整演练见 [GitHub 查看器示例](../examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md)。"


#: src/reference/host-futures.md:144
msgid ""
"Plain `host fn` rows (synchronous, run to completion inside the crossing) are the other half of the boundary — see [embedding and native modules](embedding.md)."
msgstr "普通的 `host fn` 行（同步的，在跨越内部一次运行到底）是边界的另一半——见[嵌入与原生模块](embedding.md)。"


#: src/reference/workers-and-channels.md:3
msgid ""
"Workers are **separate VMs on separate threads** with separate heaps. There is no shared memory: everything that crosses is a value on a typed channel, moved or deep-copied under the rules below. Pure rut code inside one VM is always single-threaded, which is what keeps the RC heap lock-free ([the Rc heap](rc-heap.md))."
msgstr ""
"worker 是**独立线程上的独立 VM**，拥有独立的堆。没有共享内存：一切跨越的东西都是类型化通道上的一个值，按下述规则转移或深复制。单个 VM 内的纯 rut 代码永远是单线程的，这正是 RC 堆免锁的原因（[Rc 堆](rc-heap.md)）。"


