#: src/reference/loading.md:82
msgid ""
"`pending_tasks()` is the idle test — zero means the program has nothing runnable. There is no job executor inside the VM: parking, waking, and timing are these three verbs plus `set_now` ([Async and await](async.md)). A program that mounts no async packages simply has no launcher; `await` stays cold-poll inline ([The async model](../core-concepts/async-model.md))."
msgstr ""
"`pending_tasks()` 是空闲判据——零意味着程序没有任何可运行的东西。VM 内部没有作业执行器：停放、唤醒与计时就是这三个动词加 `set_now`（[异步与 await](async.md)）。不挂载任何异步包的程序就是没有启动器；`await` 保持内联的冷轮询（[异步模型](../core-concepts/async-model.md)）。"


#: src/reference/loading.md:89
msgid "The soft-fail law (the err channel)"
msgstr "软失败法则（err 通道）"


#: src/reference/loading.md:91
msgid ""
"An `entry fn -> (?T, err)` never produces `Err`. The pair decodes at `vm.call` as `Ok` — **with data in the pair**: a non-empty `err` string means the turn failed softly; an empty `err` means success (nil value = \"not found\"). `Err` remains exclusively the trapped turn: a bug, wiring drift, exhausted fuel — the loud channel."
msgstr ""
"`entry fn -> (?T, err)` 绝不产出 `Err`。这个对偶在 `vm.call` 处解码为 `Ok`——**数据就在对偶里**：非空的 `err` 字符串意味着这一轮软失败；空的 `err` 意味着成功（nil 值 = \"未找到\"）。`Err` 仍然专属于被陷阱打断的轮次：一个 bug、接线漂移、燃料耗尽——响亮的通道。"


#: src/reference/loading.md:97
msgid ""
"The law for host event loops (**the pump pattern**): per queued event, call the turn entry, then —"
msgstr "宿主事件循环的法则（**泵送模式**）：对每个排队的事件，调用轮次入口，然后——"


#: src/reference/loading.md:100
msgid ""
"**`Ok`**: decode the pair. A non-empty err is _reported_ (surfaced to the user/log, retained) and the loop **keeps draining**: the container survives, the queue proceeds, the page stays alive. A returned err must never poison the container or kill the drain — it is data the host acts on."
msgstr ""
"**`Ok`**：解码对偶。非空的 err 被_上报_（呈现给用户/日志，予以保留），循环**继续排空**：容器幸存，队列继续，页面保持存活。返回的 err 绝不能毒化容器或杀死排空——它是宿主据以行动的数据。"


#: src/reference/loading.md:105
msgid ""
"**`Err`**: the pump aborts **loud** — a trapped turn is a bug, not data. The `Vm` itself survives for the next good turn."
msgstr "**`Err`**：泵送**响亮**地中止——被陷阱打断的轮次是 bug，不是数据。`Vm` 本身幸存下来，迎接下一个正常的轮次。"


#: src/reference/loading.md:108
msgid ""
"On a raw JSON boundary (the wasm host), the envelope carries `\"err\"` beside `\"trap\"`: a soft-fail run reads `{\"trap\": null, \"err\": \"…\"}`, a success reads `\"err\": null`, and a panic sets `trap` with `\"err\": null`. `trap` never fills `err`. Fuel and heap reporting are unchanged by this."
msgstr ""
"在原始 JSON 边界上（wasm 宿主），信封在 `\"trap\"` 旁边携带 `\"err\"`：软失败的运行读到 `{\"trap\": null, \"err\": \"…\"}`，成功读到 `\"err\": null`，panic 则设置 `trap` 且 `\"err\": null`。`trap` 绝不填入 `err`。燃料与堆报告不因此改变。"


#: src/reference/loading.md:113
msgid "Parse-time robustness"
msgstr "解析期的健壮性"


#: src/reference/loading.md:115
msgid ""
"The same embeddability pillar holds at the other end of the pipeline: the [frontend](frontend.md) is stack-bounded with explicit nesting budgets — malformed or hostile module source yields diagnostics, never a host stack overflow, and a module with diagnostics never reaches the VM."
msgstr ""
"同一根可嵌入性支柱在流水线的另一端同样成立：[前端](frontend.md)以显式的嵌套预算限定栈深——畸形或敌意的模块源码产出诊断，绝不会溢出宿主栈，而带诊断的模块绝不会抵达 VM。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:3
msgid ""
"Errors are values and bugs are traps — either way, the first question is _where_. The story has two halves: compile-time diagnostics (one model from the first illegal byte to the last type error) and runtime traces (raw captures, lazy symbolication)."
msgstr ""
"错误是值，bug 是陷阱——无论哪种，第一个问题都是_在哪里_。这个故事有两半：编译期诊断（从第一个非法字节到最后一个类型错误的同一个模型）与运行时追踪（原始捕获，惰性符号化）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:8
msgid "Compile-time diagnostics"
msgstr "编译期诊断"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:10
msgid ""
"One model serves every frontend and checking stage ([The frontend](frontend.md)):"
msgstr "一个模型服务所有前端与检查阶段（[前端](frontend.md)）："


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:18
msgid ""
"Byte-offset spans; one renderer (`render_diags`) produces the caret form — a primary line, secondary labels, notes — sorted by span so output is stable across files and phases. The parser recovers at statement boundaries and keeps going, so a file yields many diagnostics, not one. Compilation stops before IR if any diagnostic exists; there is no warnings-only lane."
msgstr ""
"字节偏移 span；一个渲染器（`render_diags`）产出插入符形态——主行、次级标签、附注——按 span 排序，因此输出跨文件、跨阶段保持稳定。语法分析器在语句边界恢复并继续前进，因此一个文件产出许多条诊断，而不是一条。只要存在任何诊断，编译就在 IR 之前停止；没有只警告的通道。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:25
msgid ""
"A compile trap worth knowing: name-level misses that involve [Dependency kinds](dependency-kinds.md) peers have dedicated diagnostics (a missing optional peer's integration is never a bare _unresolved name_)."
msgstr ""
"一个值得知道的编译陷阱：涉及[依赖种类](dependency-kinds.md) peer 的名字级未命中有专门的诊断（缺失的可选 peer 的集成绝不是一条光秃秃的 _unresolved name_）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:30
msgid "Runtime traces"
msgstr "运行时追踪"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:32
msgid "Capture — raw pcs, nothing else"
msgstr "捕获——只有原始 pc，别无其他"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:34
msgid ""
"`capture_stacktrace() -> StackTrace` (a builtin: the engine itself implements it, compiler-lowered) walks the frame stack and stores raw frames:"
msgstr "`capture_stacktrace() -> StackTrace`（一个内建：引擎自己实现它，编译器下降）遍历帧栈并存储原始帧："


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:38
msgid ""
"the active frame innermost, then every saved frame outward, as `(func, call-site pc)` pairs — about 8 bytes per frame;"
msgstr "最内是活跃帧，然后向外是每个保存的帧，形如 `(func, call-site pc)` 对——每帧约 8 字节；"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:40
msgid ""
"**no name lookup, no source access, no symbolication at capture** — capture is cheap enough for any error path;"
msgstr "**捕获时不查名字、不访问源码、不做符号化**——捕获足够便宜，任何错误路径都负担得起；"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:42
msgid ""
"saved-frame pcs are resume points, so symbolication backs one op to the call site;"
msgstr "保存帧的 pc 是恢复点，因此符号化会向回退一个操作到调用点；"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:44
msgid "target-independent by construction — the same walk runs on wasm."
msgstr "从构造上与目标无关——同一遍历在 wasm 上同样运行。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:46
msgid ""
"The result lives in a dedicated immutable trace cell: a snapshot, shared by handle, safe to store in error tuples. It takes no user impls and **never crosses the host boundary** — a trace is a rut-side diagnostic object ([The host boundary](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md))."
msgstr ""
"结果住在一个专用的不可变追踪单元里：一个快照，按句柄共享，可以安全地存进错误元组。它不需要任何用户 impl，而且**绝不跨越宿主边界**——追踪是 rut 侧的诊断对象（[宿主边界](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md)）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:51
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"builtin class StackTrace {\n"
"    fn len(self) -> i32;          // frame count (innermost first)\n"
"    fn name(self, i: i32) -> str; // frame i's function name\n"
"    fn line(self, i: i32) -> i32; // call-site line (0 when stripped)\n"
"    fn col(self, i: i32) -> i32;  // call-site column (0 when stripped)\n"
"    fn render(self) -> str;       // the symbolication string\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"builtin class StackTrace {\n"
"    fn len(self) -> i32;          // frame count (innermost first)\n"
"    fn name(self, i: i32) -> str; // frame i's function name\n"
"    fn line(self, i: i32) -> i32; // call-site line (0 when stripped)\n"
"    fn col(self, i: i32) -> i32;  // call-site column (0 when stripped)\n"
"    fn render(self) -> str;       // the symbolication string\n"
"}\n"
"```"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:61
msgid "Out-of-range `i` traps `IndexOutOfBounds` — the index is a bug, not data."
msgstr "越界的 `i` 触发 `IndexOutOfBounds` 陷阱——索引是 bug，不是数据。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:63
msgid "The tiers"
msgstr "分层"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:65
msgid "tier"
msgstr "层"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:65
msgid "when it exists"
msgstr "何时存在"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:67
msgid "`StackTrace` capture"
msgstr "`StackTrace` 捕获"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:67
msgid "explicit; a depth-proportional frame walk (~30 ns base + ~0.2 ns/frame)"
msgstr "显式；与深度成比例的帧遍历（约 30 ns 底价 + 每帧约 0.2 ns）"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:67
msgid ""
"opt-in at raise sites — a rich err carries `trace: ?StackTrace` only where the producer decides the cost is worth it"
msgstr "在抛出点选择加入——只有当生产者判定代价值得时，富 err 才携带 `trace: ?StackTrace`"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:68
msgid "`Trap`"
msgstr "`Trap`"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:68
msgid "automatic at trap unwind"
msgstr "陷阱展开时自动"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:68
msgid "bugs, overflow, `panic` — the loud channel carries `kind` + message"
msgstr "bug、溢出、`panic`——响亮通道携带 `kind` + 消息"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:69
msgid "`?` / err propagation"
msgstr "`?` / err 传播"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:69
msgid "zero cost — no auto-capture on propagation"
msgstr "零开销——传播时不自动捕获"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:69
msgid "always"
msgstr "始终"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:71
msgid ""
"Opt-in is the design: the cheap error path stays cheap, and capture is pay-per-capture."
msgstr "选择加入就是设计：便宜的错误路径保持便宜，捕获按次付费。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:74
msgid "Symbolication — lazy, per index"
msgstr "符号化——惰性，按索引"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:76
msgid "Members symbolicate **on access**, against the loaded program:"
msgstr "成员**在访问时**对照已加载的程序符号化："


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:78
msgid "`name(i)` — one interner lookup for frame _i_'s function name."
msgstr "`name(i)`——一次驻留器查找，取帧 _i_ 的函数名。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:79
msgid ""
"`line(i)` / `col(i)` — one direct read of the function's position table (pc → `(line, col)`, parallel to the pc → byte-offset span table; [Module binary and verification](module-binary.md))."
msgstr ""
"`line(i)` / `col(i)`——对函数位置表的一次直接读取（pc → `(line, col)`，与 pc → 字节偏移的 span 表平行；[模块二进制与校验](module-binary.md)）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:82
msgid "`render()` — the only whole-trace pass, innermost first:"
msgstr "`render()`——唯一的一次整条追踪的遍历，最内帧在前："


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:89
msgid ""
"There is no eager symbolication and no frames array — a frame array would mint rut-side data per access and fix the representation into the surface."
msgstr "没有急切的符号化，也没有帧数组——帧数组会在每次访问时铸造 rut 侧数据，并把表示钉死在表面里。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:93
msgid "Restoration paths"
msgstr "还原路径"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:95
msgid ""
"A trace is captured against whatever is loaded — possibly a stripped, published artifact. Four ways back to names:"
msgstr "追踪是针对当时加载的东西捕获的——可能是一个已剥离、已发布的产物。回到名字有四条路："


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:98
msgid ""
"**In-VM (the default).** The loaded program carries its interner and position tables; every member call symbolicates from them."
msgstr "**VM 内（默认）。**已加载的程序携带自己的驻留器与位置表；每次成员调用都从它们符号化。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:100
msgid ""
"**Recompile by determinism.** Serialization is deterministic — same source + same compiler version ⇒ byte-identical binary ⇒ identical pcs — so tooling can symbolicate a captured trace against a locally rebuilt binary ([The compiler pipeline](compiler.md))."
msgstr ""
"**靠确定性重编译。**序列化是确定性的——相同源码 + 相同编译器版本 ⇒ 逐字节相同的二进制 ⇒ 相同的 pc——因此工具可以对照本地重建的二进制为捕获的追踪符号化（[编译器流水线](compiler.md)）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:104
msgid ""
"**Stripped, no artifact.** Traces still _work_: they degrade to the pc-only render form above, and stay restorable via path 2 later."
msgstr "**已剥离、无产物。**追踪仍然_可用_：它们退化为上文仅 pc 的渲染形态，并且日后仍可经路径 2 还原。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:106
msgid ""
"**The stripped artifact's private symbol table.** Name resolution and position lookup follow the loaded program — so supplying a `.rutsym` sidecar at load time (`run --symbols`, or `apply_symbols_to_session` as a library call) restores real names and line/col before any trace is taken. The sidecar's law — what mangles, what stays, the mixed-closure refusal — is [Symbol stripping and `.rutsym` sidecars](symbol-stripping.md)."
msgstr ""
"**已剥离产物的私有符号表。**名字解析与位置查找都跟随加载的程序——所以在加载时提供一份 `.rutsym` 旁车（`run --symbols`，或以库调用 `apply_symbols_to_session`）就能在任何追踪被捕获之前还原真实名字与行/列。旁车的法则——什么改名、什么保留、混合闭包的拒绝——见[符号剥离与 `.rutsym` 旁车](symbol-stripping.md)。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:114
msgid "Trap messages"
msgstr "陷阱消息"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:116
msgid ""
"A trap renders as its kind plus message, e.g. `IndexOutOfBounds: index 9, len 3`, `OutOfFuel: fuel exhausted — the frame is parked; add fuel and resume()`. Traps do not carry captures — the trace surface is the opt-in rut-side snapshot — but the host that receives `Err(Trap)` gets the kind, the message, and (via `vm.fuel_used`, `heap_usage()`) the budget context ([VM core](vm-core.md))."
msgstr ""
"陷阱渲染为种类加消息，例如 `IndexOutOfBounds: index 9, len 3`、`OutOfFuel: fuel exhausted — the frame is parked; add fuel and resume()`。陷阱不携带捕获——追踪表面是那个选择加入的 rut 侧快照——但收到 `Err(Trap)` 的宿主会拿到种类、消息，以及（经由 `vm.fuel_used`、`heap_usage()`）预算上下文（[VM 核心](vm-core.md)）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:123
msgid "Where the surfaces live"
msgstr "表面住在哪里"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:125
msgid ""
"`panic(msg)` — the core builtin that raises; the `Disposal` trait is the cleanup surface ([The Rc heap and destructors](rc-heap.md))."
msgstr "`panic(msg)`——负责抛出的 core 内建；`Disposal` trait 是清理表面（[Rc 堆与析构器](rc-heap.md)）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:128
msgid ""
"`capture_stacktrace()` and the `StackTrace` class — ambient builtin names, no `use` required ([core and the swappable packages](stdlib.md))."
msgstr ""
"`capture_stacktrace()` 与 `StackTrace` 类——环境自带的内建名字，无需 `use`（[core 与可换包](stdlib.md)）。"


#: src/reference/diagnostics.md:131
msgid ""
"The web runner surfaces the same data in its envelope: `\"trap\"` beside `\"err\"` ([Loading and the embed loop](loading.md))."
msgstr "web 运行器在它的信封里呈现同样的数据：`\"trap\"` 在 `\"err\"` 旁边（[加载与嵌入循环](loading.md)）。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:3
msgid ""
"`rut pack mod/` reads a module directory and emits **one file** — `mod.rutbundle` — a zip archive carrying the module in one of two root kinds, paired with the format version: a **lib** pkg packs **compiled** (v9 — the root's `.rutc` binary, its scope ledger, and each dependency as a compiled `.rutc` group or a source file set), and a `type = \"host\"` pkg packs as a **decl** root (v10 — its `.d.rut` surface rides as source; single-package). A bundle is the same contract as the directory it was packed from, in one file: the loader mounts it exactly like the directory, and the two compile to identical programs."
msgstr ""
"`rut pack mod/` 读入模块目录并产出**一个文件**——`mod.rutbundle`——一个 zip 档案，以两种根之一携带模块，与格式版本配对：**lib** 包**编译**打包（v5——根的 `.rutc` 二进制、其作用域台账、每个依赖作为编译的 `.rutc` 组或源文件集），`type = \"host\"` 包打包为**声明**根（v6——其 `.d.rut` 面以源码承载；单包）。捆绑包与打包前的目录是同一契约，收进一个文件：加载器像挂载目录一样挂载它，两者编译出相同的程序。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:14
msgid "Layout rules"
msgstr "布局规则"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:16
msgid ""
"**Entry names are paths relative to the module root** — `rut.jsonc`, `<pkg>.rutc`, `<pkg>.d.rut`, `<dep>/…` group entries for deps. No directories otherwise, no metadata entries. Unknown extra entries are ignored by loaders (forward compatibility) — except in a v10 decl bundle, where a group entry, a root `.rutc`, or a ledger is a contradiction and refuses (see [the v10 layout](#the-v10-layout))."
msgstr ""
"**入口名是相对模块根的路径**——`rut.jsonc`、`<pkg>.rutc`、`<pkg>.d.rut`、依赖的 `<dep>/…` 组条目。除此之外没有目录，也没有元数据条目。加载器忽略未知的额外条目（向前兼容）——但 v10 声明捆绑包例外：组条目、根 `.rutc` 或台账都是矛盾，会拒绝（见 [v10 布局](#the-v10-layout)）。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:22
msgid ""
"The manifest's `name` is the package name the bundle answers to — a bare `[a-zA-Z0-9_]+` name, the same law as directory manifests."
msgstr "清单的 `name` 是捆绑包所对应的包名——一个裸的 `[a-zA-Z0-9_]+` 名字，与目录清单同一法则。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:24
msgid "Includes and splices never escape the archive: there is no outside."
msgstr "包含与拼接绝不逃出归档：没有外部。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:26
msgid "The v9 layout — a compiled root"
msgstr "v9 布局——编译根"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:28
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"rut.jsonc                byte-for-byte; \"format\": \"rutbundle\", \"format_version\": 9\n"
"rut.scopes               the pack-time scope ledger (scope = \"spec\" rows)\n"
"<pkg>.rutc               the root's compiled binary — bodies + surface\n"
"<pkg>.rut                the root's generic-bearing source, when its surface\n"
"                           exports generics (the riding law, below)\n"
"<pkg>.d.rut              the root's surface text (humans, LSP), when it declares one\n"
"<dep>/rut.jsonc          per dep group, mixed kinds:\n"
"<dep>/<dep>.rutc           linkable dep → a compiled group (its rut.jsonc rides too);\n"
"                           generic exports ride compiled — the binary carries\n"
"                           the closure's instantiations in its ledger\n"
"<dep>/<dep>.rut            the group's generic-bearing source, when its surface\n"
"<dep>/group-*.rut …        exports generics (the entry + the peer-deps group\n"
"                           files, verbatim — the riding law, below)\n"
"<dep>/<dep>.d.rut          its surface text, when it declares one\n"
"<leaf>/rut.jsonc           splice-needed dep (the `inline` flag) or a host\n"
"<leaf>/<leaf>.rut           pkg → a source group: the source file set\n"
"<leaf>/<leaf>.rut …         (entry, libs, peer groups)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:48
msgid ""
"The **`.rutc` binaries are the linking truth**: bodies plus the surface on the wire ([module binary and verification](module-binary.md)). A consumer binds a compiled group's exports from the binary alone — nothing is rebuilt from `.d.rut` text. The `.d.rut` files ride for humans and tooling; the loader never reads them."
msgstr ""
"**`.rutc` 二进制是链接的真相**：函数体加线上的表面（[模块二进制与验证](module-binary.md)）。使用方仅凭二进制就绑定编译组的导出——没有任何东西从 `.d.rut` 文本重建。`.d.rut` 文件为人类与工具随行；加载器从不读它们。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:54
msgid ""
"The **scope ledger** names the pack-time scope of every linked module in the closure (engine mounts included). A decoded program's ids spell its pack-time scopes; the loader resolves each through the ledger to the module to ensure and rebases the ids onto its own numbering — pack-time and load-time numbering never have to agree. A reference with no ledger row is refused."
msgstr ""
"**作用域台账**记下闭包里每个被链接模块的打包期作用域（连引擎挂载也在内）。解码程序的 id 写明它的打包期作用域；加载器经台账把每个作用域解析到要确保的模块，并把 id 重定基到自己的编号上——打包期与加载期的编号从不需要一致。台账里没有对应行的引用会被拒绝。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:60
msgid ""
"**Mixed groups, one classifier**: the same splice law that rules the graph (the `inline` flag — [modules and visibility](modules-and-visibility.md)) decides each package's kind. Refuse, never guess: the packer calls the graph's own classifier, there is no second implementation."
msgstr ""
"**混合的组，一个分类器**：统治模块图的同一条拼接法则（`inline` 旗标——[模块与可见性](modules-and-visibility.md)）裁定每个包的种类。拒绝，绝不猜测：打包器调用的就是图自己的分类器，没有第二份实现。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:65
msgid ""
"**Generics ride compiled — and their source rides beside them** (the generic-source riding law): instantiation is owned by the declaring package, and the pack walk seeds each generic dep with the instantiations its consumers spell — the binary's instantiation ledger names every `(owner, decl, arguments)` row. A compiled pkg whose surface exports an OPEN generic surface (generic fns, generic type exports, generic methods, generic-target impls) ALSO rides the source that serves consumer-spelled shapes: the entry lib, each `entry.libs` file, and each `peer-deps` group file, verbatim, beside the binary. The entry lib's presence is the loader's dispatch marker; non-generic pkgs (`http`, `ink`, `strbuild`) stay source-free. At the consumer's link, a request the ledger lacks lowers the ridden text in the consumer's session and compiles the monomorphized body with owner = the pkg's spec — one row program-wide, indistinguishable from a pack-time one, nothing persisted. A bundle with no riding source refuses such a request loudly (`this bundle predates generic-source riding — re-pack it`), never mislinks. `--strip` refuses the combination: the ridden text would recompile clean-named beside mangled binaries."
msgstr ""
"**泛型以编译形式跨越 —— 且其源码在旁承载**（泛型源码承载法则）：实例化由声明包持有，打包遍历以其消费者拼写的实例化种子化每个泛型依赖 —— 二进制的实例化台账命名每一行 `(owner, decl, arguments)`。表面导出开放泛型表面（泛型 fn、泛型类型导出、泛型方法、泛型目标 impl）的编译 pkg 还会在二进制旁承载服务消费者拼写形状的源码：入口 lib、每个 `entry.libs` 文件、每个 `peer-deps` 组文件，逐字，就在二进制旁。入口 lib 的存在是加载器的分发标记；非泛型 pkg（`http`、`ink`、`strbuild`）保持无源码。在消费者的链接处，台账缺失的请求会在消费者的会话中降低被承载的文本，并以 owner = 该 pkg 的 spec 编译单态化代码体 —— 全程序一行，与打包期产生的无从分辨，不持久化任何东西。没有承载源码的包会大声拒绝这类请求（`this bundle predates generic-source riding — re-pack it`），绝不错误链接。`--strip` 拒绝该组合：被承载的文本会在被改名的二进制旁以干净名字重新编译。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:84
msgid ""
"**The root must be linkable** — else `pack: <pkg> is inline — its source is its interface and it cannot be published compiled; share the directory instead`. A root that has nothing to compile is not this refusal: a `type = \"host\"` pkg packs as a v10 decl root, below."
msgstr ""
"**根必须可链接**——否则 `pack: <pkg> is inline — its source is its interface and it cannot be published compiled; share the directory instead`。没有东西可编译的根不是这条拒绝：`type = \"host\"` 包按 v10 声明根打包，见下。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:89
msgid "The v10 layout — a host root"
msgstr "v10 布局——宿主根"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:91
msgid ""
"A `type = \"host\"` pkg's root IS its declaration surface, so a host bundle is the manifest plus that surface, riding as source — single-package, no ledger, no groups, nothing to decode:"
msgstr "`type = \"host\"` 包的根**就是**它的声明面，所以宿主捆绑包 = 清单 + 该面，以源码承载——单包，无台账，无组，无可解码之物："


#: src/reference/bundles.md:95
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"rut.jsonc                byte-for-byte; \"format\": \"rutbundle\", \"format_version\": 10\n"
"<pkg>.d.rut              the declaration surface — the root itself\n"
"```"
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:100
msgid "The pairing is **total**, both directions refused at the version gate:"
msgstr "配对是**完全的**，两个方向都在版本门处拒绝："


#: src/reference/bundles.md:102
msgid ""
"**v9 ⇔ compiled.** A host manifest at v9 refuses — a v9 bundle's root must be a `.rutc` a host pkg cannot have."
msgstr "**v9 ⇔ 编译。** 宿主清单在 v9 拒绝——v9 捆绑包的根必须是 `.rutc`，宿主包给不出。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:104
msgid ""
"**v10 ⇔ decl.** A lib manifest at v10 refuses — lib roots stay v9, compiled."
msgstr "**v10 ⇔ 声明。** lib 清单在 v10 拒绝——lib 根留在 v5，编译。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:106
msgid ""
"A v10 bundle carrying a root `.rutc` (`a host bundle's root is its surface, not a compiled unit`), a `rut.scopes` ledger, or any group entry (`a host bundle is single-package`) refuses: contradictions, never guesses."
msgstr ""
"携带根 `.rutc`（`a host bundle's root is its surface, not a compiled unit`）、`rut.scopes` 台账或任何组条目的 v10 捆绑包拒绝：只认矛盾，从不猜。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:110
msgid ""
"Writers emit 10 **only** for decl roots — every lib bundle stays byte-identical v9, and old readers refuse a v10 bundle loudly at the version gate."
msgstr "写入方**只**为声明根发出 10——每个 lib 捆绑包保持字节等同的 v9，旧读取器在版本门大声拒绝 v10 捆绑包。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:114
msgid ""
"`rut pack <host-dir>` works (the surface verifies by parsing and lowering once — the exact lane a mount runs — then rides as source), `--strip` refuses on a host root (`no symbols to strip` — no programs, no sidecar), and `rut run <host.rutbundle>` refuses with intent: a host bundle carries a declaration surface — nothing to run; bind its rows from the embedder ([host fns](host-fns.md)). The mount is the same lane a host group rides inside a v9 bundle: the surface lowers into the pkg's host rows."
msgstr ""
"`rut pack <host-dir>` 可用（该面以解析并 lowering 一次来验证——与挂载同一条车道——然后以源码承载），宿主根上 `--strip` 拒绝（`no symbols to strip`——没有程序，没有旁车），`rut run <host.rutbundle>` 带着意图拒绝：宿主捆绑包携带的是声明面——无物可运行；从嵌入方绑定它的行（[宿主函数](host-fns.md)）。挂载与 v9 捆绑包内宿主组承载的车道相同：面 lowering 成该包的宿主行。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:123
msgid "The manifest — `rut.jsonc`"
msgstr "清单——`rut.jsonc`"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:125
msgid ""
"First entry in the zip; JSONC (the directory grammar: `//` and `/* */` comments and trailing commas are legal); the same manifest grammar the directory form uses, byte-for-byte the directory's manifest — which is what makes a bundle-shaped directory pack unchanged:"
msgstr ""
"zip 中的第一个条目；JSONC（目录文法：`//` 与 `/* */` 注释以及尾随逗号都合法）；与目录形态使用同一份清单文法，逐字节就是目录的清单——这正是让捆绑包形态的目录原样打包的原因："


#: src/reference/bundles.md:130
msgid ""
"```jsonc\n"
"{\n"
"  // the bundle LAYOUT version — independent of the module-binary\n"
"  // version; a host root declares 10 instead (see the v10 layout)\n"
"  \"format\": \"rutbundle\",\n"
"  \"format_version\": 9,\n"
"  // the package this bundle answers to\n"
"  \"name\": \"plugin\",\n"
"  // directory-time; the compiled form rides plugin.rutc instead\n"
"  \"entry\": { \"lib\": \"./plugin.rut\" },\n"
"\n"
"  // the whole dep closure rides the archive\n"
"  \"deps\": {\n"
"    \"server\": { \"path\": \"../server\" }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:148
msgid ""
"Directory loading **ignores** `format`/`format_version` — a directory is not a bundle — which is why the keys are safe to write into every module manifest today: `examples/03-plugin/plugin` is a working directory that also packs unchanged."
msgstr ""
"目录加载**忽略** `format`/`format_version`——目录不是捆绑包——这正是今天把这些键安全写进每个模块清单的原因：`examples/03-plugin/plugin` 是一个工作目录，同时也能原封不动地打包。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:153
msgid ""
"The rest of the manifest grammar — deps tables, `inline`, `style` — is defined in [Project structure and rut.jsonc](project-structure.md); the dependency semantics are [Dependency kinds](dependency-kinds.md)."
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:158
msgid "Url deps — bundles by reference"
msgstr "url 依赖 — 按引用的捆绑包"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:160
msgid "A consumer may pin a bundle by url instead of vendoring it:"
msgstr "消费者可以用 url 固定一个捆绑包，而不是将其内嵌（vendor）："


#: src/reference/bundles.md:162
msgid ""
"```jsonc\n"
"{\n"
"  \"deps\": {\n"
"    \"server\": { \"url\": \"https://example.com/server.rutbundle\", \"sha256\": \"<64-hex>\" }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:170
msgid ""
"The mount is the bundle mount, one gate earlier: the embedder's remote produces the bytes (`DepRemote` — the standard `HttpRemote` is cache-first), then the loader runs the same container/layout/name checks and — before all of them — the **pin law**: the bytes must hash to the manifest row's `sha256`, on every load, or the load refuses naming the dep, the url, and both hashes. The url dep mounts as a **leaf**: its bundle brings the whole closure (every declared dep satisfied by an in-archive group — the closure law is unchanged, and a url row inside a packed bundle is inert metadata; loading a bundle never fetches)."
msgstr ""
"挂载就是捆绑包挂载，只是提前了一道门：嵌入方的远程产出字节（`DepRemote` — 标准的 `HttpRemote` 是缓存优先的），然后加载器执行同样的容器/布局/名称检查，而且 — 先于所有检查 — 执行**固定值法则**：字节必须散列到清单行的 `sha256`，在每次加载时皆然，否则加载被拒绝，并指名依赖、url 与两个哈希。url 依赖作为**叶子**挂载：它的捆绑包带来整个闭包（每条声明的依赖都由档案内的组满足——闭包法则不变，打包好的捆绑包内的 url 行是惰性元数据；加载捆绑包从不拉取）。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:180
msgid ""
"Because the manifest rides byte-for-byte, url rows carry into a consumer's own `rut pack` output, satisfied by the rode-along groups: the archive's groups re-encode from the consumer session's units (one `.rutc` path), source groups copy their file set under the new prefix, and the same manifest + pins still pack byte-identically. v1 refuses, loudly and named, the cases that would emit a bundle the loader must reject: an archive source group still declaring `dev-deps` directories (vendor the dep), a compiled group the consumer's closure never uses (it cannot ride unpackaged), and a declared dep that did not ride."
msgstr ""
"由于清单逐字节随行，url 行会带进消费者自己的 `rut pack` 输出，由随行组满足：存档的组从消费者会话的 units 重新编码（唯一的 `.rutc` 路径），源码组把它的文件集复制到新前缀下，而相同清单 + 相同固定值仍逐字节相同地打包。v1 会响亮地、指名道姓地拒绝那些会产出加载器必须拒绝的捆绑包的情形：仍在声明 `dev-deps` 目录的存档源码组（vendor 这个依赖）、消费者闭包从不使用的编译组（它无法未打包地随行），以及没有随行的声明依赖。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:191
msgid "The layout ledger"
msgstr "布局台账"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:193
msgid ""
"`format_version` versions the zip layout and manifest keys themselves. Loaders refuse a version they do not know **before reading anything else** — refuse, never guess; the same gate makes an older loader refuse a newer bundle."
msgstr ""
"`format_version` 给 zip 布局与清单键本身定版本。加载器在**读取任何其他内容之前**就拒绝自己不认识的版本——拒绝，绝不猜测；同一道门也让旧加载器拒绝新捆绑包。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:198
msgid "version"
msgstr "版本"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:198
msgid "layout"
msgstr "布局"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:198
msgid "status today"
msgstr "今天的现状"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:200
msgid "one module, sources only"
msgstr "单模块，仅源码"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:200 src/reference/bundles.md:201
#: src/reference/bundles.md:202 src/reference/bundles.md:203
msgid "refused — re-pack the directory"
msgstr "拒绝——请重新打包该目录"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:201
msgid "+ the whole `deps` graph as `<pkg>/` groups"
msgstr "+ 整张 `deps` 图，作为 `<pkg>/` 组"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:202
msgid "+ each package's `peer-deps` `lib` group files"
msgstr "+ 每个包的 `peer-deps` `lib` 组文件"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:203
msgid "+ each package's `entry.libs` files"
msgstr "+ 每个包的 `entry.libs` 文件"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:204
msgid "compiled: `.rutc` (v17) + `.d.rut` per linkable pkg — the manifest TOML"
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:204 src/reference/bundles.md:205
msgid "refused — re-pack the directory (the pre-JSON shape)"
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:205
msgid "decl: a `type = \"host\"` root — the manifest TOML"
msgstr ""


#: src/reference/bundles.md:206
msgid ""
"compiled, the manifest JSON (`rut.json`): `.rutc` (v17) + `.d.rut` per linkable pkg — generic exports included, their instantiations seeded into the binaries, and a generic-owning pkg's source riding beside its binary — mixed source groups for `inline` deps and host pkgs"
msgstr ""
"编译，JSON 清单（`rut.json`）：每个可链接 pkg 一份 `.rutc`（v17）+ `.d.rut`——泛型导出在内，其实例化被播种进二进制，拥有泛型的 pkg 的源码在其二进制旁承载——`inline` 依赖与宿主 pkg 的混合源码组"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:206 src/reference/bundles.md:207
msgid "refused — re-pack the directory (the pre-JSONC wire)"
msgstr "拒绝——请重新打包该目录（JSONC 之前的线格式）"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:207
msgid ""
"decl, the manifest JSON (`rut.json`): a `type = \"host\"` root — the manifest + its `.d.rut` surface, single-package"
msgstr "声明，JSON 清单（`rut.json`）：一个 `type = \"host\"` 根——清单 + 它的 `.d.rut` 表面，单包"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:208
msgid ""
"compiled, the manifest JSONC (`rut.jsonc`): the v7 layout under the JSONC cutover — the manifest file renamed, comments + trailing commas legal"
msgstr "编译，JSONC 清单（`rut.jsonc`）：JSONC 切换下的 v7 布局——清单文件更名，注释 + 尾随逗号合法"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:208
msgid "**the lib root's layout**"
msgstr "**lib 根的布局**"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:209
msgid ""
"decl, the manifest JSONC (`rut.jsonc`): a `type = \"host\"` root — the manifest + its `.d.rut` surface, single-package"
msgstr "声明，JSONC 清单（`rut.jsonc`）：一个 `type = \"host\"` 根——清单 + 它的 `.d.rut` 表面，单包"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:209
msgid "**the host root's layout**"
msgstr "**宿主根的布局**"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:211
msgid ""
"The 8→9 bump rides the manifest's own RENAME (`rut.json` → `rut.jsonc`): the entry name is layout, so the number moves with it — an old reader must never silently misparse a file whose name it does not know. Each historical extension existed because the added files were _part of the package_: a bundle that dropped peer groups or multi-lib files would load base-only — semantically wrong. v7 replaced the source contract with the compiled one — one exception, the riding law above: a generic-owning compiled pkg's source rides beside its binary so consumer-spelled shapes stay servable. Source sharing as the general contract stays a directory (`rut run <dir>`), as it always was outside bundles."
msgstr ""
"8→9 的跳变搭载在清单自身的更名上（`rut.json` → `rut.jsonc`）：条目名就是布局，所以数字随它移动——旧读取器绝不能静默误解析一个它不认识其名字的文件。每一代历史扩展都因新增文件是*包的一部分*而存在：一个丢掉 peer 组或多 lib 文件的包会只装载基座 —— 语义错误。v7 用编译契约替换了源码契约 —— 一条例外，即上面的承载法则：拥有泛型的编译 pkg 的源码在其二进制旁承载，使消费者拼写的形状保持可服务。作为一般契约的源码共享仍是目录（`rut run <dir>`），一如包外世界的惯例。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:224
msgid ""
"Peer-gated packages publish inside v9 two ways, per their group-kind law: a NON-generic compiled declarer's peer groups compile into its binary at pack time (the rows ride the binary; the group files do not travel), and a splice-needed declarer publishes as a source group, its group files riding beside the entry — the loader's peer gate appends by presence exactly as in a directory world ([Dependency kinds](dependency-kinds.md)). A generic-owning compiled declarer rides its group files too (the riding law), and the on-demand recompile splices exactly the rows whose peers are in the consumer's closure."
msgstr ""
"Peer 门控的包以两种方式在 v9 内发布，依其组别类法则：非泛型的编译声明者，其 peer 组在打包期编译进其二进制（行随二进制跨越；组文件不随行）；需要拼接的声明者以源码组发布，其组文件在入口旁承载 —— 加载器的 peer 门按存在性追加，与目录世界完全一致（[依赖类别](dependency-kinds.md)）。拥有泛型的编译声明者也承载其组文件（承载法则），按需重编译只拼接 peer 在消费者闭包中的那些行。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:234
msgid ""
"**The ledger namespaces per archive.** Each archive's scope rows shift into a fresh numeric range of the mounting session (boot passes through), and its binaries rebase with that same map **before** mounting — so two independently packed bundles can share one session without their pack-time numberings ever arguing. First-mount-wins still decides which body a shared group name keeps, and a group's ledger row must still be the scope its own binary carries (refuse, never guess — that check is per archive). The CDN lane below is the reason this exists: per-package bundles are packed independently, each numbering its own closure."
msgstr ""
"**台账按档案命名空间化。** 每个档案的作用域行移入挂载会话的新数值区间（启动穿过其间），其二进制在挂载**前**用同一映射重定基——于是两个独立打包的捆绑包可共享一个会话，打包期编号永不争吵。先挂载者胜仍决定共享组名保留哪个体，组的台账行仍须是其二进制自带的作用域（拒绝，从不猜——该检查按档案进行）。下方的 CDN 车道就是它存在的理由：按包捆绑包独立打包，各自给自己的闭包编号。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:245
msgid "The `bundle` module"
msgstr "`bundle` 模块"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:247
msgid ""
"The container codec, the `rut.jsonc` grammar, the source file-set collector, and the reader (both root kinds) live in the driver's `rut_driver::bundle` module — **filesystem-free**. Every read goes through a one-method `Source` trait: `rut_driver::bundle::FsSource` is the real filesystem (the CLI, native hosts); an in-memory path→bytes map serves tests and wasm hosts. The packer itself needs the compiler and lives beside it (`rut_driver::pack_dir`) — it returns the bundle bytes; writing the output file stays with the caller. Mounting a bundle into a session stays in the loader ([Loading](loading.md)), over `rut_driver::bundle::Bundle` and its parsed `rut_driver::bundle::Layout` — the compiled root and its ledger + groups, or the decl root and its surface."
msgstr ""
"容器编解码、`rut.jsonc` 文法、源文件集收集器与读取器（两种根）都住在驱动 crate 的 `rut_driver::bundle` 模块——**无文件系统**。每次读取都经过单方法 `Source` trait：`rut_driver::bundle::FsSource` 是真实文件系统（CLI、原生宿主）；内存中的路径→字节映射服务于测试与 wasm 宿主。打包器本身需要编译器，住在它旁边（`rut_driver::pack_dir`）——它返回捆绑包字节；写出输出文件留在调用方。把捆绑包挂载进会话仍在加载器里（[Loading](loading.md)），经由 `rut_driver::bundle::Bundle` 与其解析出的 `rut_driver::bundle::Layout`——编译根及其台账 + 组，或声明根及其表面。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:260
