msgid ""
"fixed entry order — `rut.jsonc` first, then the scope ledger, the root's binary, then dep groups in name order (deduplicated, recursive);"
msgstr "固定条目顺序——先是 `rut.jsonc`，再是作用域台账、根的二进制，然后依赖组按名字排序（去重、递归）；"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:267
msgid "fixed (zeroed) timestamps;"
msgstr "固定（清零）的时间戳；"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:268
msgid "STORE (no compression) — determinism over size."
msgstr "STORE（不压缩）——确定性优先于体积。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:270
msgid ""
"This is the module binary's determinism law extended one level up ([Module binary and verification](module-binary.md)): bundles are content-cacheable, and two builds of the same module diff to nothing."
msgstr ""
"这是模块二进制的确定性法则向上一层的延伸（[模块二进制与校验](module-binary.md)）：捆绑包可按内容缓存，同一模块的两次构建 diff 为零。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:274
msgid "Stripping — the private sidecar"
msgstr "剥离——私有的旁车"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:276
msgid ""
"`rut pack <dir> --strip` emits the bundle as above **plus a private symbol table** at the sibling path `<out-without-ext>.rutsym`. Every renameable name in the `.rutc` binaries mangles to `%N` and every function's span/position tables leave — the sidecar carries exactly what left, so supplying it at load restores real names and line/col for stack-trace symbolication. The sidecar is never an entry inside the archive. It needs a fully-compiled closure (a source group that could bind a compiled group's surface is a pointed refusal); without `--strip`, packing is unchanged. The whole law lives in [Symbol stripping and `.rutsym` sidecars](symbol-stripping.md). `run` accepts `--symbols <file.rutsym>` against a compiled bundle ([The rut CLI](cli.md))."
msgstr ""
"`rut pack <dir> --strip` 在上述内容之外，**外加一份私有符号表**，写在旁边的路径 `<out-without-ext>.rutsym`。`.rutc` 二进制里每个可改名的名字都改名为 `%N`，每个函数的区间/位置表都离开——旁车携带的正是离开的东西，因此在加载时提供它就能为栈追踪符号化还原真实名字与行/列。旁车绝不是归档里的一个条目。它需要一个全编译的闭包（可能绑定某编译组表面的源码组会被明确拒绝）；不加 `--strip` 时，打包一切照旧。完整的法则见[符号剥离与 `.rutsym` 旁车](symbol-stripping.md)。`run` 对编译的捆绑包接受 `--symbols <file.rutsym>`（[rut CLI](cli.md)）。"


#: src/reference/bundles.md:289
